<p><span data-ccp-props="{}">&nbsp;</span></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/apaleo/senior-product-manager-ai-products-agentic-hospitality-germany-426998","tags":[],"job_types":[],"location":"Germany","created_at":1794692722},{"slug":"solutions-engineer-munich-465984","company_name":"True Talent Solutions Partners","title":"Solutions Engineer","description":"<h3>About the Role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join a team bringing digital tools to industrial research and development. You will lead technical pre-sales engagements, helping prospective customers understand how modern data management can support their R&amp;D workflows and accelerate innovation.</p><h3>What You'll Do</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the technical pre-sales process from initial demonstrations through value cases, technical evaluations, and pilot execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build tailored demonstrations, workshops, and pilots for prospective customers' research and development workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with sales colleagues and customer stakeholders to communicate business value and support new customer acquisition.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead technical evaluations and presentations that explain how digital R&amp;D data tools support research and innovation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentor team members supporting technical evaluations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write scripts and configure platform integrations for customer engagements as needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Travel 25% to 50% for customer meetings, presentations, and workshops.</p></li></ul><h3>What We're Looking For</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Four to seven years of relevant experience, including at least four years in digitalization, change management, or R&amp;D leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An advanced degree in chemistry, chemical engineering, or materials science, ideally with a machine learning or computational focus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong chemistry or materials science knowledge and experience with industrial R&amp;D workflows and laboratory informatics systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and demonstrating technical platforms for enterprise customers, with a value-based selling approach.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in digital transformation or change management; R&amp;D leadership in the chemicals or materials sector is valuable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Python scripting skills are a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness and ability to travel 25% to 50%, and authorization to work in the US, UK, or Germany. Visa sponsorship is not available.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">For the Munich location, professional fluency in the relevant local language and fluent English are expected.</p></li></ul><h3>Compensation &amp; Benefits</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Base salary: $120,000 to $150,000 annually. Visa sponsorship is not available.</p><h3>Location</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid role based in Munich, Bavaria, Germany. London or New York may also be possible.</p><hr><p>Compensation: $120K – $150K</p><ul><li> • $120K – $150K</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/true-talent-solutions-partners/solutions-engineer-munich-465984","tags":["Client Roles"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1794692411},{"slug":"senior-legal-partner-berlin-240302","company_name":"True Talent Solutions Partners","title":"Senior Legal Partner","description":"<h3>About the Role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">A Germany-based, AI-enabled legal services firm is seeking a senior partner to help grow its practice and shape how technology supports legal work. You will bring an established client portfolio, continue advising those clients, and work with the founding team to develop a scalable model for commercial and compliance services.</p><h3>What You'll Do</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help shape the firm's growth and expand its client relationships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring a portable client portfolio to the firm's technology platform while continuing to serve existing clients.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build market credibility and develop opportunities through your professional network, including private equity and venture capital contacts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify opportunities to provide commercial and compliance services across your client base.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with the founding team to identify recurring legal matters that can be streamlined through AI and automation.</p></li></ul><h3>What We're Looking For</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">12 to 20 or more years of German legal practice, with experience at partner level.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">German-qualified Volljurist and admitted Rechtsanwalt, with native-level German and professional English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A personally held, portable book of business valued at €1 million or more, with a diversified client base and strong private equity or venture capital relationships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in recurring, automatable work such as commercial contracts, IT and data, corporate or venture capital, or regulatory matters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience using AI tools, such as OpenAI-based tools, and a willingness to adapt legal workflows through automation.</p></li><li><p style="min