&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We believe in inclusivity and are therefore dedicated to ensuring all employees – across gender identity, race, ethnicity, sexual orientation, religion, life experience, background and more – feel welcome and included in the company. We promote diversity because we believe it is essential to our ability to think holistically.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/engelhart/software-engineer-data-berlin-351586","tags":["Technology"],"job_types":[],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1794682518},{"slug":"operations-strategy-manager-energy-markets-berlin-346294","company_name":"trawa","title":"Operations & Strategy Manager - Energy Markets","description":"<h1>Operations &amp; Strategy Manager</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Permanent employee · Full-time · Berlin (HQ)</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>Our mission for you</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">European energy costs are twice as high as in the US and China, and electricity demand is expected to double by 2050. This puts European industry under massive cost pressure – and companies need to act now.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">trawa is building the solution: the first integrated B2B energy platform that brings together energy procurement, energy management and the marketing of flexible assets in one product. This helps companies save up to 30% on their recurring electricity costs while switching to renewable energy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're the fastest-growing B2B energy platform in Europe. Active in Germany and Austria now, and expanding operations to a third market in 2027. We're on the road to European scale and move fast – the market window is open and we intend to own it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Now we are looking for an Operations &amp; Strategy Manager to own a business-critical part of our energy value chain: the processes behind how we configure, price and quote long-term energy products for our customers.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>About trawa</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">trawa is a tech-driven scale-up based in Berlin with around 100 employees, combining deep energy market expertise with in-house software development. We've raised over €35M to date, most recently a €24M Series A in May 2025, backed by Balderton, Headline, Speedinvest, AENU, Magnetic and Tiny VC. This role is based in our Berlin office, where we work together in person most of the week. We offer flexible working hours, so you can shape your day in a way that works for you.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>The Team</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll join our Energy &amp; Trading team, which owns the energy side of our business – from sourcing and portfolio management to making sure our customers' energy products work in practice. You'll report directly to our Energy &amp; Trading Manager and work closely with the COO, our Trading Team, Sales, Pricing, Product and Tech. You start without direct reports, but with a clear mandate: own our CPQ process end-to-end and grow the margin it generates.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>Who we are looking for</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong quantitative skills:</strong> You think analytically, feel at home with numbers and data and can confidently challenge quantitative results – without having to be a quant or developer yourself. Ideally, you have a degree in a quantitative or business field (e.g. economics, engineering, industrial engineering, business administration).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business acumen &amp; process mindset:</strong> You think commercially, care about margins and unit economics, enjoy turning messy processes into robust, scalable ones and prioritise by impact. Experience with commercial processes such as pricing or deal desks, in energy, financial services or any other industry, is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Interest in energy markets:</strong> You are fascinated by how energy markets work – from wholesale and forward markets to PPAs, hedging and pricing – and want to dive deep into them. Knowledge of the German energy market is a plus; experience in (energy) trading is explicitly not required – what matters is your drive to understand the mechanics and make the processes behind them work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hungry &amp; ambitious:</strong> You want to grow fast, take on responsibility early and set high standards for yourself. You don't wait for instructions and enjoy a steep learning curve, and work experience in a high-paced environment, e.g. a start-up, scale-up or consulting, is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High ownership &amp; structured execution:</strong> You drive topics end-to-end, align stakeholders across departments and turn ideas into scalable processes with tangible business impact. An affinity for AI-powered tools and automation to make processes faster and smarter is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong communication:</strong> You speak German at native level and very good English, and you translate confidently between commercial, quantitative and operational perspectives.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Operations &amp; Strategy Manager, you combine a strong analytical mind with process excellence and commercial drive:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own our CPQ process:</strong> You take end-to-end ownership of our CPQ (Configure, Price, Quote) processes for long-term energy products – from the customer request through pricing and offer creation to trade execution, across Sales, Pricing, Trading and Operations and for all our customer segments. You make this process faster, more robust and scalable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stabilise and grow our margins:</strong> Our customers hedge their energy costs with long-term products from us, such as PPAs and Futures/Forwards. You are responsible for stabilising our margins on these hedges and increasing them in the medium term – covering a multi-million euro gross margin.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pave the way to more complex products:</strong> Over the past three years, we have shown that we can profitably price, buy and sell energy. You build on that foundation and develop our long-term offering towards more complex, higher-margin products that fit our customers' needs even better.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bridge between trading and business:</strong> You work closely with our quant trading and data science team and turn their models and insights into processes and systems that work across teams and markets – so that pricing, risk and market insights reliably translate into better decisions and products for our customers.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>90 Day Goals</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>After 6 Weeks (Onboarding):</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business understanding:</strong> You have understood trawa's business, product and energy value chain in detail and got to know all relevant internal and external stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Portfolio knowledge:</strong> You understand our long-term product portfolio (PPAs, Futures/Forwards), our customers' hedging needs and how pricing, margins and risk come together in our offers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>CPQ mapping:</strong> You have mapped our current CPQ process – from customer request and pricing to offer creation and trade execution – and identified the key pain points and margin levers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Month 3 (Ramp-Up):</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Go-to CPQ owner:</strong> You are the go-to person for our CPQ process and have implemented first improvements that make it faster and more robust.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Margin transparency:</strong> You have created transparency on our margins across long-term hedges and derived first measures to stabilise them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Target process:</strong> You have designed a target CPQ process, started its implementation and proposed first, more complex products for our long-term offering.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>Why us?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact:</strong> European SMEs spend between €150k and €10M per year on electricity – most are overpaying and locked into outdated procurement. Your work will directly change how thousands of companies buy, manage and use energy. The impact is measurable, the market is massive, and the timing is now.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership:</strong> We empower our team members to take ownership of their work and drive results, regardless of background or experience level.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; Growth:</strong> We provide an annual budget and dedicated time for professional development. You'll have opportunities for mentorship, learning and career progression.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Diversity and Inclusion:</strong> We're an equal opportunity employer, and our team reflects that. Our organisation brings together over 15 nationalities, contributing a variety of languages, experiences and perspectives. At trawa, we're family-friendly with parents across all levels, and our diversity is represented throughout the company, including leadership. We're committed to an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Package &amp; Benefits:</strong> We offer a competitive compensation package including salary and stock options, 30 days of vacation, and a range of benefits including subsidies for home internet and lunches, a Sports Club membership, dedicated learning days with an annual learning budget, plus a weekly team lunch and regular team events.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At trawa, we're dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive and authentic workplace. If you're excited about this role but your experience doesn't align perfectly, we encourage you to apply – you may be the right fit for this or another opportunity.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/trawa/operations-strategy-manager-energy-markets-berlin-346294","tags":["Energy Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin HQ","created_at":1794681612},{"slug":"remote-portfolio-accountant-384566","company_name":"Access Destination Services","title":"Portfolio Accountant","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Access Your Potential.</strong><br />Join us to create and deliver experiences that inspire people, spark connection, and bring imagination to life—while having a lot of fun doing it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the Job</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re seeking a detail-oriented and organized <strong>Portfolio Accountant</strong> to join our Finance &amp; Accounting team! In this role, you’ll manage the day-to-day accounting operations for an assigned Access territory, ensuring accurate financial records, timely reporting, and effective financial support for territory operations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working closely with territory leadership and the broader Finance &amp; Accounting team, you’ll oversee accounts payable, accounts receivable, general ledger transactions, month-end closing activities, and financial reporting. This is a great opportunity for someone who enjoys working independently, solving problems, and building strong relationships with internal teams while keeping financial operations running smoothly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You'll Be Doing</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Accounting &amp; Financial Reporting</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage day-to-day accounting activities for an assigned territory, including accounts payable, accounts receivable, and general ledger transactions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Process supplier payments, client deposits, final payments, expense reports, and journal entries accurately and within established deadlines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare and maintain general ledger entries, account reconciliations, and supporting financial documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Complete month-end closing activities, ensuring financial records are accurate and up to date.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enter territory actuals into monthly budget comparison worksheets, review results for discrepancies, and flag variances for Controller review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor territory revenue, expenses, and cash flow to support accurate financial reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide financial information and supporting documentation to the Controller and Finance &amp; Accounting leadership.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Territory Accounting Support</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as a primary accounting resource for employees within the assigned territory.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with territory leadership and internal departments to resolve accounting-related questions and discrepancies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review and submit territory-specific labor and staffing reports in accordance with established procedures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support territory budgeting, forecasting, and financial reporting activities as assigned.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure timely and accurate processing of financial transactions to support ongoing territory operations.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compliance &amp; Financial Accuracy</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain accurate accounting records in accordance with applicable accounting standards and company policies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist with internal and external audits by maintaining organized financial records and supporting documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure accounting activities are completed in accordance with established procedures and reporting deadlines.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Training &amp; Team Collaboration</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide accounting-related guidance and training to new employees within the assigned territory as needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with the Finance &amp; Accounting team to ensure consistent application of established procedures, communicate accounting concerns, and escalate issues as appropriate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support additional territory-level accounting projects and responsibilities as assigned.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>About You</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We know that there’s no one in the world like you. And we know that you have a lot to offer the next company you work with. Below is a list of “nice-to-haves”, but don’t let those deter you from applying. Access believes that an inclusive team and culture is important. We seek applicants from all backgrounds to ensure we get the best, most creative talent on our team.</p><h2>Nice-to-haves:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li