e, test and packaging teams aligned and moving towards clear milestones.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for someone with an engineering background who has moved into programme or project management and still enjoys getting into the technical detail. You will be credible with engineers, able to understand the real constraints and dependencies, and able to turn them into plans, priorities and decisions that keep work moving.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work in a fast-paced, deep-tech environment where the work spans external partners as well as internal teams, and where clear ownership, early risk flagging and disciplined execution make a real difference to how quickly we get to deployment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll be doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the delivery of cross-functional technical programmes, from planning through to milestone completion</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain integrated plans, timelines and critical paths across photonics, electronics, firmware, test and packaging</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate technical requirements and engineering constraints into clear scope, priorities and deliverables</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify, track and escalate risks, dependencies and blockers early, and drive them to resolution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate tape-outs, fabrication runs and build cycles with external foundry, manufacturing and test partners</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run regular programme reviews, stand-ups and milestone gates, with clear actions and accountability</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Report progress, risks and trade-offs to engineering leads and senior leadership with data-led clarity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with engineering teams to define test readiness, qualification plans and re