 Development on strategic transactions such as fundraising and M&amp;A, partner with UK and regional leaders on new-market entry, support licence expansion, and help align Airwallex’s global policies and governance with UK and relevant EMEA requirements. You’ll also advise on marketing, referral and partnership initiatives, helping the business move quickly while managing legal and regulatory risk.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide clear, pragmatic advice on UK and relevant EMEA legal and regulatory requirements, helping teams navigate applicable rules while enabling responsible growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support Corporate Development on fundraising rounds and strategic transactions, including due diligence, data rooms, corporate approvals, investment documentation, cap table changes and ongoing governance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the business, Regulatory Legal and Regulatory Compliance teams on expansion into and launches in new markets across the UK and EMEA, including regulatory mapping, entity and licensing considerations, and corporate governance requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Align Airwallex’s policies, procedures and corporate governance frameworks across jurisdictions, with particular focus on UK requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Draft, review and negotiate referral agreements, marketing and sponsorship agreements, and other commercial arrangements, ensuring risks are appropriately managed and documented.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise on marketing, advertising and promotions, including claims, disclosures, digital campaigns, co-marketing and referral programmes, while supporting the review of customer-facing materials for legal and regulatory compliance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate and manage outside counsel on specialised matters in the UK and across EMEA, ensuring advice is high-quality, cost-effective and aligned to Airwallex’s risk appetite and business goals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use technology and AI-enabled tools, including templates, playbooks, contract lifecycle tools and knowledge bases, to increase the speed, consistency and quality of legal work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll work from our London office three days a week.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What we're looking for</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essentials</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualification as a solicitor or barrister in England and Wales, or an equivalent qualification in another UK jurisdiction, and in good standing with the relevant professional body.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in financial services and corporate law, preferably gained at a fast-growing technology or fintech company and/or a top-tier law firm.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated interest in financial services regulation and the fintech industry, with willingness to go deep on payments, e-money, money services and related regulatory topics in the UK and EMEA.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">In-depth knowledge of, or strong familiarity with, the UK legal and business environment, including how UK legislation, FCA requirements and cross-border rules impact fintech and payments businesses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience drafting and negotiating corporate and commercial agreements, with strong written and verbal communication skills that make complex issues clear to non-lawyers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong stakeholder management skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams, including Corporate Development, Finance, Product, Compliance, Risk and Marketing, across time zones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated capa