"created_at":1794724813},{"slug":"manager-associate-director-project-management-london-347583","company_name":"Relationrx","title":"Manager/Associate Director - Project Management","description":"<h2><strong>About Relation</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relation is a sector defining TechBio company developing transformational medicines, with technology at our core. Our ambition is to understand human biology in unprecedented ways, discovering therapies to treat some of life’s most devastating diseases. We leverage single-cell multi-omics from patient tissue, functional assays, and machine learning to drive disease understanding, from cause to cure.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are scaling rapidly and building a team of exceptional individuals to push the boundaries of drug discovery. You will work in highly interdisciplinary teams where biology, computation, and engineering come together to solve complex problems that have not been solved before. Our state-of-the-art wet and dry labs in the heart of London are designed to accelerate this integration and translate insight into impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are committed to building diverse and inclusive teams. Relation is an equal opportunities employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital or civil partnership status, gender reassignment, race, colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin, religion or belief, disability, or age.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By joining Relation, you will help define how medicines are discovered and deliver meaningful impact for patients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relation is offering an outstanding opportunity for an experienced Project Manager to work in close partnership with our Programme and Project Leaders, putting you in a prime position to help shape delivery plans and drive our osteoporosis programme forward.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working across the full discovery journey, you'll help move the programme through Target ID, Hit-to-Lead, Lead Optimisation, Candidate Selection and beyond — coordinating across the multiple projects that make up the programme, our internal interdisciplinary teams, and third-party partners such as CROs, all while navigating the ambiguity of discovery-stage science with confidence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll operate at programme level, with visibility across every project within the osteoporosis programme, partnering with the Programme Leader and the Project Leaders who own each individual project. If this sounds like you, and you thrive in matrixed environments and want a real hand in shaping how tomorrow's medicines are discovered, come and join us in the heart of London.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Day to day, you will</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Programme, Project Leaders and sponsors to understand the strategic objectives and delivery requirements across the programme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Orchestrate the matrix team to deliver against project objectives, motivating all team members with clear direction and communication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with functional leads to ensure appropriate resource allocation and to onboard supplementary resources where needed to support delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively manage plans, budgets, risks and issues across the programme, escalating to senior management when appropriate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support leadership in navigating high-impact, high-risk situations with clear analysis, high transparency and a spirit of partnership — even in the face of significant adversity or major obstacles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate scientific and strategic objectives into integrated project plans, timelines and milestones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate execution across the wet lab, ML research, data science and engineering teams, owning cross-team dependencies and prioritisation, and actively monitoring interdependencies across teams as the programme evolves.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify and manage risks across the programme, working with team leads to mitigate blockers before they affect delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate joint governance bodies (steering committees, working groups, technical committees) — agendas, materials, minutes and follow-ups — and ensure decisions are documented and actioned.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate status clearly to internal leadership and external partners, surfacing decisions and trade-offs as they arise.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain project documentation, decision logs and operational hygiene to a standard that supports a multi-year, partnered effort.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate resource allocation and operational support across the computational and wet lab teams where required.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify and embed improvements to ways of working as the programme evolves.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Professionally, you will have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A degree in life sciences, project management, or a related field; advanced degree or equivalent industry experience welcome.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant Programme/Project management experience in biotech, pharma, or comparable scientific R&amp;D settings, ideally including early-stage discovery programmes (target ID through to candidate selection), sufficient to operate as the senior Project manager for a major, multi-year effort.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort managing a programme where scope and workstreams may evolve significantly as science matures from exploratory biology through to a defined lead series.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scientific literacy sufficient to engage credibly with discussions spanning wet lab biology, single-cell omics, and machine learning, and enough grounding in the discovery pipeline (target validation, hit-to-lead, lead optimisation) to track progress and flag risk without needing to do the science yourself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with stage-gate or portfolio governance frameworks as applied to early discovery programmes (e.g. go/no-go criteria, TPP evolution, milestone-based progression).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience overseeing third-party or outsourced work packages (e.g. CROs, academic collaborators, specialist service providers) — tracking deliverables, timelines, and quality against agreed scope, and escalating issues appropriately.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency with modern project management methodologies, artifacts and tools (e.g. MS Project, Smartsheet, Asana, Jira; Gantt, RAID logs).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organisational skills with a record of managing complex, interdependent works treams in matrixed environments. Comfort with the operational realities of R&amp;D projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written and verbal communication, including the ability to write clearly for senior external audiences.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><u>Bonus Experience</u>: </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Awareness of the discovery-to-IND pathway and its major inflection points (IND-enabling tox, CMC/formulation, DMPK, regulatory strategy) sufficient to anticipate future PM needs, even if this programme doesn't reach that stage during the role's tenure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Any exposure to pre-IND regulatory interactions or translational/preclinical handover</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Personally, you</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are comfortable working in a matrixed environment, <strong>balancing multiple stakeholders </strong>and contributing effectively across teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take <strong>ownership of your work</strong>, proactively seek opportunities to contribute, and enable others to do their best work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Communicate openly and directly</strong>, give and receive feedback constructively, and handle challenging conversations with respect.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Actively seek out diverse perspectives</strong>, build strong working relationships, and contribute to shared goals across teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Embrace challenges with openness and resilience</strong>, set high standards for yourself, and strive to deliver meaningful outcomes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Working Style &amp; Culture at Relation</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Relation, we operate in a <strong>matrixed, interdisciplinary environment</strong>, where impact is driven through collaboration across scientific, technical, and operational domains. We collaborate, and you will partner with colleagues across multiple teams and projects, contributing your expertise while aligning to shared company priorities. We work together and win together! <strong>The patient is waiting!</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Recruitment Agencies</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please note that Relation does not accept unsolicited resumes from agencies. Resumes should not be forwarded to our job aliases or employees. Relation will not be liable for any fees associated with unsolicited CVs.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/relationrx/manager-associate-director-project-management-london-347583","tags":["Growth"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794724813},{"slug":"capital-allowances-manager-london-116119","company_name":"Unity Advisory","title":"Capital Allowances Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Unity Advisory</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unity Advisory is a modern advisory business built for today's CFO, with connected solutions across finance, deals and tax. Focussed on client outcomes, seasoned experts lead every engagement, in an operating model powered by AI and free from audit conflict.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building out our capital allowances offering and are looking for a Manager. You'll run a portfolio of client engagements, from single-asset claims through to large multi-site capital expenditure projects, working across all sectors. You'll support the technical lead on claims, act as the main point of contact for clients, and drive growth in this part of the practice.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a genuine opportunity to shape how the team operates, not slot into an existing one. Unity's technology and AI tools handle the heavy lifting on claim preparation and data analysis, freeing you up for the technical judgement and client relationships that actually move the needle.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead a portfolio of capital allowances engagements across multiple sectors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare, review and submit capital allowances claims, ensuring technical accuracy and compliance with current legislation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise clients on fixed asset tax treatment, expenditure planning and related incentives, including structures and buildings allowances and R&amp;D-adjacent capital reliefs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage HMRC correspondence and enquiries, negotiating on clients' behalf where needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interpret asset schedules, fixed asset registers and financial data to identify qualifying expenditure and maximise client outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce clear, well-structured technical reports and client-facing deliverables.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coach junior team members through day-to-day oversight, review and quality control.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to business development, including proposals, pitches and opportunities within existing client relationships.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical skills — able to interpret financial data and asset schedules, and pick up new digital tools quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid track record in capital allowances or fixed asset tax advisory, gained at an established advisory or accountancy firm.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical knowledge of UK capital allowances legislation, comfortable managing multiple live engagements at once.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CTA, ACA, ACCA, RICS or equivalent qualification.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident communicator — credible with senior stakeholders, able to explain complex tax positions in plain terms.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are committed to an inclusive and accessible recruitment process. Please let us know if you need any reasonable adjustments or support when applying or arranging your interview.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We do not accept unsolicited CVs from third-party agencies.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/unity-advisory/capital-allowances-manager-london-116119","tags":["Tax"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London, Mayfair","created_at":1794724811},{"slug":"advisory-data-architect-london-16290","company_name":"Unity Advisory","title":"Advisory Data Architect","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Unity Advisory</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unity Advisory is a modern advisory business built for today's CFO, with connected solutions across finance, deals and tax. Focussed on client outcomes, seasoned experts lead every engagement, in an operating model powered by AI and free from audit conflict.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an experienced Advisory Data Architect to own data design across our advisory engagements. This is a platform and design-authority role with a hands-on edge, combining finance-focused business understanding with modern data architecture, platforms and governance. You will define how data - across a client’s business - is structured, governed, and served so that AI, analytics, and management reporting are reliable and scalable. As a Senior Manager, you will lead architecture decisions, guide engineers, shape client data strategy, architecture, governance, and be accountable for the coherence and quality of the data estate you design.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a client-facing role within our AI Advisory team, setting the data architecture that our engagements — and our clients' AI ambitions — are built on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define target-state data architectures for clients — models, storage, pipelines, and access patterns — balancing rigour with delivery realism.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish data modelling standards and curated domain layers across the a variety of systems (e.g. ERP, CRM, Manufacturing) and data sources, with end-to-end lineage and provenance sufficient for audit and controls.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Map and integrate finance source systems (ERP, EPM, sub-ledgers, and consolidation tools) into governed, analytics-ready models.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design the finance data foundations for applied AI/ML: governed retrieval sources for RAG, feature stores, and the architecture that keeps AI systems fed with trustworthy, reconciled finance data.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set patterns for secure, compliant finance data platforms — access control, data sensitivity, segregation of duties, isolation, and alignment to standards such as ISO 27001.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide architectural direction for cloud data platforms, infrastructure as code, CI/CD, and observability, ensuring designs are cost-aware and operable.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define the data lineage and controls that support responsible production AI — monitoring, confidence scoring, and human-in-the-loop review.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate ambiguous business and client problems into clear architectural decisions and scoped roadmaps under delivery pressure.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own key technical trade-offs and communicate them clearly to engineers, product stakeholders, and senior client sponsors.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentor data engineers, raise the technical bar across the team, and contribute reusable patterns, reference architectures, and accelerators.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essential</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant experience designing and delivering data architectures for production systems, with evidence that your designs have shipped and run - not remained on paper.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep expertise in data modelling, warehouse/lakehouse design, and data governance.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on background in SQL and Python, and fluency with at least one major cloud provider (AWS or Azure) and modern data platforms (e.g. Snowflake, Databricks).</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">System-level judgement on how data architecture shapes AI outcomes: designing governed sources for RAG, structuring data for retrieval and orchestration, and deciding where structured outputs and tool use fit.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to set standards and lead engineers while remaining close to implementation.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong stakeholder skills, including engaging senior client sponsors and explaining architectural trade-offs clearly.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong Preference</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience architecting the data layer behind AI or analytics products in production.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Informed views on the trade-offs between fine-tuning, RAG, and long-context approaches, and how each changes data architecture requirements, including context window economics and prompt caching.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with infrastructure as code, CI/CD, and observability for data platforms.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Awareness of MCP and tool-orchestration concepts and their implications for composable, data-driven AI systems.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent use of AI-assisted development tools (e.g. Claude Code, Cursor), with a clear view of where they help and where human design judgement must lead.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Security and compliance experience (e.g. ISO 27001 alignment, access control design).</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Consulting or advisory background, owning problems end-to-end rather than a single workstream.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evidence of self-directed building — side projects, internal tools, or startups.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to finance data, PE/M&amp;A, or portfolio-company environments.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relevant certifications (e.g. AWS/Azure architect-level credentials).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are committed to an inclusive and accessible recruitment process. Please let us know if you need any reasonable adjustments or support when applying or arranging your interview.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;ma