">We are on an incredible journey to build a <strong>global leading company, with a </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/en/careers"><strong><u>unique culture</u></strong></a>. We already partner with 40K+ companies of all sizes, serving more than 1M+ members, and have reached €800M+ in ARR.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prevention as the new norm. That's what we're building with our team of 1000+ people. If it speaks to you: we're hiring across France, Spain, Belgium, and Canada. And beyond.</p><h1>Role overview 🌟</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Alan has passed 1M members, works with 40K+ companies and operates in seven countries. New products and a flagship international event are coming, and the Brand team is investing in bigger campaigns. So far brand spend has gone mostly to broad awareness. We now need targeted B2B campaigns for specific verticals (for example TNS, retirees, very small company owners), run alongside the broad campaigns to reinforce them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own these vertical B2B brand campaigns for France, plus a portfolio of other brand projects. You'll work closely with the Brand Lead, Product Marketing, Growth, segment owners and Sales. This is an individual-contributor role at C1-D level.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you'll do</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Vertical campaigns:</strong> Define the audience, message, proof points and channels for each priority vertical. Choose priorities and objectives with segment owners, Growth and Product Marketing. Run each campaign from brief to post-mortem, and build reusable toolkits (messaging, assets, case studies) for other teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product and offer launches:</strong> Support the launch of new product features (e.g. Mo, Alan Précision) and new offers (e.g. Alan retirees) in France. Work in strong collaboration with the Product teams to build a creative, impactful go-to-market that stands out in the market. Turn product positioning into launch plans and assets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partnerships and events: </strong>Run vertical-specific events, sponsorships, ambassador and creator partnerships that build credibility with each audience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Local markets:</strong> Give feedback on local briefs and plans. Spot French initiatives that could scale to other markets and capture them in playbooks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Measurement:</strong> Set KPIs for every project (reach in the target, qualified leads, pipeline influenced, brand perception). Run test-and-learn with Growth and Data. Manage budgets, vendors and deadlines.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>You're a good fit if you</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have<strong> 7+ years </strong>of <strong>in-house brand marketing</strong> (B2C, B2B or B2B2C). Paid media or media planning is a big plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have<strong> led at least two B2B campaigns</strong> or <strong>brand projects end to end</strong>, and can walk us through the problem, your choices and the measurable result.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have <strong>managed agencies and budgets</strong> and made trade-offs when resources were tight.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are a<strong> generalist </strong>across campaigns, content, partnerships, events and PR, with sharp creative judgment you can defend with senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set<strong> brand KPIs</strong> and link brand work to pipeline or lead quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work well with Sales and Growth and can influence without authority.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Written and verbal communication fluency in<strong> English and French</strong></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For this opportunity, we are aiming to hire within the<strong> C1-D </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="postings-link" href="https://alan.com/en/careers/a/salary-equity"><strong>level range</strong></a><strong>.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>🎯 Important note: we hire people, not roles</strong>.</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited about this opportunity but don't check every box, we'd love to hear from you. Everyone, no matter how underrepresented, should feel free to apply, as it can only bring learnings or success.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you identify yourself as a woman: Did you know that research shows women often apply only when meeting 100% of requirements?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remember, this is just a guide, not a checklist. We'll be thrilled to receive your application!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🔖 Check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/about"><u>About Alan</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/careers"><u>Career</u></a> pages, as well as our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/alan"><u>Medium</u></a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://blog.alan.com/"><u>blog</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.com/Overview/Working-at-Alan-EI_IE1696043.11,15.htm"><u>Glassdoor page</u></a> for more info.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>You want to know more about Alan?</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🙌 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/en/careers/a/salary-equity"><u>Perks &amp; Benefits</u></a>: Alaners are provided with a stimulating environment and perks ensuring they are happy, efficient and spend only high-quality time with co-workers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤘 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/en/about/a/leadership-principles"><u>A strong culture</u></a>: People joining Alan are often surprised and delighted by our innovative working method. We have a set of cultural values that guide our approach to work</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/alan/brand-manager-b2b-anywhere-in-france-463852","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Anywhere in France","created_at":1794703212},{"slug":"research-scientist-foundation-models-and-multimodal-ai-paris-108085","company_name":"Owkin","title":"Research Scientist – Foundation Models and Multimodal AI","description":"<h1>About us</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owkin is an agentic AI company pioneering Biological Artificial Superintelligence to solve problems in biology where human researchers alone have failed.<br />Owkin builds K Pro - an AI scientist for pharmaceutical research and strategic decision-making. K Pro orchestrates a suite of AI skills and tools to decode complex biology, accelerate research, and dramatically increase productivity.<br />K Pro is built on Owkin’s unrivalled multimodal patient data network, state-of-the-art AI for biology and a decade of experience working with pharmaceutical partners.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Position is based in our Paris office or remotely in France, UK, Germany.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Please submit your CV in English</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>About the role:</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"> We are seeking a driven <strong>Research Scientist</strong> with hands-on expertise in Foundation Models (FMs) and Multimodal AI to help drive the next phase of our machine learning platform.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role, you will bridge cutting-edge AI research and practical application. Rather than training massive base models from scratch, your focus will be on fine-tuning, adapting, and aligning open-weights foundation models across diverse data modalities (e.g. structured tabular data, single-cell scRNA-seq, image representations, and natural language) to build multimodal systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><h1>In particular, you will be responsible for:</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Model adaptation and optimization:</strong> Adapt, fine-tune, and evaluate state-of-the-art open-source foundation models (e.g., domain-specific transformers, vision-language models) using fine-tuning and transfer learning strategies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Multimodal integration:</strong> Design and implement cross-modal alignment architectures (e.g., contrastive learning, projection heads, unified embedding spaces) to fuse structured, sequential, and text/image data layers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pipeline and evaluation engineering:</strong> Build rigorous, domain-tailored benchmarking frameworks and evaluation pipelines to validate model reliability, generalization, and downstream task performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Applied R&amp;D collaboration:</strong> Work closely with cross-functional teams (data engineers, domain specialists, and software engineers) to integrate adapted models into scalable production and inference workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Low-hanging fruit innovation:</strong> Identify high-impact, incremental improvements in data pre-processing, embedding representation, and fine-tuning to maximize model performance without unnecessary computational overhead. </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><h1>About you</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Required qualifications / experience:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Education:</strong> Ph.D. or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Machine Learning, Mathematics or a related quantitative field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience:</strong> 2-4 years of post-degree experience applying deep learning and foundation models to complex datasets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Foundation models:</strong> Demonstrated experience adapting and fine-tuning foundation models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Multimodal learning:</strong> Proven experience with cross-modal representation learning, joint embedding alignment (e.g., CLIP-style architectures), or vision-language models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical stack:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced proficiency in Python and modern deep learning frameworks (<strong>PyTorch</strong>, Hugging Face ecosystem).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with fine-tuning techniques.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with data engineering tools for handling large-scale or multi-modal datasets (Parquet, AnnData, HDF5).</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"> Preferred qualifications/bonus:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with biological or omics data (e.g., scRNA-seq, spatial transcriptomics, clinical and/or histology data).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience deploying or scaling models using containerized environments (Docker, Kubernetes) and cloud infrastructure (AWS/GCP).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of open-source contributions or peer-reviewed publications at top ML conferences (NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR, CVPR) or domain-specific journals.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"> #LI-HB1</p><h1>What we offer</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible work organization</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Friendly and informal working environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Opportunity to work with an international team with high technical and scientific backgrounds</p></li></ul><h1>Recruitment Process &amp; Security</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please complete the form and submit your CV.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owkin is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, gender, sexual orientation, age, color, religion, national origin, protected veteran status or on the basis of disability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owkin is a great place to work. As a coveted workplace we are, unfortunately, vulnerable to recruitment phishing scams. We urge all job seekers and candidates to be wary of potential scams. Most of these have individuals posing as representatives of prominent companies, including Owkin, with the aim of obtaining personal, sensitive, or financial information from applicants. These scams prey upon an individual’s desire to obtain a job and can sometimes “feel” like a genuine recruitment process. Some red flags are identified below. Should you encounter a recruitment process that claims to be for Owkin but is not consistent with the below, please do not provide any personal or financial information:</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Legitimate Owkin recruitment processes include communication with candidates through recognized professional networks, such as LinkedIn.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communication is always through an official Owkin email address (from the @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://owkin.com">owkin.com</a> domain), over the phone or through our applicant tracking system (Ashby).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Owkin talent team do use platforms such as LinkedIn, however if you have any concern or doubt about this contact, please ask for them to send an email from @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Owkin.com">Owkin.com</a>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Owkin talent team will not solicit personal data from candidates during the application phase including, but not limited to, date of birth, social security numbers, or bank account information;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Legitimate Owkin interviews may be conducted over the phone, in person, or via an approved enterprise videoconferencing service (Google Meets). <strong>They will not occur via Signal, Telegram or Messenger</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owkin offers of employment are based on merit and only extended once a candidate has interviewed with members of the talent and hiring team. Offers will be extended both verbally and in written format.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you think that you have been a victim of fraud,</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check the identity of the talent team on LinkedIn</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check our senior team on our website <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://owkin.com/team/"><u>https://owkin.com/team/</u></a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check the existence of the position on our website: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.owkin.com/careers#current-opportunities"><u>https://www.owkin.com/careers#current-opportunities</u></a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notify Owkin's recruitment unit at this address <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- style="min-height:1.5em">contact the following authorities:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">[FR] <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://internet-signalement.gouv.fr/"><u>https://internet-signalement.gouv.fr/</u></a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">[UK] <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.actionfraud.police.uk/reporting-fraud-and-cyber-crime"><u>https://www.actionfraud.police.uk/reporting-fraud-and-cyber-crime</u></a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">[US] <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://reportfraud.ftc.gov/"><u>https://reportfraud.ftc.gov/</u></a></p></li></ul></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/owkin/research-scientist-foundation-models-and-multimodal-ai-paris-108085","tags":["R&TECH"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794703212},{"slug":"technical-delivery-manager-paris-463863","company_name":"Legora","title":"Technical Delivery Manager - Paris","description":"<h2>About Us</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Legora is redefining how legal work gets done. Not built for lawyers, built with them. We work alongside the world’s best legal teams, who expect excellence, precision, and speed, and we hold ourselves to the same bar.<br /><br />Our AI-native workspace lets legal professionals move faster, think more clearly, and operate with sharper precision. By analysing thousands of documents in minutes and powering end-to-end workflows, we cut through complexity, teams can focus on what matters: judgment, strategy, and outcomes.<br /><br />2,100+ customers across 80+ countries trust us, including Cleary Gottlieb, Goodwin, Linklaters, White &amp; Case, Dentons, and Barclays. We’ve scaled to<strong> $200M+ in ARR</strong>, with teams across Europe, North America and APAC, and continue to expand through acquisitions including Qura, Walter AI, Graceview, Cadastral, and Wexler.<br /><br />We partner with world-class performers: including Aaron Judge and the New York Yankees, Ludvig Åberg (and his caddie), and campaigns featuring Jude Law.<br /><br />Joining Legora means three things.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>lean in: </strong>ownership over titles, outcomes over intentions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>fight for excellence:</strong> high standards, direct, ego-free feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We<strong> grow together:</strong> as a team and with our customers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mission before ego. Everyone contributes. No one coasts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re driven by impact, pace, and raising the bar. This is the place.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong> <br /><br />As a Technical Delivery Manager at Legora, you will play a central role in ensuring customers successfully deploy, integrate, and adopt our AI-native platform. You'll lead end-to-end technical implementations, act as the primary technical point of contact, and shape how seamlessly new customers go live and scale within Legora.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Be Doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead integration projects from kickoff through go-live, owning technical documentation, test plans, and rollout execution to ensure on-time, high-quality delivery</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the dedicated technical point of contact during implementation and early adoption, including proactive monitoring and regular stakeholder updates through go-live and the post-rollout period</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Configure and support customer environments including SSO, DMS integrations (iManage, SharePoint, NetDocuments), and API-based connections</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide dedicated post-rollout technical support for enterprise clients, troubleshooting advanced issues and driving high customer satisfaction</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate across Sales, Engineering, and Customer Success to align on requirements and ensure a smooth rollout experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver technical training and guidance to customer teams on configuration, workflows, and best practices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Feed insights from delivery projects back to product and engineering to improve future implementations</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in technical delivery, implementation, or a similar customer-facing technical role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong hands-on experience with SSO, authentication protocols, and enterprise integrations (DMS platforms, APIs)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent project management skills with a structured, proactive approach to managing multiple parallel projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to translate technical concepts clearly for non-technical audiences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communicator who builds trusted relationships across customer and internal teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working autonomously in a fast-paced, high-growth environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional proficiency in French or German</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Legora is an Equal Opportunity Employer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Legora, we believe great teams are built on diversity of thought and experience. We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive, high-performance culture where everyone can do their best work. We welcome people of all backgrounds and don’t discriminate based on race, color, religion, national origin, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.</p><hr><p>Compensation: €75K – €90K</p><ul><li> • €75K – €90K</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/legora/technical-delivery-manager-paris-463863","tags":["Global Services"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794703211},{"slug":"sar-remote-sensing-engineer-paris-289669","company_name":"Signal Processing Engineer (RF Processing & Analytics)","title":"SAR Remote Sensing Engineer","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>About the Role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As SAR Remote Sensing Engineer, you are the subject matter expert on applying advanced signal processing and machine learning to SAR data within our RF analytics team. You own the analytics layer end to end: algorithm design, real-time implementation and field validation on real captures from our own platforms. You will also shape the move toward multi-modal solutions that combine SAR with optical and RF sensor feeds. Cycles are measured in months, and the scope grows with the company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Responsibilities</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead initiatives using SAR polarimetry and coherence for automated change detection.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and prototype state-of-the-art machine learning models for SAR image segmentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop algorithms for target detection and object classification on SAR data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fuse SAR with optical, RF and other data sources to support GNSS-denied operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Port algorithms from Python prototypes to real-time pipelines with software and embedded/FPGA teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the capture, labelling and replay tooling that makes performance claims reproducible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Validate performance on simulated and real-world datasets, in the lab and on field-test campaigns.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with radar, radio, electronic warfare and computer vision teams to define what the analytics layer needs from each sensor.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Candidate Requirements</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Master’s or PhD in electrical engineering, telecommunications engineering, signal processing, applied mathematics or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of experience in radar signal processing or SAR remote sensing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of SAR phenomenology and its information content, including coherence, amplitude, phase and polarimetry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Theoretical and practical expertise in machine learning, both deep learning and classical techniques.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience taking at least one algorithm from prototype to real hardware running on real signals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong Python skills and sound engineering practices (Git, code reviews, testing, documentation).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to GEOINT, ELINT or SIGINT work is a plus, and you are comfortable with defense security vetting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to travel periodically to lab and field tests.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/signal-processing-engineer-rf-processing-analytics/sar-remote-sensing-engineer-paris-289669","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794692413},{"slug":"electrical-engineer-launcher-paris-181304","company_name":"Signal Processing Engineer (RF Processing & Analytics)","title":"Electrical Engineer (Launcher)","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Overview</strong><br /><br />Harmattan AI is developing new hardware products within the Launcher module: field-deployable drone launchers designed to be deployed and operated autonomously in demanding field environments. These products require dedicated electronics design with complex architecture in a constrained environment – PCBs integrating power conversion, energy management, control and communication interfaces – optimised for cost at volume. The Launcher team is seeking a dedicated hardware engineer to own electronics design end-to-end and accelerate the path to production milestones.<br /><br /><strong>Ideal candidate</strong><br /><br />A senior hardware engineer who has designed and shipped complex PCBs, ideally mixing digital and significant power (hundreds of watts), into production. They are rigorous on schematics, layout, and bring-up, and have a strong instinct for cost and manufacturability. They design with real-world operating conditions in mind - temperature, moisture, surges - and an interest in battery thermal management; direct experience of outdoor-deployed equipment is a plus rather than a prerequisite. They are comfortable working autonomously in a small team and can bridge hardware and firmware.<br /><br /><strong>Skills required</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">PCB schematic and layout design (Altium Designer preferred)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Power electronics design: ~300 W DC/DC conversion, protection, derating, efficiency and thermal budgets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thermal regulation: temperature sensing and control loops, battery storage temperature management, heatsinking</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Power over Ethernet (IEEE 802.3af/at/bt): combined power and data delivery, isolation, cable budgets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mixed-signal design: power management, MCU interfaces, communication buses (SPI, I2C, UART, USB, CAN, Ethernet)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hardware bring-up and debug: bench equipment proficiency</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">DFM/DFA for PCB manufacturing and assembly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Component sele