<li>
<p>2–5 years of experience in account management, customer success, or post-sales roles, ideally within SaaS, cloud computing, or technology infrastructure.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Strong technical understanding and the confidence to engage effectively with both developers and senior business stakeholders.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Proven ability to build and maintain customer relationships while managing multiple stakeholders and competing priorities.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Understanding of key commercial and customer success metrics, including churn, usage, annual and monthly recurring revenue (ARR/MRR), and net revenue retention.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Strong analytical skills, with the ability to interpret usage data, identify trends, assess account health, and make data-driven recommendations.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Excellent written and verbal communication, presentation, and negotiation skills.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Proficiency with CRM systems, analytics tools, and team collaboration platforms such as Slack.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>A proactive, self-directed approach, with the ability to take end-to-end ownership of customer accounts and deliver measurable outcomes.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Familiarity with cloud platforms, GPU infrastructure, AI/ML technologies, or developer tools is considered an advantage.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Successful completion of a background check.</p>
</li>
<li>
