r - Control Node","description":"<p><strong>About the Role </strong></p><p>Destinus is looking for a highly motivated and hands-on mechanical engineer capable of delivering engineering solutions as part of the research and development in the Destinus Systems department. In this role you will design and develop a control node for air defence and strike systems, including all relevant mechanical subsystems. The ideal candidate is a strong team player with good social and communication skills to continuously coordinate with the peers of the respective engineering disciplines and teams, has a demonstrated ability to take technical ownership during development and drive technical solutions.</p><p><strong>What you will do</strong></p><p>· Generate 3D CAD models, drawings, schematics, bills of material, and other related documentation required for manufacturing, integration and testing</p><p>· Deliver technical documentation including any engineering calculations, analysis and assumptions required to substantiate your design decisions and solutions</p><p>· Create engineering design, prototypes, and manufacturing plans for an air defence and strike systems control node</p><p>· Manage suppliers and manufacturers by addressing any technical questions and resolving any issues which may arise during the manufacturing process.</p><p>· Select standard parts, fasteners, equipment, and consumables following best practices and industry standards</p><p>· Take ownership of your design work and closely coordinate with your peers in the engineering department across the involved engineering disciplines (systems, safety, electrical, aerospace, etc.)</p><p>· Coach junior engineers and interns in mechanical design, manufacturing and CAD.</p><p>· Support the product development process through the design review process (SRR, PDR, CDR etc.)</p><p>· Support and accompany the integration, assembly and manufacturing phases of the control nodes from a mechanical engineering point of view</p><p>· Drive innovation with new ideas to keep Destinus’ air defence and strike systems</p><p>· Support both the structured product development process as well as the rapid prototyping approach at the engineering department</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><strong>What you will need</strong></p><p>· BSc. In Mechanical Engineering, Design Engineering or a related discipline.</p><p>· Ideally, technical training as a mechanical designer / drafter</p><p>· 2-5 years of working experience in mechanical engineering in defence or in a related industry sector (e.g. aerospace) with close ties to manufacturing</p><p>· Experience with design of automated solutions, special machines or test benches is a benefit</p><p>· Experience with Siemens NX is a must, experience with Teamcenter is a plus</p><p>· Ideally, experience in several different phases: design, build, integration, test, and operation.</p><p>· Knowledge of military standards (MIL-STD, STANAG, AECTP) and engineering and requirement management tools (Jama, Jira, Confluence etc.)</p><p>· Knowledge of relevant technical topics for military control nodes (communication protocols, tactical data links, firing control, radar sensors, safety etc.) is a plus</p><p>· Willingness to travel to different Destinus sites (max. 20%)</p><p>· Strong communication skills and ability to work in a fast-paced, dynamic, international and multidisciplinary development team</p><p>· Proactive, ownership-driven mindset with strong problem-solving capabilities</p><p>· Strong analytical skills and ability to work autonomously</p><p>· Fluency in English is required; German is a plus.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/destinusgroup/mechanical-engineer-control-node-zurich-68036","tags":["Aviation & Aerospace","R&D & Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Zürich, Switzerland","created_at":1794637207},{"slug":"data-platform-manager-zurich-111131","company_name":"Destinusgroup","title":"Data Platform Manager","description":"<p><strong>About the role</strong></p><p>As Data Platform Manager you will own Destinus's company data platform. Built on Microsoft Fabric, it brings together data from our different systems, and it serves the reporting and data agents that production, supply chain, program management, and finance work from every week.</p><p>You will own its architecture: how OneLake and our lakehouses are structured, how data lands in them from the systems we run, and how it holds up as more of the business comes to depend on it. You will lead a small team of data engineers — setting direction, reviewing their work, growing them — and you will keep building yourself. You are also the person who makes our AI ambitions possible: the foundation behind our data agents and our Company Brain is yours to design and deliver.</p><p>At Destinus we are redefining the future of aerospace manufacturing, building advanced Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs) across three European plants. The data you will work with is physical — parts, build progress, shortages, non-conformances — and the questions asked of it get harder each year as we grow. If you want a platform you can still shape rather than one already set in concrete, this is a good moment to arrive.</p><p><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><ul><li>Own the architecture of our Microsoft Fabric estate end to end — OneLake, our lakehouses and their bronze, silver, and gold layers, workspace and domain structure, naming conventions, and the standards that keep it coherent as it grows.</li><li>Lead, mentor, and grow a small team of data engineers: set priorities, review code, raise the technical bar, and develop the people.</li><li>Stay hands-on. You will build pipelines, notebooks, and Delta tables yourself, not only direct others who do.</li><li>Own the integrations that land data in OneLake from our source systems — ERP, HR, shopfloor, quality, and the business applications that come after them — choosing sensibly between Data Factory pipelines, dataflows, shortcuts, and mirroring for each source.</li><li>Own the gold layer and the semantic models built on it, so that Power BI reads from one governed source rather than from copies scattered around the business.</li><li>Work closely with our Business Operations &amp; Data Specialists, who represent the business owners of each domain: turn their requirements into the right gold tables, agree definitions with them, and give them a platform they can query, validate, and explain to the business with confidence.</li><li>Own lineage across the estate: know what feeds what, be able to prove it to an auditor, and make dependencies visible rather than tribal knowledge.</li><li>Build the data foundation for our AI programme — the lakehouse structures, pipelines, and knowledge graph behind our Fabric data agents and our Company Brain — and deliver it to a standard that can be trusted with a real question.</li><li>Design and maintain the OneLake security and access model together with your team: workspace roles, access groups, and the controls that decide who sees what in the lake.</li><li>Keep the platform reliable, observable, and cost-aware: monitoring, alerting, recovery, and disciplined use of our Fabric capacity — including knowing what a runaway notebook costs us.</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><strong>What You’ll Need</strong></p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Data Engineering, or a related field.</li><li>5-8 years of data engineering experience, including real ownership of a lakehouse architecture rather than only delivering against someone else's.</li><li><strong>Hands-on Microsoft Fabric experience is strongly preferred</strong> — OneLake, lakehouses, Delta tables, the SQL analytics endpoint, Data Factory pipelines, Spark notebooks, and semantic models in Direct Lake mode. If your depth is in Azure Synapse, Databricks, or Data Lake Storage Gen2 and you have since moved onto Fabric in earnest, we will take that seriously.</li><li>Strong command of the medallion pattern and of Delta Lake in practice: partitioning, schema evolution, table maintenance, and why a gold table behaves the way it does.</li><li><strong>Genuinely hands-on.</strong> Strong SQL, solid PySpark, and comfort building and orchestrating pipelines yourself. This is not a role that stops at diagrams.</li><li>Practical understanding of Fabric capacity: how workloads consume it, how to spot what is burning it, and how to keep the platform inside its envelope.</li><li> Experience leading engineers — formally, or as a technical lead who set direction and mentored others. A first step into people management is welcome if the technical leadership is already there.</li><li>Proven integration experience with ERP systems such as Microsoft Dynamics 365 / MSD, as well as APIs, flat-file landings, and change data capture from operational databases.</li><li>Solid data modelling skills, including dimensional modelling and an understanding of how a semantic layer serves Power BI.</li><li> Working knowledge of lineage, data governance, and access control in a cloud platform; exposure to Microsoft Purview is a plus.</li><li>Interest or experience in the data foundations behind AI assistants — retrieval, knowledge graphs, and preparing data so that an agent can answer with it.</li><li>Aerospace or another regulated industry is an advantage; so is experience in a start-up or scale-up.</li><li>Fluent in English; additional European languages are a plus.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><p>You are an architect who never stops building. You have strong opinions about how a platform should be structured, and you earn the right to them by being in the code. You would rather make a design decision explicit and documented than let it live in one person's head.</p><p>You care more about reliability than novelty. You know that the measure of a data platform is whether people trust the numbers that come out of it on a Monday morning, not how modern the stack looks on a slide. When something breaks, you want to know why it was possible, not just how to patch it.</p><p>You enjoy growing engineers, and you understand that leading a small team means doing the work alongside them. Above all, you want to build something durable — a foundation that holds while the company scales on top of it.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/destinusgroup/data-platform-manager-zurich-111131","tags":["Aviation & Aerospace","Production & Manufacturing"],"job_types":["Full time"],"location":"Zürich, Switzerland","created_at":1794637207},{"slug":"business-operations-data-specialist-finance-zurich-175243","company_name":"Destinusgroup","title":"Business Operations & Data Specialist (Finance)","description":"<p><strong>About the role</strong></p><p>Every number that reaches our leadership team, our board, and our auditors has to be right the first time — and that is where you come in. As a Business Operations &amp; Data Specialist focused on Finance at Destinus, you are the bridge between the owners of our financial data, the CFO, and the wider finance team and the data in our lakehouse. You own how finance data is defined, where it comes from, how it is produced, and how it reaches the people who make decisions with it.</p><p>This is as much an operations role as a reporting one. You will translate what finance needs to know into what the data platform has to deliver, working with our Data Engineers on the finance data in the lakehouse and building the dashboards the CFO and the finance team rely on. You will also improve the processes and systems that create the numbers in the first place, automate the manual work that eats the month, and make our finance data understandable to everyone who needs it, including our AI assistants.</p><p>At Destinus, we are redefining the future of aerospace manufacturing — bringing speed, precision, and innovation to every process that powers our advanced Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs). We are a fast-growing international group operating across several European entities, and the standards we hold our financial data to are rising just as quickly. Join us in building a finance reporting foundation that is accurate, traceable, and ready for any question asked of it.</p><p><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><ul><li>Be the go-to contact between the business owners of finance data — the CFO, accounts payable and receivable, and treasury — and our lakehouse: turn their questions into clear data requirements, and the data back into answers they can act on.</li><li>Build and maintain Power BI dashboards covering cash flow, receipts and collections, payables, and spend across the group, built on certified lakehouse data.</li><li>Partner with our Data Engineers on the curated (gold) layer for finance: specify the tables, fields, and business rules — entities, currencies, financial dimensions, intercompany — and validate the result against the ledger before anyone relies on it.</li><li>Prepare and quality-check entity-level data extractions from our lakehouse and ERP in support of the external audit, and keep audit requests tracked from request to delivery.</li><li>Define and document finance KPI definitions in our KPI catalog — formulas, inclusions, exclusions, owners, and sources — to a standard that withstands external review.</li><li>Describe our finance data in plain business language — what each field means, who owns it, and how sensitive it is — for our shared meanings layer, so that colleagues and our AI assistants can use it correctly without having to ask you first.</li><li>Automate what is manual today: turn recurring spreadsheet work, audit packs, and month-end routines into repeatable processes that largely run themselves.</li><li>Improve the finance processes and system configuration that create the data, working with the finance team and our ERP specialists, so that issues are fixed at source rather than corrected every month.</li><li>Help the finance team get more from the tools through training and self-service, so they can answer their own questions.</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><strong>What You’ll Need</strong></p><ul><li>Bachelor's or Master's degree in Finance, Accounting, Controlling, Economics, or a related field.</li><li><strong>A genuine finance background is essential</strong> — experience in external or internal audit, controlling, financial reporting, or FP&amp;A. This is not a data role with finance on the side; you need to understand the accounting behind the figures.</li><li>Confident with general ledger and subledger structures, trial balances, accounts payable and accounts receivable, bank reconciliations, intercompany transactions, and the principles of IFRS.</li><li>Strong expertise in Power BI (data modeling, DAX, dashboard design, troubleshooting), complemented by advanced Excel skills.</li><li>Comfortable querying data with SQL and working in a lakehouse or data warehouse environment; experience with Microsoft Fabric or a medallion (bronze/silver/gold) architecture is a plus. You will not build the pipelines — you need to know what to ask for and how to check what comes back.</li><li>Able to explain data to finance colleagues and accounting logic to technical ones — and to get both sides to agree on one definition.</li><li><strong>Hands-on experience with Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance is a strong advantage</strong> — the general ledger, accounts payable and accounts receivable modules, and the data structures underneath them. We run on D365, and someone who already knows it will be effective months earlier. An interest in improving how the system is configured and used matters as much as knowing where to click.</li><li>A track record of simplifying or automating a process, not only reporting on it.</li><li>Experience supporting an external audit, or working in a multi-entity, multi-currency international group, is a strong advantage.</li><li>Fluent in English; additional European languages are a plus.</li><li>Experience in a start-up or scale-up environment is preferred.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><p>You are precise, and you are curious about where a number came from before you are comfortable reporting it — whether that means reading the ledger or querying the lakehouse. You know the difference between a figure that looks right and a figure that can be traced back to its source, and you care about the second one.</p><p>You are not content to rebuild the same report every month. When something is manual, repetitive, or fragile, your instinct is to go upstream and fix it rather than absorb it. You enjoy working with finance colleagues who ask hard questions, and you would rather be challenged on a detail than have it slip through.</p><p>Above all, you want your work to be relied on, by the CFO, by the board, and by anyone who audits it.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/destinusgroup/business-operations-data-specialist-finance-zurich-175243","tags":["Finance","Aviation & Aerospace"],"job_types":["Full time"],"location":"Zürich, Switzerland","created_at":1794637207},{"slug":"senior-lead-auditor-cisa-zurich-242859","company_name":"coni+partner AG","title":"Senior Lead Auditor CISA","description":"<p>coni + partner, established 1993, is a consultancy company with headquarters in Zurich and subsidiaries in Düsseldorf and Shanghai. We are specialised in custom-fit staffing in tune with the corporate culture by ensuring a perfect match of professional skills, references and personal as well as social skills of successful candidates.</p><p>Our client is the Asset Management division of an international Swiss bank in Zurich. We are looking for a German-speaking audit specialist (m, f, d) as a</p><p><strong>Senior Lead Auditor CISA</strong></p><p>Your Tasks: </p><p>Lead or support risk- and system-oriented audits of the bank's asset management and advise on risk management issues / Plan and perform audits and risk-based tests of controls and provide autonomous assessments of financial, business and control processes and related IT systems / Critical and objective audits for banking operations, trading and asset management, risk management and IT from an expert, balanced and risk-based perspective / Evaluate risks and assess the efficiency of processes and effectiveness of controls / Write audit reports and recommendations based on the findings / Provide best practice advice to line managers and oversee the implementation of recommendations / Build trust and good working relationships / Ongoing interaction with the Head of Internal Audit, presenting audit findings to the Audit Committee with developing insights / Contribute to annual planning for the Head of Internal Audit / Further develop audit programs or audit related topics and associated audit procedures / Participate in committees of the Bank.</p><p>Your Profile: </p><p>Bachelor or Master in Economics / CIA, CISA, Certified Public Accountant, also ‘Fraud Examiner’ / Experience as an internal and/or external auditor in a bank, asset manager or in auditing / Professional experience in 2nd or 3rd line of defense (business or/and IT) / Interest Data Analytics and with leading audits / Audit experience in complex organizations / Interest in working with minimum supervision and finding fit-for-purpose solutions / Strong analytical and conceptual skills / Knowledge of auditing standards, the principles of internal control processes and the evaluation of results / Knowl