&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Xebia&lt;/strong&gt; pushes the boundaries of what’s possible – and you’re right in the middle of it! We’re not just consultants, but visionaries: with more than 5,000 experts worldwide, we help our clients drive their digital transformation with passion and ambition. At Xebia, it’s about more than recommendations: with innovative solutions, we create a unique combination of technology, people and processes. Our goal is to make our clients digital frontrunners – ready to turn media usage data into insights that make a difference?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the project&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our client, a large Swiss media company, is building a new platform on Azure Databricks for the usage data of its apps and websites. It will replace the commercial analytics tool they use today. Analysts are starting to work on the new platform now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You join the platform team of five developers through Xebia. Most of your time goes into implementing Jira tickets. You build and run the pipelines that take event data from Azure Event Hubs through the bronze, silver and gold layers into the tables analysts and dashboards use. You keep the Databricks and Azure infrastructure in code with Pulumi and ship changes through GitHub Actions. The team creates and refines tickets together and reviews each other&#39;s code. You&#39;ll also help analysts get started with Databricks and GitHub.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the senior person in the team, you can advise on anything from implementation details to the overall architecture, while the product owner sets the priorities. Today the role also covers the data model, the infrastructure and the platform costs, and there is room to take on more responsibility over time. The team uses AI coding assistants such as Claude in its daily work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Several years of hands-on data engineering on Databricks: building and running production pipelines with Spark, PySpark or SQL and Delta Lake, in a medallion architecture&lt;br&gt;• Architecture experience on a Databricks or Azure data platform&lt;br&gt;• Streaming or event ingestion, ideally Azure Event Hubs or Kafka&lt;br&gt;• Data modelling for analytics and BI&lt;br&gt;• Infrastructure as code, ideally Pulumi (Terraform experience transfers)&lt;br&gt;• Git, GitHub workflows and CI/CD with GitHub Actions&lt;br&gt;• Experience in larger projects&lt;br&gt;• You work well in a team and get productive with little onboarding&lt;br&gt;• Comfortable using AI coding assistants&lt;br&gt;• Fluent English&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Unity Catalog, Databricks Asset Bundles, data quality frameworks&lt;br&gt;• Dashboards in Databricks or Power BI&lt;br&gt;• Azure experience beyond Databricks&lt;br&gt;• Web and app usage tracking or digital analytics, including tracking migrations&lt;br&gt;• Media or broadcasting experience&lt;br&gt;• German&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The current engineer can hand over until the end of January. English is the working language; German is a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What makes us special&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💡 &lt;strong&gt;Innovation potential:&lt;/strong&gt; At Xebia, the focus is on innovation and pioneering spirit. You can develop your creative ideas and share innovative thoughts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌱 &lt;strong&gt;Personal growth:&lt;/strong&gt; We believe in personal development for outstanding professional experiences. Unlock your potential and keep growing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🤝 &lt;strong&gt;Community and networking:&lt;/strong&gt; Xebia is a community of technology enthusiasts. Meet professionals from different fields, share knowledge and shape innovation together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚖️ &lt;strong&gt;Flexibility:&lt;/strong&gt; We value work-life balance. Adapt your working hours and find a balance between your career and your personal life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎉 &lt;strong&gt;Great social events:&lt;/strong&gt; Ski days, B2run, spontaneous after-work apéros, Christmas and summer parties – we celebrate together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re ready to take your professional journey further, we warmly welcome you to Xebia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We look forward to meeting you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/xebiadach/senior-data-architect-senior-data-engineer-azure-databricks-39403","tags":["Delivery"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1794628526},{"slug":"head-of-product-zurich-263883","company_name":"BLP Digital AG","title":"Head of Product","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join BLP and help make the world’s business processes autonomous! </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agentic platform helps finance and operations teams worldwide remove manual work from their core business processes, so work runs end-to-end with greater control and significant productivity gains. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, over 550 enterprise customers use BLP across 1,300+ deployed projects. In the processes we automate, customers achieve productivity improvements of 5 to 10 times. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, BLP remains majority employee-owned, with Goldman Sachs holding a minority stake as a growth investor. Our success is driven by deep expertise in technology and business processes, a superior product with strong product-market fit, reflected in an expanding customer base that includes Fortune 500 companies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP is one of Switzerland's fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups; we are now entering our next phase of growth. From our headquarters on Zürich's Bahnhofstrasse, we're expanding globally, with a growing presence across Europe and North America. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us and help make autonomous operations the new standard. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The opportunity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our engineering teams build a product that enterprises run their purchase-to-pay and order-to-cash processes on every day. Much of the product knowledge behind it sits with our founders and domain experts. As we grow, we are moving from a project-oriented model, where features come top-down and success is measured by output, to a product-oriented one: empowered teams that own problems end-to-end and are measured by their impact on customers and the business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Head of Product, you lead that shift. You build the product management practice for the BLP Platform from an early stage. Our first product managers are joining stream-aligned teams, starting with Invoice and Procurement, and the team will grow to 4–5 PMs as we expand. You hire them, coach them, and set the standard for what great product work looks like at BLP.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You report to the CTO and work closely with Engineering, Projects, Sales, and our founders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and lead the product management practice for the BLP Platform: hire, coach, and develop a team of product managers as we scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Move the product organization from an output-driven model to an outcome-driven one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish the product management craft at BLP: discovery practices, evidence-based decision making, and a clear standard for what “good” looks like in the role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Transfer product knowledge out of the experts’ heads and into the teams, without losing the domain depth that got us here.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the direct line between our teams and our customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make our data usable for product decisions. We have BigQuery, PostHog, and prediction-rate analytics available, and we want product managers who reach for them by default.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape how the product organization works as we grow: intake, prioritization, roadmapping, and the operating rhythm.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute directly to product strategy for the platform.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">10+ years in product management, including experience leading or formally coaching product managers, with a real point of view on how product people are developed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in an empowered product model, where teams were assigned problems to solve rather than features to build.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of shipping enterprise B2B software that customers actually adopted.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience moving an organization toward an empowered product model, including the political and cultural side of it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to hold a position with engineers, sales, and executives, and to say no in a way that keeps the relationship.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entrepreneurial judgment: comfortable operating with incomplete information, choosing a direction, and owning the result.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enterprise ERP or finance exposure, experience with AI or agentic products in production (particularly reliability, evaluation, and trust in enterprise settings), and German are a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why BLP</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a function: you shape how product management works at BLP while the team grows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct work with the CTO and founders on product strategy for the platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A product with deep domain substance and a large enterprise customer base to learn from.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee participation plan.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we work</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact:</strong> We create measurable business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transparency:</strong> We build trust through openness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership:</strong> We take responsibility for outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellence:</strong> We relentlessly strive for greatness.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Practical information</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Location: hybrid from our Zurich, London, Munich or Cologne offices, or remote elsewhere in Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employment: full-time, permanent.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/blp-digital-ag/head-of-product-zurich-263883","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1794627628},{"slug":"senior-product-manager-zurich-374197","company_name":"BLP Digital AG","title":"Senior Product Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join BLP and help make the world’s business processes autonomous! </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agentic platform helps finance and operations teams worldwide remove manual work from their core business processes, so work runs end-to-end with greater control and significant productivity gains. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, over 550 enterprise customers use BLP across 1,300+ deployed projects. In the processes we automate, customers achieve productivity improvements of 5 to 10 times. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, BLP remains majority employee-owned, with Goldman Sachs holding a minority stake as a growth investor. Our success is driven by deep expertise in technology and business processes, a superior product with strong product-market fit, reflected in an expanding customer base that includes Fortune 500 companies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP is one of Switzerland's fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups; we are now entering our next phase of growth. From our headquarters on Zürich's Bahnhofstrasse, we're expanding globally, with a growing presence across Europe and North America. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us and help make autonomous operations the new standard. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you own</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The product decisions for your team's area of the blp platform: what gets built, in what order, and why.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The outcomes your team is accountable for, not the output.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discovery: understanding the users and customers in your area deeply enough that you can make most decisions yourself, and knowing which decisions need evidence first.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you shape with us</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The product strategy for your area, in partnership with product leadership and the domain experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">How the product organization works as it scales: intake, prioritization, and the operating rhythm. We are actively iterating these, and we want the people doing the work to shape them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The standard for product management at blp, which is still being set.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who you work with</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your stream-aligned team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Other SATs and the platform teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customers and key users directly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founders and domain experts, who hold a lot of the accumulated product knowledge in this space.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>What you'll bring</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of shipping enterprise B2B software that customers actually adopted.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entrepreneurial judgment. Comfortable operating with incomplete information, choosing a direction, and owning the result.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experienced in product discovery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Can hold a position with engineers, with sales, and with executives, and can say no in a way that keeps the relationship.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strongly preferred</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in an empowered product model, where teams were assigned problems to solve rather than features to build.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A plus</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enterprise ERP or finance exposure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with AI or agentic products in production, particularly reliability, evaluation, and trust in enterprise settings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">German, given our customer base.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>What you'll get</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real ownership.</strong> What gets built in your area is yours, from strategy through outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A product org still taking shape.</strong> Real room to shape how it works, not just execute within it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Direct access.</strong> To founders, domain experts, and the customers you're building for.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>An empowered model.</strong> A seat in it, working with strong engineering and design partners.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn more about blp and our values at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://blp.digital/company/careers">blp.digital/company/careers</a>.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/blp-digital-ag/senior-product-manager-zurich-374197","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1794627628},{"slug":"key-account-manager-german-speaking-territory-zurich-104815","company_name":"Justone Gr","title":"Key Account Manager (German Speaking Territory)","description":"<p>On behalf of our client, an international pharmaceutical company specializing in oncology, we are looking for an experienced and results-driven <strong>Key Account Manager</strong> to develop its business across German-speaking Switzerland.</p><p>We welcome candidates with a strong background in <strong>Oncology, Hematology, Immunology or other specialized therapeutic areas</strong>, particularly those with proven experience engaging directly with hospitals, private clinics and specialist physicians.</p><p>This is a field-based position (over 80% of time in the field), combining strategic account management, scientific engagement and commercial business development.</p><p></p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><ul><li>Develop and execute territory sales strategies to achieve business objectives.</li><li>Build and maintain strong relationships with specialist physicians, oncologists, KOLs, hospital pharmacists and healthcare stakeholders.</li><li>Identify business opportunities and expand the company's presence within hospitals and private clinics.</li><li>Conduct high-quality scientific and product discussions with healthcare professionals.</li><li>Monitor market trends, competitor activities and customer needs.</li><li>Collaborate closely with Medical, Marketing and Market Access teams.</li><li>Organize and participate in scientific meetings, educational events and congresses.</li><li>Maintain accurate CRM reporting and ensure compliance with pharmaceutical regulations and pharmacovigilance requirements.</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>University degree in Life Sciences, Business or a related field.</li><li><strong>Minimum 5 years of experience</strong> in pharmaceutical or biotech sales, preferably in Oncology, Hematology, Immunology or other specialty care areas.</li><li><strong>Proven experience working directly with hospitals, private clinics, specialist physicians and healthcare decision-makers.</strong></li><li>Strong understanding of the Swiss healthcare system and hospital environment.</li><li><strong>Fluent German (mandatory)</strong> and strong professional English; French is an advantage.</li><li>Excellent commercial, negotiation and relationship-building skills.</li><li>Autonomous, proactive, results-oriented and well-organized.</li><li>Proficiency in CRM tools and MS Office.</li><li>Valid Swiss driving licence (Category B).</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Annual Base Gross Salary: €110K/yr - €130K/yr </strong></li><li>Bonus </li><li>Private Health Insurance</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/justone-gr/key-account-manager-german-speaking-territory-zurich-104815","tags":["Sales","Pharmaceuticals"],"job_types":["Full time","mid-senior"],"location":"Zürich, Switzerland","created_at":1794626403},{"slug":"senior-program-manager-el2-european-tour-olten-339868","company_name":"Electraaero","title":"Senior Program Manager, EL2 European Tour","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Electra&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Air travel is about to become something more: more direct, more accessible, and more connected to the places where people live, work and want to be. Every day in the U.S., people make 35 million trips of 50–500 miles, stuck in traffic or routed through crowded hubs. Chances are, you&#39;ve been one of them. At Electra, we&#39;re changing that with the EL9, a nine-passenger, hybrid-electric aircraft that takes off and lands in just 150 feet. Our Ultra Short technology opens up thousands of new places to fly, beyond conventional runways, congested airports and long drives. We&#39;re backed by Lockheed Martin, Honeywell and Safran. Operators worldwide have signed intent-to-purchase agreements for the first 2,200 aircraft we produce, and we&#39;re moving toward first test flights in 2027.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Getting a new kind of aircraft airborne takes more than ambition. It takes our kind of bold: people who think big while working in the real world. Who move ideas into action and collaborate without silos. Who put people first and make room at the table for everyone. Who challenge one another without diminishing one another.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Sound like you? Then look beyond what you thought were your own limits, and help us take flight beyond runways.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Electra seeks an experienced Program Manager to lead the planning and execution of a European tour for Electra&#39;s EL2 technology demonstrator aircraft. This role will serve as the primary team lead for the EL2 program, partnering closely with engineering, flight test, government and commercial stakeholders, and company leadership to ensure the tour achieves its strategic objectives safely, on schedule, and within budget. &lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;After the completion of the European tour this role will transition to supporting EL9. &amp;nbsp;The exact nature of this support will depend on the candidates specific skills and interest areas; likely options include test team program management, program office support, or leading teams executing government contract&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Tour Planning and Strategy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Develop a master schedule, budget, and resourcing plan for the tour, including aircraft transport/ferry logistics, ground support, and personnel deployment to meet the overall mission objectives and success critera.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Coordinate with Sales, Business Development, and Government Affairs to prioritization of target locations, stakeholders, and events (e.g., customer demonstrations, government engagements, airshows) across the tour itinerary.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Cross-Functional Coordination&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Partner with Flight Test and Engineering teams to ensure the aircraft, crew, and support equipment are mission-ready for each tour stop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Coordinate with Legal, Regulatory, and International Trade/Export Control functions to secure necessary permissions, airspace access, and customs clearances for international operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Serve as the central point of coordination between internal teams and external partners, hosts, and government counterparts at each location&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Manage vendor and logistics partners supporting ground operations, transport, and lodging&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Risk Management and Execution&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Identify, track, and mitigate risks related to schedule, safety, logistics, weather, and geopolitical factors across tour locations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Develop contingency plans for schedule disruptions, maintenance needs, or changes in stop-level objectives&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Monitor tour execution in real time and adjust plans as needed to maintain safety and achieve strategic goals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Maintain clear documentation and traceability of decisions, approvals, and changes throughout the tour&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Reporting and Communication&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
