&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stand-out experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built or led teams on infrastructure-as-code or deployment platforms, e.g. Terraform, Pulumi, AWS CDK / CloudFormation, Kubernetes controllers, Argo CD / Flux / Helm, or Vercel / Netlify-style deploy platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managed an open-source developer tool with an active community and a frequent release cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shipped developer workflows for AI coding agents (CLI-first tooling, agent skills, MCP), or AI-assisted authoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have managed managers or multiple teams (~15 to 20+ engineers), owned a multi-year platform strategy, and grown tech leads and managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/databricks/sr-engineering-manager-developer-ecosystem-amsterdam-300494","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794639323},{"slug":"engineering-manager-developer-ecosystem-amsterdam-107355","company_name":"databricks","title":"Engineering Manager - Developer Ecosystem","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;RDQ427R369&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Databricks, we are passionate about enabling data teams to solve the world&#39;s toughest problems — from making the next mode of transportation a reality to accelerating the development of medical breakthroughs. We do this by building and running the world&#39;s best data and AI infrastructure platform so our customers can use deep data insights to improve their business.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Developer Ecosystem organisation shapes how developers and the AI agents working for them build on the Databricks Data and AI Platform, from within the product to the tools they already use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring an Engineering Manager to lead our declarative deployment framework, which turns data and AI projects into versioned, reviewable, repeatable software. It is one product with two entry points. Third-party developers use our open-source CLI from their IDEs, terminals, and CI/CD systems. First-party, they author, deploy and inspect the same projects inside the Databricks workspace. In both, AI agents increasingly do the work: coding agents drive the CLI, and our in-product AI assistant authors and deploys projects alongside the developer. Thousands of organisations run their CI/CD on it, and it is one of the fastest-growing parts of the platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team owns the deployment engine and CLI, the in-workspace authoring and deployment experience, and the metadata service and deployment history that record every deployment. The hard problems are real infrastructure-as-code problems: reconciling declared and live state, making plans safe for humans and agents to approve, keeping visual authoring and code in sync, and shipping weekly releases that remain backwards-compatible for our largest customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The impact you will have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and grow the team:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage a team of senior engineers across three closely connected areas (the deployment engine and open-source CLI, the in-workspace authoring and deployment experience, and deployment history and metadata), working with strong tech leads. Hire, coach and promote, and grow engineers into tech leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make agentic development the default path:&lt;/strong&gt; Shape how developers and AI agents author, validate and deploy projects, both inside the workspace and from the developer&#39;s own coding agent. Design the tools, skills and guardrails so agents get the same safety and auditability as humans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the strategy and roadmap:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Product and Design to set a multi-quarter roadmap for declarative deployment: agentic development, governed deployments and deployment history, enterprise CI/CD, and new resource coverage. Make the trade-offs explicit when the demand is larger than the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the bar on execution and operational excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Run a predictable delivery process for a fast-moving, open-source product with frequent releases. Own reliability, on-call health, incident response and the quality bar for a tool customers depend on to ship to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Treat backward compatibility as a product feature:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead engine and configuration migrations without forcing customers through a flag day, and communicate change clearly to customers, the community and field teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead across the platform:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive alignment with the many platform teams whose resources and services the framework deploys, and with our sibling teams in Developer Ecosystem (SDKs, CLI, IaC provider, IDE). Make the whole toolchain feel like one product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years managing software engineering teams, and 8+ years of software engineering experience overall.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building and shipping developer tools or platforms used by many external developers or internal teams, such as infrastructure-as-code, deployment or CI/CD systems, CLIs, SDKs, or internal developer platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding of declarative systems and deployment workflows: plan/apply, state management, drift and reconciliation, environment promotion, GitOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enough technical depth to engage on architecture and trade-offs with senior and staff engineers, and to hold a high-quality bar for public, versioned interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading teams through ambiguity, with competing priorities from customers, partners and platform dependencies, and making clear calls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and a customer-first mindset. You enjoy talking to developers, reading their issues, and turning feedback into roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, including with executives, partner teams and an external developer community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stand-out experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built or led teams on infrastructure-as-code or deployment platforms, e.g. Terraform, Pulumi, AWS CDK / CloudFormation, Kubernetes controllers, Argo CD / Flux / Helm, or Vercel / Netlify-style deploy platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managed an open-source developer tool with an active community and a frequent release cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shipped developer workflows for AI coding agents (CLI-first tooling, agent skills, MCP), or AI-assisted authoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/databricks/engineering-manager-developer-ecosystem-amsterdam-107355","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794639322},{"slug":"growth-director-42106","company_name":"dept","title":"Growth Director","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth Director&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Amsterdam/Rotterdam, hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;DEPT® is a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, our 4,000+ specialists deliver growth invention services across Brand &amp;amp; Media, Experience, Commerce, CRM, and Technology &amp;amp; Data. We’re 50|50 tech and marketing, partner-led, and first to move. Clients include Google, Lufthansa, Meta, eBay, and OpenAI. We have been certified B Corp and Climate Neutral since 2021.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JOB PURPOSE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is part of our&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; Experience &amp;amp; Engineering&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; team based in the Netherlands. We combine our skills in developing future-ready technical solutions with our expertise in creating beautiful designs to deliver exceptional and engaging digital experiences that build lasting relationships with our clients like Gant, Inter Milan, bol.com and Just Eat Takeaway.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Growth Director who is hungry to build something. In this role, you will identify and develop new business opportunities for our Netherlands team, helping ambitious brands solve complex digital challenges through the combined power of technology, design, and strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you thrive on finding the right clients, crafting compelling pitches, and seeing your work turn into lasting partnerships, this role is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Engagement &amp;amp; Relationship Building&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and nurture relationships with marketing and technology decision-makers at prospect organisations, translating their challenges into clear, compelling solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent DEPT® with confidence in client conversations, demonstrating knowledge across digital experience, engineering, and emerging technologies like AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales &amp;amp; Pipeline Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and qualify new business opportunities through direct outreach, events, partnerships, and collaboration with the marketing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage your own pipeline end-to-end, from first contact to signed proposal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use CRM tools (e.g., Salesforce) to track activity, report on progress, and develop good habits around forecasting and pipeline hygiene.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; Pitching&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with delivery leads, solution architects, and strategists to build proposals and pitches that showcase DEPT®&#39;s strengths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop familiarity with our key technology partners (e.g., Shopify, Adobe, Optimizely) and understand how those partnerships create opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in business development, consultative sales, or a client-facing role with a strong commercial component, within a digital agency, tech consultancy, or related environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling project-based work, with exposure to digital experience, content management and publishing, ecommerce, or technology services. Familiarity with solutions like CMS, PIM, DAM, or content supply chain is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable engaging with senior stakeholders at manager and director level, with the ambition to grow into C-level conversations over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A structured approach to prospecting and pipeline management, you know how to keep deals moving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator who can explain complex ideas in straightforward, client-friendly language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative by nature, you enjoy working across teams and bringing people together around a pitch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in Dutch and English language&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to digital experience platforms, ecommerce solutions, or cloud/technology services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with multi-stakeholder sales cycles and how to navigate them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in how AI and emerging technology are reshaping digital services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WE OFFER:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A flexible, hybrid working policy (2-3 days from the office, depending on location) and the opportunity to work from abroad for 13 weeks a year.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;24 vacation days per year and the possibility to buy an unlimited number of extra vacation days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DEPT®/YOU Learning Menu and DEPT®/YOU Special Programs. Develop your skills with courses and programs tailored to your needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay happy and healthy with a contribution to your health through the OpenUp platform, gym and wellness discounts, and healthy lunches at the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get a discount on your lease bike and ride in style. You can also enjoy hassle free-commutes with an NS Business Card.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A reputation for doing good. DEPT® has been a Certified B Corp® since 2021, has been named a &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.greatplacetowork.nl/en/certification/certified/dept&quot;&gt;Great Place To Work since 2022&lt;/a&gt; in the Netherlands and named ‘Agency of the Year’ at both The Lovies and The Webby Awards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awesome clients. Whether big, small, local or global — at DEPT® you’ll get the opportunity to work with all of them. And we celebrate all of our successes together!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can discover even more employee benefits &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/nl-nl/employee-benefits/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHY DEPT®?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, we create what is next by pioneering ideas, acting fast, and moving further because standing still just is not in our DNA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are drawn to people who stay curious, move with intent, and never stop inventing. Our culture runs on three values: better together, relentlessly curious, and get sh*t done. It is how we work, how we grow, and how we make things that matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DEPT®, you will find the freedom to explore, the space to collaborate, and the trust to make a real impact for our clients, for each other, and for the world we are helping to build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DIVERSITY, EQUITY &amp;amp; INCLUSION&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DEPT®, we take pride in creating an inclusive workplace where everyone has an equal opportunity to thrive. We actively seek to recruit, develop, nurture, and retain talented individuals from diverse backgrounds, with varying skills and perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not sure you meet all qualifications? Apply, and let us decide! Research shows that women and members of underrepresented groups tend not to apply for jobs when they think they may not meet every requirement, when in fact they do. We believe in giving everyone a fair chance to shine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also encourage you to reach out to us and discuss any reasonable adjustments we can make to support you throughout the recruitment process and your time with us.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Want to know more about our dedication to diversity, equity, and inclusion? Check out our efforts &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/the-good-company/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/dept/growth-director-42106","tags":["Commercial - Business Development"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1794639320},{"slug":"senior-security-operations-engineer-198564","company_name":"Samsara","title":"Senior Security Operations Engineer","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Samsara (NYSE: IOT) is the pioneer of the Connected Operations™ Cloud, which is a platform that enables organizations that depend on physical operations to harness Internet of Things (IoT) data to develop actionable insights and improve their operations. At Samsara, we are helping improve the safety, efficiency and sustainability of the physical operations that power our global economy. Representing more than 40% of global GDP, these industries are the infrastructure of our planet, including agriculture, construction, field services, transportation, and manufacturing — and we are excited to help digitally transform their operations at scale.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Working at Samsara means you’ll help define the future of physical operations and be on a team that’s shaping an exciting array of product solutions, including Video-Based Safety, Vehicle Telematics, Apps and Driver Workflows, and Equipment Monitoring. As part of a recently public company, you’ll have the autonomy and support to make an impact as we build for the long term.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of our Security Operations Team, you will collaborate with a global team of engineers to monitor and respond to security events, lead security incidents as Incident Commander, and lead digital forensic investigations in support of Employee Relations, Legal, Compliance, or Information Security cases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Although you will be focused on security incident response, you will also have the opportunity to create and maintain runbooks, and automated workflows, and assist in process refinement and implementation. You will collaborate with a diverse team of engineers, and key stakeholders on security initiatives across the company. Above all, your focus is bringing Security expertise to the table in a collaborative, humble, and practical manner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; This role is open to candidates residing in Netherlands&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You should apply if:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You want to impact the industries that run our world:&lt;/strong&gt; Every phone call you answer and every email you send can affect whether truck drivers deliver goods on time and without accidents, whether students get dropped off safely from school, or whether power gets restored quickly after a natural disaster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You thrive the most when solving problems:&lt;/strong&gt; Our constantly expanding technology and the complexities faced by our customers provide an exciting range of challenges for our Customer Success teams. With a growth mindset and a desire to learn, you will strategically partner with our customers to find unique solutions to help keep their operations safe, efficient, and sustainable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are a natural relationship builder:&lt;/strong&gt; Whether the relationship is with our customers or with cross-functional teams in Samsara, you are in constant communication and collaboration with key stakeholders to win as a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are the architect of your own career:&lt;/strong&gt; If you put in the work, this role won’t be your last at Samsara. This Customer Success team is still shaping its future and you will have plenty of autonomy and opportunities to master your craft in a hyper growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You want to be with the best: &lt;/strong&gt;At Samsara, we win together, celebrate together and support each other. You will be surrounded by the best and brightest professionals out there.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor security events and provide technical analysis on alerts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead information security incidents and employee insider investigations by developing the incident response strategy, lead the execution through incident closure, while providing incident updates to key stakeholders throughout the incident&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver security guidance clearly and concisely for incident response and insider threat initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate the building of services, capabilities, integrations, and implementations of technologies to support security operations, incident response, and insider threat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion, role model, and embed Samsara’s cultural principles (Focus on Customer Success, Build for the Long Term, Adopt a Growth Mindset, Be Inclusive, Win as a Team) as we scale globally and across new offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in our on-call rota covering weekends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements for the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in Security Incident Response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate investigative findings and strategies to technical staff, executive leadership, and legal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build scripts or tools to support Samsara’s investigation processes, with proficiency in Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and train security operation engineers on data collection, analysis, and reporting technical analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience acting as a lead during security incident response, including monitoring and triaging alerts, and coordinating across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of analysis and forensics techniques on macOS, Windows, and Linux&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience utilizing SIEM tools to perform log reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in cloud architecture and security (AWS, GCP) and cloud-based services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participation in an on-call rotation, with the potential to work outside standard business hours, including late evenings, when responding to high-severity incidents as part of our global incident response team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role will be part of our EMEA so your hours will be aligned to the UK. As an operational time you may be expected to work flexible hours around this to support the load of the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An ideal candidate also has:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience working on insider threat initiatives or employee investigations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Information Security, or a related field - or relevant industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GIAC Certified Incident Handler (GCIH) or similar Certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with common security frameworks and standards, including NIST Cybersecurity Framework, ISO 27001, FedRAMP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Total Rewards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Samsara, we build for the people who keep the global economy moving. We want owners, not passengers, which is why &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.samsara.com/company/careers/benefits&quot;&gt;our rewards&lt;/a&gt; are designed to fuel high-impact builders. Our compensation program delivers above-market total compensation through a combination of base salary, performance-based bonus/variable pay, and equity (for eligible roles) in a high-growth public company. We meaningfully differentiate pay for our top performers, who have the opportunity to earn above-market compensation that can outpace the broader market over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond compensation, we provide the foundations that enable long-term success: a flexible, employee-led remote model, a professional development stipend, comprehensive health and parental leave plans, and more. If you’re ready to build for the long term and own the outcome, your journey starts here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible Working&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Samsara, we embrace a flexible working model that caters to the diverse needs of our teams. Our offices are open for those who prefer to work in-person and we also support remote work where it aligns with our operational requirements. For certain positions, being close to one of our offices or within a specific geographic area is important to facilitate collaboration, access to resources, or alignment with our service regions. In these cases, the job description will clearly indicate any working location requirements. Our goal is to ensure that all members of our team can contribute effectively, whether they are working on-site, in a hybrid model, or fully remotely. All offers of employment are contingent upon an individual’s ability to secure and maintain the legal right to work at the company and in the specified work location, if applicable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Belonging at Samsara&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Samsara, we welcome everyone regardless of their background. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, protected veteran status, disability, age, and other characteristics protected by law. We depend on the unique approaches of our team members to help us solve complex problems and want to ensure that Samsara is a place where people from all backgrounds can make an impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Samsara is an inclusive work environment, and we are committed to ensuring equal opportunity in employment for qualified persons with disabilities. Please email &lt;a ---------- or &lt;a href=&quot;https://forms.gle/DrM6DFQUiSgfPtCVA&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; if you require any reasonable accommodations throughout the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Authenticity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use &lt;a href=&quot;https://hiretofu.com/privacyPolicy&quot;&gt;Tofu&lt;/a&gt;, a fraud detection tool, to validate the authenticity of applications and protect against identity fraud. This ensures we are connecting with real people and allows us to prioritize genuine candidates. Please see Samsara’s &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.samsara.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fraudulent Employment Offers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Samsara is aware of scams involving fake job interviews and offers. Please know we do not charge fees to applicants at any stage of the hiring process. Official communication about your application will only come from emails ending in ----- ----- or ----- For more information regarding fraudulent employment offers, please visit our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://samsara.com/blog/avoiding-fake-job-offers&quot;&gt;blog post here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/samsara/senior-security-operations-engineer-198564","tags":["IT Security"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1794639318},{"slug":"order-delivery-coordinator-c-uas-the-hague-375383","company_name":"Robin Radar","title":"Order & Delivery Coordinator (C-UAS)","description":"<h2><strong>Your next mission</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Anchor our system deliveries. Connect internal teams seamlessly – so our life-saving radars reach the front lines without delay.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our Order &amp; Delivery Coordinator (C-UAS), you run the administrative engine behind dispatching our IRIS radar systems. You take charge of order flows in Odoo ERP, align documentation, and organise clean internal handovers from Operations to dispatch readiness. Working alongside Project Management, Customer Success, and Operations, you keep our internal gears turning smoothly. Your sharp attention to detail ensures our teams stay focused and our radars deploy on schedule.</p><h2><strong>What you'll do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Order processing and data integrity</strong>: Process incoming sales orders in Odoo ERP across the entire lifecycle. Verify system data, hardware configurations, and commercial terms with high accuracy. Maintain order statuses, serial numbers, and delivery confirmations daily.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compliance and export documentation</strong>: Compile and verify complete delivery documentation packages before dispatch. Review export control paperwork, QA certificates, shipping manifests, and packing lists. Ensure every system leaves our premises with watertight paperwork.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Logistics coordination and internal handovers</strong>: Coordinate handovers with the Warehouse and Logistics crew with complete shipping files. Monitor dispatch statuses once Operations releases each radar system. Keep internal handovers structured, clean, and ready for physical freight execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-functional status tracking</strong>: Supply real-time ERP delivery status updates to Project Management and Customer Success. Share accurate tracking data and handover packages across departments. Monitor administrative workflows proactively to eliminate handover bottlenecks and protect dispatch targets.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What you bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vocational degree (MBO Level 4 / Associate degree) or equivalent practical experience in administration, supply chain, or logistics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of experience in administrative support, order processing, or logistics coordination, preferably within a high-tech manufacturing or hardware environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience working with ERP systems and databases (experience with Odoo is a strong advantage)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience handling compliance or logistics paperwork, such as shipping manifests, export control documentation, or QA certificates</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong command of English (both written and spoken) and working proficiency in Dutch is considered a strong asset</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High attention to detail with a methodical approach to data accuracy and documentation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organisational and coordination skills to handle multiple handovers efficiently</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborative, supportive mindset suited for cross-functional internal operations</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working for a Great Place to Work® certified company;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive pension plan;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commuting allowance;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30 days of paid holiday leave (with the possibility to buy 3 additional days);</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Opportunities to develop your skills even further through training and certifications;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High quality laptop/desktop, monitor, headphones, and any other equipment necessary for your role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An international team of 30+ nationalities, full of high performance colleagues you can exchange experiences with and learn from. As well as having a lot of fun in our social events and Friday drinks!</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Robin Radar is a defence technology leader in detecting, tracking and classifying drones and other small airborne objects. Our radars and software protect military sites, borders and critical infrastructure from drone threats, and also help prevent bird strikes in aviation and reduce the impact of wind farms on wildlife. Our work shows up at defence and security sites, airports and wind farms around the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're one of the top 10 fastest-growing companies in the Netherlands, with a crew of bright minds across 30+ nationalities. Growth doesn't mean we lose the plot – eyes on the skies, feet on the ground. Our values keep us grounded: WE TRUST. WE OWN IT. WE AIM HIGH.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Want to work on next-level radar tech, solve real problems, and never have to pretend your job has meaning?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You'll fit right in – we're saving you a seat.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/robin-radar/order-delivery-coordinator-c-uas-the-hague-375383","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Delft","created_at":1794638435},{"slug":"senior-data-analytics-engineer-amsterdam-214056","company_name":"Polarsteps","title":"Senior Data & Analytics Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Looking for a new adventure? You’ve come to the right place.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're an Amsterdam-based team of 100 (and counting) with 25+ nationalities amongst us! A varied bunch of “Citizens of The World” with a wide range of skills and hundreds of thousands of kilometers under our travel belts. And we have something important in common (other than our very well-worn passports): <strong>We want to change the way people travel.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And that's exactly what we're doing, with the travel app to plan, track, and relive trips in a smart and beautiful way.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Polarsteps has over 23 million users already, but, for us, this is just the beginning. We have big plans for the future, and so we need even more talented and enthusiastic people to help us on our journey.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Want to know more about us? <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="framer-text framer-styles-preset-15qact6" href="https://careers.polarsteps.com/">Here</a> you go.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Your expedition at Polarsteps - Senior Data &amp; Analytics Engineer</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Over the past 10+ years, Polarsteps has grown massively through word-of-mouth, thanks to our product and tech department building a top-quality user experience for all our travelers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our first Senior Data &amp; Analytics Engineer, you'll own the foundation that every data-driven decision at Polarsteps is built on. Product &amp; growth teams run experiments and analyse the data every week, leadership need clear reports for investors, and all of that depends on data that is reliable, modelled and compliant. You'll set the direction for our data platform, bring structure to data governance, and own the data infra that helps our product managers, marketers and data scientists do their job even better. You'll work closely with the Head of Engineering on infrastructure and architecture, and with the Head of Growth and product teams on what the business needs from data.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With 20M+ users and ratings of 4.8 and 4.7 on the app stores and features in multiple Google and Apple showcases, we've got an impressive past. But we're even more excited for the future, and you'll play a crucial role in building the data foundation that gets Polarsteps to 100M+ travelers around the globe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Your itinerary</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>What your journey at Polarsteps will look like day-to-day.</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the data platform roadmap: set the strategy for our data infrastructure and warehouse, make the build-vs-buy and tooling calls, and oversee execution together with DevOps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, build and maintain scalable ingestion pipelines for both internal (product events, back-end data) and external sources (ad platforms, attribution, app store data).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain a clean, documented modeling layer (e.g. dbt) that serves as the single source of truth for analysts, data scientists and self-serving PMs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead data governance: define and enforce event naming and tracking standards, a schema change process, documentation, and dashboard ownership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embed privacy in the data stack: make sure personal data is categorized, minimized and pseudonymized before it reaches downstream and third-party tools, in close collaboration with Legal</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the health of the stack: monitoring, alerting, data quality checks and cost management, so issues are caught before they reach stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define who owns what across our data tooling (e.g. Mixpanel, our warehouse and BI layer), and help teams get the most out of self-serve analytics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enable data enrichment to unlock deeper insights for Product and Growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Explore how we can safely use LLMs (such as Claude) on top of our data for analysis and reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the go-to data partner for Product, Engineering and Growth, and help grow the data function as Polarsteps scales.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>The equipment in your backpack</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>What we're hoping you'll bring with you.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ 5+ years of experience in data engineering, analytics engineering or a hybrid data role, ideally in a B2C product or mobile app company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ Strong SQL and Python, and hands-on experience modeling large event datasets in a modern warehouse (e.g. ClickHouse, Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ Experience with dbt and an orchestration tool such as Airflow or Dagster.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ Proven track record of bringing structure to data governance: tracking plans, event ownership, documentation and data quality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ Experience with product analytics tools (e.g. Mixpanel, Amplitude) and BI tools (e.g. Metabase, Looker).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ Comfortable owning infrastructure decisions: cloud (AWS/GCP/Azure), infrastructure-as-code (e.g. Terraform), CI/CD for data.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ A pragmatic, ownership-driven mindset: you're happy to set the strategy and get your hands dirty, and you enjoy the hygiene work others tend to avoid.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ Excellent communication skills: you can explain trade-offs to engineers and to non-technical stakeholders alike.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong> Bonus points if you have:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>✨ </strong>Experience with mobile attribution or marketing data (e.g. AppsFlyer, SKAdNetwork, ad platform APIs).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>✨ </strong>Experience with reverse ETL or CDPs (e.g. RudderStack, Twilio Segment).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>✨ </strong>Experience with experimentation data and A/B testing infrastructure.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>✨ </strong>Knowledge of GDPR and handling personal data responsibly in an analytics stack.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>1st class Polarsteps extras</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Some cool things to make the journey extra sweet.</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A yearly free flight or train ride to a random location! Give our Teleporter a spin <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.polarsteps.com/teleporter">here.</a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A shiny MacBook to work your magic on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid working, our way. Work from home <em>and</em> the office, we ask everyone to be in the office 2 days a week. It’s how we stay flexible, focused, and meaningfully connected in person.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An extensive home office set-up, everything from noise-canceling headphones to a standing desk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30 days of vacation <em>(for adventures or sitting on the couch, it's up to you).</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Two paid Culture Days for days that are important to you but not recognized by the official Dutch calendar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The option to switch up your zoom background by working from another country for up to 8 weeks a year.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A personal development budget for that curious mind of yours!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A pension plan to help you save for those around-the-world retirement trips.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Delicious daily team lunches.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Awesome monthly parties, as well as team trips away.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A lively office in downtown Amsterdam, with travel costs reimbursed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free Polarsteps Travel Books to contain all your far-flung adventures.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Polarsteps, we believe the best products are built by people as diverse as the travelers using our apps! That's why we specifically encourage people underrepresented in the tech industry to apply for a role with us. Because we believe that diversity, be it age, race, sexual orientation, physical ability, ethnicity, or gender identity, makes both the world and the workplace better.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/polarsteps/senior-data-analytics-engineer-amsterdam-214056","tags":["Growth & Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794638435},{"slug":"av-industry-expert-german-speaking-utrecht-280261","company_name":"Rentman","title":"AV Industry Expert (German-speaking)","description":"<h1><strong>About us</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rentman is a B2B SaaS scale-up building a smart, powerful operations management platform to support event and media production teams. Our users plan everything from small shoots to massive festivals in 70+ countries, and they all rely on Rentman to keep their gear, people, and timing perfectly in sync. We’re based in Utrecht (NL) with a second office in Toronto (CA), and our 100+ team members work in a culture that’s open, flat, and inclusive, where curiosity drives us, ownership matters, and everyone has the freedom to challenge ideas and make an impact. Check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://rentman.io/public-roadmap">public roadmap</a> to see what’s coming next!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/user-content/d722c125-c3d1-4d3f-8dbf-08d8ac4ab137/1abd1b97-44fa-4e7c-92e0-d04d95cf059f/Screenshot_2026-07-22_at_17.03.37.png" /></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Mission of this role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Netherlands is Rentman's biggest customer base, and DACH is our second-biggest. As an Implementation Specialist (German-speaking) on our Professional Services team, you make sure our German-speaking customers get the same excellent, hands-on support as everyone else.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are the solution expert who helps customers realize the full value of Rentman. You deliver paid trainings to existing customers that accelerate onboarding, boost account health and broaden usage across teams. Everything comes from our standardized service catalogue: the offering is standard, the application is tailored to each customer. These services come on top of what every Rentman customer already gets free of charge: support, the support center and for some a dedicated CSM.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">When you're not delivering customer trainings, you help the wider team stay useful year-round: you build standardized video trainings based on the most common questions coming out of our support center, and you're available to represent Rentman at customer events or trade shows in German-speaking markets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you'll do</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integrate Rentman knowledge with customer-centricity and commercial acumen to provide tailored training, in both German and English, that enhances customer usage, satisfaction, and professional services revenue.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver at least 60% of your time as direct, standardized-but-tailored training to customers, one-on-one or in groups.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">When you're not training customers, build standardized video trainings/webinars addressing the most common issues raised through our support center.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent Rentman at customer-facing events or trade shows in German-speaking markets when needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Always look for opportunities to expand and optimize our professional services and serve more customers in a standardized way.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain top-level knowledge of Rentman's functionality and industry challenges to advise customers effectively, and keep this knowledge current.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excel in administration and process efficiency to ensure internal processes (availability, booking, invoicing) run smoothly, and the customer journey is frictionless.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Adopt a customer-friendly attitude and deliver high-quality training to ensure an optimal customer experience.</p></li></ul><div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/user-content/d722c125-c3d1-4d3f-8dbf-08d8ac4ab137/3c95dc18-9519-4446-b1af-13a805537681/Screenshot_2026-07-23_at_10.38.46.png" /></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What we are looking for </strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Native or very fluent in German, and fluent in English. You're equally comfortable running a training in either language.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've worked inside the AV, production company, or event rental industry and know its workflows from the inside. This is what lets you speak credibly to customers about how they run their business, not just how the software works.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with Rentman or similar equipment rental or event management software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're curious about how customers actually get their work done and where the tool could serve them better.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take ownership of your pipeline and your numbers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You communicate clearly, both with customers and internally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You keep your training administration, scheduling, and invoicing organized so the customer journey stays frictionless.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can join us in the Utrecht office as this is a hybrid role.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to haves</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience training or onboarding customers on a SaaS platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to more than one segment, such as dry hire, staging, broadcast, or corporate AV.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An existing network in the German/DACH AV and event industry.<br /></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What you’ll get </strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary based on experience, plus 8% holiday allowance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A results-based bonus based on company performance (up to a full 13th month's salary)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 vacation days to recharge</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Earn an extra day of PTO for each year at Rentman, from your second anniversary up to five years.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A 4-week paid sabbatical after 5 years to go on an adventure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible WFH policy &amp; work from anywhere for 4 weeks a year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension plan through BrightPensioen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An annual training budget to grow your skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to OpenUp for mental well-being and personal growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your choice of a shiny new Windows, Linux, or Mac</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay active with the team: join the Rentman football team, squash and padel, plus a discounted Urban Sports membership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An OV Business card if you live more than 10km from the office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An ambitious, inclusive, and diverse international team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A flexible, energizing workplace with free lunches, office perks (PS5, ping pong, D&amp;D), legendary karaoke nights, and regular team activities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An amazing office in the heart of Utrecht, in the historic Drift 17</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Our process</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here's a breakdown of our recruitment process to give you a clear idea:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Introduction Call with the recruiter about the job &amp; Rentman, online (30-45 mins)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Past Experience &amp; Culture Interview with the team, online o