nizations set clear expectations, define what a role entails, assess performance fairly, support employee growth and make compensation transparent and explainable. From clear roles to fair rewards, all within one continuous process.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">We do this with a driven team of 55+ colleagues. Hundreds of companies in the Netherlands, from scale-ups to corporates, already use Learned. Now we're taking the next step: </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">Germany</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">As </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">Senior Partnership Manager Germany</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> you're part of our founding DE team. You build the partner channel from scratch and become the face of Learned in the German HR ecosystem.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">Lay the foundation for our partner channel in Germany</span></strong></h4><p><span style="color:#000000">You build our German partner channel from the ground up. You decide how we do partnerships in Germany, and then you make it happen: from the first partner to a network that brings in a steady flow of new business.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Our network has two parts:</span></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Implementation partners:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> HR consultants and advisory firms that bring Learned to their clients.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Learning partners:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> </span>companies specialized in job evaluation and learning &amp; development.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">What you’ll do</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Set the strategy.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Map the German HR ecosystem and decide which partners to focus on first. Set clear targets for the channel and make sure partners and direct sales strengthen each other.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Build the foundation.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Shape the partner model for Germany: partner tiers, the commercial terms, and the playbook and processes that let the channel grow. Our Dutch partner programme is your starting point. You adapt it to the German market.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Find and close new partners.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Start conversations at board level, then negotiate and close partnerships.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Turn partners into growth.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Onboard and enable partners, build joint plans and turn them into a steady source of new business.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Activate the market.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Put Learned on the map in Germany with partner and customer events, such as roundtables, webinars and breakfast sessions. You work together with marketing and get operational support for running them.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">How your time is split (at the start)</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">~50%: Finding new partners</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">~30%: Partner management</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">~10%: Events and activation</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">~10%: Strategy</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#000000">As the network grows, your focus shifts towards partner management and scaling the channel. You might also build a team around it.</span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who you work with</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Yo