eriment with image and video processing using Python;</p></li><li><p>Help with data preparation, testing, and evaluation of AI outputs;</p></li><li><p>Participate in product meetings and contribute ideas to ongoing AI projects. </p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p><strong>YOUR PLAYER PROFILE</strong> </p><ul><li><p>Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, AI, Data Science, or a related field (or equivalent experience); </p></li><li><p>You live in or around Amsterdam (already in The Netherlands); </p></li><li><p>Looking forward to work at our office for 4 days per week;</p></li><li><p>Proficiency in Python programming;</p></li><li><p>Basic understanding of Large Language Models and how they are used in applications;</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of SQL for database querying and data manipulation;</p></li><li><p><span style="color:#222222">Familiarity with AI-powered coding agents, such as Claude Code or OpenAI Codex;</span></p></li><li><p>Familiarity with APIs and structured data formats (JSON, REST);</p></li><li><p>Strong curiosity and willingness to learn modern AI tooling; </p></li><li><p>Strong analytical and problem-solving skills;</p></li><li><p>Ability to work independently and as part of a team; </p></li><li><p>Good communication skills.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>NICE TO HAVE</strong></p><ul><li><p>Familiarity with Docker, Airflow, Git;</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with multimodal or visual AI models;</p></li><li><p>Basic knowledge of cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, or GCP);</p></li><li><p>Interest in RAG pipelines, AI agents, or MLOps concepts.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>OUR OFFER</strong></p><ul><li><p>Hands-on experience with state-of-the-art AI technologies;</p></li><li><p>Mentorship from experienced AI and machine learning engineers;</p></li><li><p>Exposure to real-world, production AI systems;</p></li><li><p>A competitive salary, pension plan, and flexible vacation days;</p></li><li><p>A daily catered lunch and fresh fruit at our Amsterdam office;</p></li><li><p>Annual sports tournaments, team outings, and Friday afternoon drinks;</p></li><li><p>A dynamic and creative work environment with colleagues who share the same passion. </p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em>Do you want to contribute to the global growth of 433 and make an impact in the football world? Apply now!</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/433/jr-ai-engineer-amsterdam-262980","tags":["Tech"],"job_types":["Entry","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Amsterdam , Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1794605478},{"slug":"graduate-risk-analyst-amsterdam-171787","company_name":"Imc","title":"Graduate Risk Analyst","description":"&lt;p&gt;Your IMC journey begins with a three-week Global Trainee Program led by our seasoned engineers and traders, during which you’ll link up with graduates from all IMC regions: Europe, the United States, India and Asia-Pacific. During this traineeship, you’ll learn more about IMC, the basics of trading and options theory. Training continues back at your local office, where you’ll receive support from a dedicated mentor. As a Graduate Risk Analyst, you operate at the beating heart of our business: in the dealing room of IMC’s Amsterdam office. Your work supports IMC’s critical day-to-day risk management activities, including the monitoring and analysis of our markets, as well as our credit, liquidity, and operational risks. What happens next is up to you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR CORE RESPONSIBILTIES &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become an expert in options, financial markets, and how IMC applies algorithmic trading as a market maker&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the ongoing development of IMC’s proprietary risk management systems, together with our Engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse developments in the markets in which we trade and identify risks and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an integral part of your team by advising on limit requests, monitoring intraday and overnight risks, and discussing key exposures with our trading desks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR SKILLS AND EXPERIENCES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recent or upcoming graduates seeking to join IMC full-time in February 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An academic background in Mathematics, Physics and/or Econometrics or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in a programming language is preferred (Python, MATLAB or R)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First-class analytical skills and a desire to solve complicated problems creatively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in financial markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note: If you have already applied for this position during the current recruitment season and were not selected, you may reapply when the next recruitment season begins in Summer 2027. We encourage you to focus on enhancing your skillset before reapplying.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to current U.S. immigration and visa restrictions, some candidates may not be eligible to obtain the U.S. business visa required as part of our Global Traineeship Programme. As the programme includes mandatory training in the United States shortly after joining, we are unfortunately unable to proceed with applications from candidates who are unable to obtain the required visa within the programme timeline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;If you are a dual passport holder of another nationality or a European citizen who wants to relocate back to Europe, you remain welcome to apply and should inform our campus recruitment team of your situation:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ---------- class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;IMC is a research-driven trading firm where quantitative modeling, machine learning, and engineering shape how modern markets are traded. A stabilizing force in markets since 1989, we provide liquidity across trading venues, delivering the best outcome in value and risk management to investors. Using our own technology and capital, we build proprietary systems and algorithms that operate across global markets. Our researchers, traders, and engineers work as a collective, combining rapid experimentation, advanced infrastructure, and real-time feedback to turn insight into execution and execution into advantage.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/imc/graduate-risk-analyst-amsterdam-171787","tags":["Risk Management"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794596129},{"slug":"director-of-finance-ecosystem-amsterdam-85525","company_name":"Prosus","title":"Director of Finance - Ecosystem","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who We Are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've ordered dinner through Just Eat Takeaway. You've bought and sold on OLX. You've paid with PayU. Chances are, you've already used a Prosus company today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are Prosus, a global technology company powering some of the world's leading lifestyle ecommerce businesses. Every day, billions of people across India, Latin America, Europe and beyond use our products and services to buy, sell, pay, connect and discover.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our AI-driven ecosystem spans 100+ companies across ecommerce, food delivery, fintech and experiences, serving billions of consumers worldwide. AI powers how we operate and innovate, with more than 60,000 active AI agents helping our teams build, scale and move faster. Through our investment team, we also back the founders and technologies shaping the future: From robotics and autonomous systems to synthetic biology and frontier AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guided by our five values <strong>Innovation, Results, People, Impact, and Entrepreneurship,</strong> culture is our competitive advantage. We thrive with experimentation; we build, we test, we learn, we iterate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in shaping the future of technology at global scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Strategic Finance, Planning &amp; Analysis team drives financial performance management across Prosus's global ecosystems - partnering with operating companies and Group Finance to ensure targets are met and capital is deployed effectively. The EU ecosystem team sits at the centre of Prosus's ambition to build a leading lifestyle e-commerce platform in Europe, and this Director role is the financial engine behind that ambition.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own the full Strategic FP&amp;A function for Prosus's European portfolio, managing the annual budgeting, planning, and forecasting cycle across a multi-entity, multi-country ecosystem, and leading the operating cadences that keep business unit CFOs, ecosystem leads, and Group Finance aligned. Within your first 60 days, you'll have established a working rhythm with every BU and minority investment finance team in the region. Within your first quarter, you'll hold full ownership of the EU ecosystem budgeting and forecasting cycle.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an active moment for the portfolio. M&amp;A and divestiture activity is ongoing, and you'll be a direct contributor to at least one strategic transaction within your first year,  not as a reviewer, but as a hands-on partner to the ecosystem leads driving those decisions. The team you'll lead is five to six direct reports; developing their capabilities and raising the bar on finance practice across the BU finance teams is as much a part of the role as the numbers themselves.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This isn't a reporting function. This is financial leadership for one of Prosus's most strategically significant regions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You think in systems and act with precision. You're comfortable holding the full picture of a complex, multi-entity portfolio while also rolling up your sleeves on the analysis that makes a business case credible or a forecast defensible. Ambiguity doesn't slow you down - you move forward with the information available, surface the brutal facts clearly, and adjust as the picture sharpens.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built trust with senior stakeholders before - CFOs, business leads, Group Finance counterparts, not just by managing up but by being the person in the room who brings clarity. You give direct, evidence-based points of view and create space for the people around you to do the same. You care about the growth of your team as much as the quality of the output, and you understand that both are how a finance function earns its seat at the table.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Deep experience in finance or FP&amp;A at group or multi-entity level, with a background in digital economy, e-commerce, consumer internet, or a closely adjacent sector</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Proven ability to lead end-to-end budgeting, forecasting, and planning cycles across complex, matrixed organisations - coordinating multiple finance teams toward a single, coherent view</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Hands-on track record analysing financial statements, business cases, and performance data to surface actionable insight for senior decision-makers</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Comfortable partnering directly with business unit CFOs and ecosystem leads on strategic projects including M&amp;A, divestiture, and performance benchmarking with the credibility to challenge and the judgement to know when to align</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Experience managing and developing a finance team, with a genuine investment in building capability at every level</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Fluent English communication, written and spoken, with the ability to translate financial complexity into clear, concise narratives for diverse audiences</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Familiarity with Group Finance functions (tax, treasury, reporting, consolidation) and how a finance function at this level interfaces with each</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Experience with Hyperion or OneStream is a plus</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Background in minority investment oversight or portfolio company finance is a plus</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Exposure to multi-country or cross-border finance environments in Europe is a plus</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Typical Day</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your day might begin with a performance review call with a business unit CFO - working through the latest actuals, flagging variances, and agreeing on the narrative before it reaches Group Finance. From there, you're likely in the detail: a forecast model that needs stress-testing, a business case for a potential acquisition, or a consolidation question that cuts across tax, treasury, and reporting.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Throughout the day, your team is moving in parallel - running analyses, preparing materials, coordinating with BU finance counterparts across the EU. You check in, unblock, and give direct feedback. By afternoon, you might be in a working session with an ecosystem lead on a live strategic project, or preparing the ecosystem performance summary that feeds into the Group FP&amp;A cycle.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Global Impact: Play a crucial role in shaping the future of global commerce.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Growth Opportunities: Expand your expertise through diverse global challenges and unique opportunities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Innovative Culture: Join a forward-thinking team that values strategic insights and fosters continuous innovation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Creative Environment: Engage in work that encourages creativity and constant improvement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Collaborative Atmosphere: Benefit from autonomy and self-management in a supportive and positive workspace.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Hybrid Work: Experience the satisfaction of our flexible model tailored to balance work and life.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Competitive Compensation: Enjoy a salary package that reflects your skills and contributions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Comprehensive Benefits: From health and wellness to learning, and everyday perks, we offer a well-rounded package designed to help you thrive at work and beyond.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Prosus?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Prosus, your colleagues include 60,000 AI agents… and your job is to figure out what that actually means. We're one of the largest operators of agentic AI on the planet, inside a $100B+ portfolio across 100+ companies and two billion people. The humans here own what AI can't do alone: judgment, creativity, and the call on what gets built next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Own the impact. Work the ecosystem. Earn your growth. Build with backing.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Curious about our perks and benefits? Take a look </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://prosusbenefits.com/"><em><u>at this page</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Diversity &amp; Inclusion Commitment</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We respect the dignity and human rights of individuals and communities wherever we operate in the world. Building an inclusive workplace where everyone feels welcome and can thrive is critical for us. We provide access to education, which helps everyone understand the important role they play and the positive impact they can have.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Want to know more about life at Prosus? Explore our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.prosus.com/the-prosus-way"><em>culture and values</em></a><em>.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/prosus/director-of-finance-ecosystem-amsterdam-85525","tags":["Investment Org. - Finance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794595221},{"slug":"senior-cyber-security-specialist-amsterdam-453476","company_name":"Prosus","title":"Senior Cyber Security Specialist","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who We Are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've ordered dinner through Just Eat Takeaway. You've bought and sold on OLX. You've paid with PayU. Chances are, you've already used a Prosus company today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are Prosus, a global technology company powering some of the world's leading lifestyle ecommerce businesses. Every day, billions of people across India, Latin America, Europe and beyond use our products and services to buy, sell, pay, connect and discover.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our AI-driven ecosystem spans 100+ companies across ecommerce, food delivery, fintech and experiences, serving billions of consumers worldwide. AI powers how we operate and innovate, with more than 60,000 active AI agents helping our teams build, scale and move faster. Through our investment team, we also back the founders and technologies shaping the future: From robotics and autonomous systems to synthetic biology and frontier AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guided by our five values <strong>Innovation, Results, People, Impact, and Entrepreneurship,</strong> culture is our competitive advantage. We thrive with experimentation; we build, we test, we learn, we iterate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in shaping the future of technology at global scale.</p><h2><strong>The Problem You'll Solve</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Cyber Specialist, you'll be part of Prosus' Global Cyber team, helping our businesses identify, understand and manage their most critical cyber and technology risks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work across a diverse portfolio of businesses, delivering hands-on security testing, advisory and assurance projects that strengthen security.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will use AI natively in everything you do. Your work will span a broad range of cybersecurity and technology domains, including:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Delivering cyber risk assessments, security reviews and controls testing across complex technology environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conducting red teaming exercises and long-term Advanced Persistent Threat (APT) simulations to identify vulnerabilities and test organisational resilience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assessing cloud infrastructure, data platforms, DevOps environments and CI/CD pipelines to identify security weaknesses and opportunities for improvement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Designing and facilitating cyber crisis simulations to test business preparedness and incident response capabilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Providing practical, constructive recommendations that help management strengthen security without slowing down innovation or business growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partnering with technology and business leaders across our global portfolio to translate complex technical risks into meaningful business outcomes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a full-time global role based in our Amsterdam (Zuidas) office, with up to 30% international travel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who You Are</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hands-on cybersecurity professional with strong technical specialist experience in offensive security, security engineering or red teaming. You enjoy getting into the technical detail, investigating threats and identifying weaknesses rather than focusing solely on governance, risk and compliance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An AI and technology enthusiast who enjoys understanding how systems work, building harnesses and getting hands-on with complex technical environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable navigating code, CI/CD pipelines, cloud environments and modern technology architectures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entrepreneurial in your mindset, with exposure to both fast-moving start-ups and larger, more mature IT organisations, not afraid to use AI to get the job done.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A confident communicator who can build trusted relationships, tell compelling stories and translate technical concepts into clear business language.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equally comfortable engaging with CTOs, CIOs, security leaders, architects, developers and system administrators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A global mindset, with interests beyond technology and an openness to travelling internationally, including to less conventional destinations.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You Bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3–7 years of relevant professional experience in cybersecurity, with a strong technical foundation in offensive security, threat intelligence, red teaming or related disciplines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience conducting or supporting penetration tests, security assessments, adversary simulations, threat investigations or other offensive security activities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands on work with AI harnesses and offensive AI models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with cloud technologies, data platforms and modern software engineering environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working across different organisational environments, ideally including both entrepreneurial and more established technology businesses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relevant certifications such as CEH, OSCP, CISSP, CISM or CISA are welcome, but we value practical technical expertise and hands-on experience over certifications alone.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Prosus?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Prosus, your colleagues include 60,000 AI agents… and your job is to figure out what that actually means. We're one of the largest operators of agentic AI on the planet, inside a $100B+ portfolio across 100+ companies and two billion people. The humans here own what AI can't do alone: judgment, creativity, and the call on what gets built next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Own the impact. Work the ecosystem. Earn your growth. Build with backing.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Curious about our perks and benefits? Take a look </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://prosusbenefits.com/"><em><u>at this page</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Diversity &amp; Inclusion Commitment</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We respect the dignity and human rights of individuals and communities wherever we operate in the world. Building an inclusive workplace where everyone feels welcome and can thrive is critical for us. We provide access to education, which helps everyone understand the important role they play and the positive impact they can have.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Want to know more about life at Prosus? Explore our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.prosus.com/the-prosus-way"><em>culture and values</em></a><em>.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/prosus/senior-cyber-security-specialist-amsterdam-453476","tags":["Investment Org. - Finance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794595221},{"slug":"large-enterprise-account-executive-nordics-benelux-netherlands-195953","company_name":"N8N","title":"Large Enterprise Account Executive, Nordics & Benelux","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The AI orchestration of your wildest imagination.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">n8n is the open workflow orchestration platform built for the new era of AI. We give technical teams the freedom of code with the speed of no-code, so they can automate faster, smarter, and without limits. Backed by a fiercely inventive community and 500+ builder-approved integrations, we’re changing the way people bring systems together and scale ideas for impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since our founding in 2019, we’ve grown into a diverse team of over 260 - working across Europe and the US, connected by a shared builder spirit and with our centre of gravity in Berlin. Along the way, we’ve:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cultivated a community of more than 650,000 active developers and builders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Earned 190K+ GitHub stars, making us one of the world’s Top 40 most popular projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by top investors, from Sequoia’s first German seed to our SAP's recent strategic investment - bringing us to a $5.2bn valuation</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />That’s the company we’ve built. Now we’d love to see what <em>you </em>can build. If you’re applying, try n8n out - whether you’re technical or not - and share a screenshot of your first workflow with us. The easiest place to start is here: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://app.n8n.cloud/register"><u>app.n8n.cloud/register</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re in a defining moment of an incredible journey. Come and build with us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎯 Your main goal will be to land and expand n8n inside the world’s largest organisations, closing the biggest deals in our portfolio.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Large Enterprise Account Executive covering Nordics &amp; Benelux, you will own a territory of global-scale accounts and lead long, complex deals from first conversation to multi-year commitment:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>BUILD STRATEGIC ACCOUNT PLANS</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and execute account strategies for organisations with 5,001 or more employees</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Open doors with outbound campaigns aimed at CTOs, CIOs and engineering and platform leaders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn community adoption inside large companies into sponsored, funded opportunities.</p></li></ul><h3>LEAD COMPLEX, MULTI-THREADED DEALS</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run deep discovery, quantify business impact and build an executive-level business case.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Map and align decision makers across engineering, IT, security, legal and procurement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Solutions Engineers, Partnerships and Customer Success to prove value and de-risk adoption.</p></li></ul><h3>CLOSE AND EXPAND AT SCALE</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the cycle through security, legal and procurement, typically over three to six months or more.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Negotiate six-figure deals with confidence and keep clear commercial control.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan expansion across business units and use cases, and share what you learn with Product and leadership.</p></li></ul><h2>REQUIREMENTS</h2><h3>Must-haves</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🏢 Large Enterprise sales:</strong> You have at least five years of enterprise SaaS sales experience, selling into organisations with 5,001 or more employees, and you can explain customer size, deal complexity and cycle length.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>💰 Six-figure deals:</strong> You have closed multiple deals of £100k+ ACV in multi-stakeholder cycles of three to six months or more.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧑‍💻 Technical buyers and executives:</strong> You have sold to developers, engineers, CTOs and CIOs, and you can carry a technical conversation and an executive one in the same deal.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🎯 New-logo hunter:</strong> You generate your own pipeline through outbound and win new customers rather than relying on expansion or inbound.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📈 Track record:</strong> You have consistently hit or exceeded quota over the past two to three years.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧭 Structured selling:</strong> You use a methodology such as MEDDPICC and navigate technical evaluations, procurement, legal and security reviews.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📍 Location:</strong> You are based in the Nordics / Benelux. This role involves regular travel to customers in the region.</p></li></ul><h3>Nice-to-haves</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🛠️ Technical product background:</strong> You have sold developer tools, cloud infrastructure, data, AI or automation platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🤝 Partner-led deals:</strong> You have worked deals with system integrators or cloud partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🚀 Open source or PLG exposure:</strong> You understand how community adoption turns into enterprise revenue.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why join us?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will close the largest deals in our portfolio and shape how n8n sells to the world’s biggest organisations, with a product technical teams already use and love. You will work closely with Solutions Engineers, Partnerships, Customer Success and Product, and leadership will listen to what you learn in the field. n8n is growing at an exceptional pace, backed by a vibrant community and a remote-first culture built on autonomy, experimentation and high talent density. Apply now and help us bring AI-powered automation to the global enterprise.<strong> </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>n8n is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, colour, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We can sponsor visas to Germany; for any other country, you need to have existing right to work.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Our company language is English.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>You care about diversity and inclusion? We do too! Check out our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/Diversity-inclusion-and-belonging-n8n-c1bec2fff536422d868b1a438d990e35?pvs=21"><em>Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging initiatives at n8n</em></a><em> (</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/n8n/Diversity-inclusion-and-belonging-n8n-c1bec2fff536422d868b1a438d990e35"><em>https://www.notion.so/n8n/Diversity-inclusion-and-belonging-n8n-c1bec2fff536422d868b1a438d990e35</em></a><em>).</em></p><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Location disclaimer:</strong> If you see multiple job postings for the same role, it is most likely because we're hiring remotely for this role and posting in different locations to make sure every potential candidate can see the role. Please apply to the location you're the most likely to work from in the future. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Benefits </strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive compensation</strong> 💸 – We offer fair and attractive pay.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership</strong> 💪 – Our core value is to “empower others,” and we mean it—you’ll get a slice of n8n with equity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work/life balance</strong> 🏖️ – We work hard but ensure you have time to recharge:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Europe:</strong> 30 days of vacation, plus public holidays wherever you are.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>US:</strong> 20 vacation days, 8 sick days, plus public holidays wherever you are.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Health &amp; wellness</strong> 🩺 –</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Europe:</strong> We provide benefits according to local country norms.*</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>US</strong>: Multiple low-premium, low-deductible medical plans with coverage for individuals and families—plus a no-cost premium HDHP option with a pre-seeded HSA—along with dental and vision coverage.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Future planning</strong> 💰 –</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Europe:</strong> We provide pension contributions according to local country norms.*</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>US:</strong> 401(k) retirement plan with a 4% employer match.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Financial security</strong> 🛡️ –</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Europe:</strong> We provide benefits according to local country norms.*</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>US: </strong>Company-paid short-term and long-term disability insurance, plus life insurance to support you and your loved ones.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Career growth</strong> 📈 – We hire rising stars who grow with us! You’ll get €1K (or equivalent) per year to spend on courses, books, events, or coaching to level up your skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A passionate team</strong> 🤩 – We love our product, and we prove it with regular hackathons where we see who can build the coolest thing with it!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remote-first</strong> 🌏 – Our team works remotely across Europe, with regular off-sites for team bonding. Some roles, like sales in the US, are hybrid—please check the job description.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Giving back</strong> 🤝 – We're big fans of open source, and you'll get $100 per month to support projects you care about.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transparency</strong> 🙏 – We all know what everyone’s working on, how the company is doing—the whole shebang.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>*Country and/or State specific details provided in your employment agreement.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/n8n/large-enterprise-account-executive-nordics-benelux-netherlands-195953","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Netherlands","created_at":1794595221},{"slug":"security-architect-de-lier-31641","company_name":"Priva","title":"Security Architect","description":"<p class="Paragraph SCXW48555210 BCX8">Are you a security specialist in the OT space looking to expand your expertise into cloud solutions? Are you a cloud security champion passionate about bringing your expertise into OT/IoT space? At <strong>Priva Product Development Organisation </strong>we are looking for the <strong>Security Architect</strong> who will shape the security of our products.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW48555210 BCX8"> &nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW48555210 BCX8"><strong>Security Architect in Priva Product Development – Why this role matters</strong>&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW48555210 BCX8">At Priva, we develop hardware products and software services for horticulture and building automation. Seeing the importance of our products for our customers, we recognize the need to continuously keep these secure in the ever evolving, fast-paced world. The security requirements in our landscape span four different areas:&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ol class="NumberListStyle1 SCXW48555210 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW48555210 BCX8">Physical/embedded device security.&nbsp;</p></li></ol><ol start="2" class="NumberListStyle1 SCXW48555210 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW48555210 BCX8">OT (operational technology) network security.&nbsp;</p></li></ol><ol start="3" class="NumberListStyle1 SCXW48555210 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW48555210 BCX8">OT network to Priva-hosted cloud services communications.&nbsp;</p></li></ol><ol start="4" class="NumberListStyle1 SCXW48555210 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW48555210 BCX8">Priva's hybrid on-prem/multi-cloud platform applications security, including applications, infrastructure, CI/CD pipelines.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ol><p class="Paragraph SCXW48555210 BCX8">What makes this role truly unique is that our products contain long-lived hardware components that our customers run for years. Engineering future-proofed security solutions and maintaining a security posture at existing sites across all these areas having wide range of varying implementations and security needs creates a great challenge and a great fun.&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW48555210 BCX8">As part of the architecture team, you will play a key role in shaping the future of Priva's portfolio offered on the global market. You define security standards, security practices and security designs for our products that are used in tens of thousands of buildings and greenhouses. You work across product, engineering, and operations teams to ensure security controls and adhered to, implemented and tested as you have designed these. That’s real impact.&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW48555210 BCX8"><strong>What you will be doing</strong>&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW48555210 BCX8">As a Security Architect, you have a very simple mission: you see to it that Priva's hardware products and software (cloud) services are secured against known and emergent threats in lines with the industry standards and practices. You build upon your strong background in securing device/OT networks, cloud applications, and engraining the security practices in the daily work of Agile teams to achieve consistent security posture across all Priva products, designs, and customer deployments.&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW48555210 BCX8"> As a security architect, you are trusted counterpart of Priva Security, Quality, and Compliance officer to define, review, and execute controls arising from ISO9001 and ISO27001 standards and internal initiatives. You are responsible for presenting the necessary evidence of Priva’s compliance with these controls to the auditors.&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW131319278 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW131319278 BCX8">Security standards, policies, and design patterns library&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW131319278 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW131319278 BCX8">Security architecture review process&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW131319278 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW131319278 BCX8">Risk register and residual risk acceptance documentation&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW131319278 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW131319278 BCX8">Periodic product security implementation reviews, including maintaining non-compliance register&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW131319278 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW131319278 BCX8">Defined requirements, products and work packages for security-focused projects with 3rd party service providers, reviewing and accepting their deliverables, and supervising the implementation of these deliverables in the Priva hardware products and software services.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW131319278 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW131319278 BCX8">Regulatory compliance (IEC 62443-4, ISO 27001, ISO 9001 or other standard that may be applicable in specific geographies)&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW131319278 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW131319278 BCX8">Threat intelligence briefing relevant to OT/IoT threat landscape&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW131319278 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW131319278 BCX8">Designing, implementing, and reviewing security controls applied at major customer sites.&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW131319278 BCX8">Above all, this is a hands-on role – occasionally writing code is included. You connect the industry’s best practices, ISO standards, product vision with the daily work of the product team. As a security architect, you practice what you preach. You explain, coach, and show by example the implementation of security as Secure SDLC in the developer’s daily work.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8"><strong>To succeed in this role:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">You are passionate about OT security; you have great interest in the application of our products in the field. You are curious to grasp how our products truly work for our customers to find the best balance between security, reliability, and cost. You share the opinion that "if I don't secure Priva’s applications, then no one else will".&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">You identify and eliminate issues in the development cycle that can jeopardize the security posture. You know and can show by example how to "test <em>securely</em> as well as test <em>security</em>"&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">You are a great collaborator who can be a valuable sparring partner with product managers to understand and refine customer's needs for security so that you define the right security designs for market segments. Engineering managers rely on your ability to steer security implementations within the product teams.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">You are comfortable designing products that our customers will be running for years; comfortable providing guidance to LCM activities for existing customers to update hardware and software components to continuously stay secure.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">You share the knowledge about security subjects; you explain why security practices exist and what they achieve in the long run.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">You can translate security designs into engineering specifications, appraise implementation designs, conduct code reviews. This role with a strong hands-on component, not just a pure governance role.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">You understand and can register, document, and communicate clearly risks and trade-offs between differen t project execution scenarios&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">You have had hands-on experience implementing security designs using modern programming language and frameworks, and you are able to coach product teams to increase their secure coding maturity e.g. by running threat modelling workshops with the engineering team.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">You have vast experience with architecture roles with 3-5 years of experience specifically focusing on security.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">In addition, you have the following technical expertise:&nbsp;</p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">Proven track record across at least two of the three domains: OT/IoT/embedded security, network security, cloud security&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">You are familiar with modern authentication and authorization frameworks (JWT, OpenID, SAML) and (REST) API security and protection approached&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">ISO 27001 and IEC 62443-4 understanding at a working level&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">Working knowledge with or excellent ability to apply the PKI and certificate lifecycle management at scale; also, with the vision how to implement this in OT/IoT deployment contexts&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">Solid network security understanding: firewall policy, micro-segmentation, DMZ design for IT/OT boundaries&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">Zero trust architecture principles&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">Secure SDLC and DevSecOps tools and practices (think about OWASP, SANS25, Snyk, Black Duck, etc)&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8"> &nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8"><strong>The following competence is desired:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">OT/ICS protocols and architectures (such as BACnet Secure Connect, Modbus, DNP3, MQTT, AMQP)&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">Embedded device security for industrial PCs, systems-on-chip, and microcontrollers: secure boot, hardware security modules (HSMs), TPM, secure enclave concepts, firmware &amp; data signing, encryption&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">Cloud security on at least one major platform (AWS, Azure, or GCP)&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">Container and Kubernetes security&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">Secrets management and key management systems (HashiCorp Vault, AWS KMS, Azure Key Vault)&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW62144440 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW62144440 BCX8">Priva's technical stack is C#/C++/.NET and Angular. Experience implementing production projects with this stack is preferred, but not required if you are able to learn it quickly (based on your vast experience)&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW170785910 BCX8"><strong>What we offer you</strong>&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW170785910 BCX8"> &nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW170785910 BCX8">💶 <strong>Excellent remuneration</strong> — competitive and aligned with experience.&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW170785910 BCX8">🌴 <strong>30 days holiday</strong> per year, with the option to buy 5 more at half price.&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW170785910 BCX8">🏦 <strong>Excellent pension contribution</strong>.&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW170785910 BCX8">🎓 <strong>Education budget</strong> of €1,000 per year.&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW170785910 BCX8">⏰ <strong>Flexible working hours</strong>.&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW170785910 BCX8">🍱 <strong>Onsite canteen</strong> (e.g., poke bowl for €2).&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW170785910 BCX8">🏋️ <strong>Free onsite gym</strong>.&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW170785910 BCX8">🎉 <strong>Vibrant, open culture</strong>.&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/priva/security-architect-de-lier-31641","tags":["Tech & Data"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"De Lier, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1794594677},{"slug":"remote-talent-acquisition-partner-europe-amsterdam-rotterdam-370843","company_name":"DeepHealth","title":"Talent Acquisition Partner-Europe","description":"<p class="MsoNormal">DeepHealth is seeking an experienced Talent Acquisition Partner based in Europe to own high-impact, full-cycle recruiting across European markets and support global hiring as needed. This is a hands-on execution role in a fast-paced, high-volume environment where searches are varied, specialized, and rarely repeatable. The successful candidate will combine a strong B2B SaaS recruiting background with exceptional organization, proactive sourcing, and strategic hiring manager partnership, developing a deep understanding of each position and delivering tailored hiring strategies. This position contributes to continuous improvement of an evolving global Talent Acquisition function but is not responsible for building or leading the function.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Essential Duties and Responsibilities</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Own full-cycle recruitment across multiple European markets, with additional support for US, Canadian, and APAC hiring as business needs require.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Manage a high-volume, diverse portfolio of technical, commercial, product, and corporate requisitions while maintaining quality and responsiveness.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Lead detailed intake meetings to understand business objectives, essential competencies, technical requirements, hiring priorities, and candidate profiles for each distinct search.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Develop tailored sourcing and assessment strategies for niche and business-critical roles; proactively engage passive candidates through direct sourcing, LinkedIn Recruiter, referrals, and professional networks.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Build trusted relationships with hiring managers, HR Business Partners, and leaders; advise on talent markets, compensation expectations, hiring feasibility, and selection strategy.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Challenge and refine role requirements constructively, distinguish must-haves from preferences, and proactively address obstacles to hiring.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Coordinate screening, interviewing, feedback, offer development, negotiation, and hiring handoffs while delivering timely, transparent candidate communication.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Independently prioritize competing requisitions, manage calendars and deadlines, maintain strong follow-through, and adapt quickly to changing business needs.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Maintain accurate ATS records and provide regular reporting on pipeline health, time-to-fill, sourcing effectiveness, bottlenecks, and hiring progress.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Use recruiting technology, AI-assisted tools, and appropriate automation to improve sourcing and execution efficiency while preserving sound judgment and human oversight.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Ensure hiring activities comply with relevant country-specific employment requirements, GDPR, data privacy standards, and DeepHealth policies.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Partner with the global People and Communications teams to strengthen DeepHealth’s employer brand across European markets.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Plan and deliver local talent-attraction initiatives, such as recruitment events, university or professional-community partnerships, networking activities and employee referral campaigns.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Build relationships with local universities, professional associations and talent communities to develop pipelines for priority roles.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Represent DeepHealth professionally and communicate its mission and employer value proposition throughout the candidate journey.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>PLEASE NOTE: </strong>This is not an exhaustive list of all duties, responsibilities and requirements of the position. Other functions may be assigned and management retains the right to add or change duties at any time.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Minimum Qualifications, Education and Experience</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListBullet">5+ years of progressive, hands-on full-cycle Talent Acquisition experience, including substantial recruiting experience within B2B SaaS organizations (required).</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Demonstrated experience recruiting across multiple European countries and navigating differences in talent markets, employment practices, and hiring processes (required).</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Proven ability to manage a high volume of varied, complex requisitions across multiple job families rather than repeated hiring for a single profile (required).</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Experience recruiting technical roles such as Software Engineering, Cloud/DevOps, Product, Data Science, or AI/ML, alongside commercial or corporate functions (required).</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Strong direct sourcing capability, including passive candidate engagement and role-specific market mapping (required).</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Demonstrated ability to build strategic relationships with hiring managers and senior stakeholders, advise on hiring strategy, and influence decisions (required).</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Exceptional time management, prioritization, organization, communication, and attention to detail (required).</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Experience with applicant tracking systems, LinkedIn Recruiter, recruiting metrics, and modern sourcing tools (required).</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Professional fluency in written and spoken English and ability to collaborate across international time zones (required).</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Experience developing employer-brand activity or delivering local talent-attraction initiatives, such as recruitment events, university partnerships, professional-community engagement or employee advocacy (preferred).</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Experience recruiting into the United States, Canada, and APAC (preferred).</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Experience in healthcare technology, enterprise imaging, PACS/RIS, radiology software, or clinical AI (preferred).</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Experience supporting global SaaS organizations, including Employer of Record arrangements, and familiarity with Recruitee or comparable ATS platforms (preferred).</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Additional European language proficiency (preferred).</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Quality Standards</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Communicates and collaborates professionally with colleagues, candidates, hiring managers, and external partners.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Demonstrates initiative, integrity, discretion, accountability, and confidentiality in all areas of performance.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Follows applicable local, regional, and country employment laws, including data privacy requirements.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Follows all DeepHealth policies, procedures, safety, and compliance standards.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet">Adapts to new priorities, tools, systems, and ways of working.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListBullet"> Completes responsibilities accurately, efficiently, and within agreed timelines.</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Travel</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">This position may require occasional global travel of up to 10%, based on business needs.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Working Environment</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Remote (Europe); specific employing country and work arrangement subject to confirmation.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Physical Demands</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">The employee must be able to perform the essential duties and responsibilities of the position, wit