><strong>Ce que tu vas faire chez nous</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build &amp; Run de A à Z</strong> : tu conçois et fais évoluer des features end-to-end : design, développement, releases et suivi en production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on &amp; design</strong> : tu codes, refactores et améliores l'existant. Tu participes à l'architecture avec le CTO et poses les bases d'un système capable de scaler.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>PR review &amp; excellence technique</strong> : tu élèves le niveau de l'équipe en challengeant le code, la modélisation, les cas limites et la maintenabilité.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Intégrations robustes</strong> : tu construis des APIs et des systèmes résilients adaptés à des contraintes métier fortes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fiabilité &amp; observabilité</strong> : tu conçois des systèmes capables de détecter et prévenir les problèmes avant qu'ils n'atteignent les utilisateurs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leadership technique</strong> : tu accompagnes les développeurs de l'équipe, partages tes pratiques et fais grandir les personnes autour de toi.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ce qui t'attend techniquement</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stack</strong>: TypeScript, Next.js, NestJS, MongoDB, Redis, AWS, monorepo Turborepo</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Observabilité</strong> : Sentry, BetterStack, OpenTelemetry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Façon de travailler</strong> : Kanban, sans sprint. On livre en petits incréments et on deploy plusieurs fois par jour</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Profil recherché</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">6+ ans d'expérience avec une expérience prouvée sur des produits en production utilisés par de vrais utilisateurs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tu as déjà construit et opéré un backend dans la durée. Tu connais les compromis d'une architecture qui doit tenir dans le temps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tu es capable de couvrir tout le cycle : compréhension du produit, system design, développement, déploiement et run.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tu as le réflexe des cas limites. Quand on manipule des documents légaux et des données dont nos clients dépendent au quotidien, la question « que se passe-t-il si cet appel échoue au milieu ? » compte plus que la maîtrise d'un framework.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tu sais prendre des décisions avec une information incomplète et les assumer. On cherche quelqu'un qui tranche, pas quelqu'un qui organise une quatrième réunion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tu sais avancer dans l'imparfait. La dette technique existe, elle est nommée et priorisée : tu préfères faire progresser le produit plutôt que de viser une perfection théorique.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tu utilises l'IA au quotidien et tu veux participer à construire nos pratiques et nos outils, pas seulement coder plus vite.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tu as déjà joué un rôle de Tech Lead : ownership d'un système, décisions d'architecture et accompagnement d'autres développeurs.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Processus de recrutement</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Echange RH</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entretien technique avec un développeur de l'équipe</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entretien technique (algorithme et design technique) avec le CTO</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entretien de fit avec deux des fondateurs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prise de référence et offre</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Conditions</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Salaire</strong>: 50-65 k€ selon expérience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Télétravail</strong>: full remote (et des bureaux à Paris si tu en as envie)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/hexa/remote-senior-software-engineer-75803","tags":["Filiz"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1794616817},{"slug":"forward-deployed-engineer-munich-209208","company_name":"remberg","title":"Forward Deployed Engineer (f/m/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>At remberg, you’ll help to keep the world running.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everything that gets produced relies on a maintenance team behind the scenes that keeps the machines, equipment and infrastructure running. We are helping these teams by simplifying their work with modern, agentic maintenance software. At remberg, we are serving clients like Remondis, Würth, Edeka, Rotkäppchen and 300+ more.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Supported by the visionary founders of category-defining businesses such as Celonis, Dash0, UiPath, Personio and Forto, as well as leading investors like Earlybird, Speedinvest, Oxx, Acton, and Fly Ventures, remberg is positioned to be the European category leader for modern, agentic maintenance software.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHAT THE ROLE OFFERS</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Als <strong>Forward Deployed Engineer</strong> sorgst du dafür, dass remberg bei unseren Kunden zum Herzstück der Instandhaltung wird. Du arbeitest hands-on zwischen Prospects, Kunden, Product und Engineering. Du verbindest remberg mit SAP und anderen ERP-Systemen, bringst Sensor- und Maschinendaten auf die Plattform und gibst der remberg KI den Kontext, den sie braucht, um in der Industrie echten Mehrwert zu liefern. Du baust, was Kund:innen brauchen, bringst es schnell live und lässt deine Learnings direkt ins Produkt einfließen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Als erster FDE bei remberg gestaltest du die Rolle von Grund auf und baust die ersten Playbooks. Du berichtest direkt an Julian Borg, unseren Co-Founder und CPO, und arbeitest eng mit Kunden, Go-to-Market sowie Product und Engineering zusammen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du arbeitest hybrid aus unserem Office in München und bist im Schnitt ein paar Tage im Monat bei Kunden vor Ort.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>THE IMPACT YOU'LL HAVE</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>SAP/ERP-Integration:</strong> Du entwickelst Integrationen zwischen remberg und SAP (z. B. SAP PM/MM, S/4HANA, ECC) oder anderen ERP-Systemen. Dabei begleitest du sie vom technischen Scoping über das Data Mapping bis zum stabilen Betrieb nach dem Go-live.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Kundenkommunikation: </strong>Für Instandhaltung, Operations und IT bist du die technische Ansprechperson, vor Ort und remote. Du übersetzt Business-Anforderungen in technische Lösungen und erklärst sie so, dass alle mitkommen. Bei Kundencalls und Sales Deals in der späten Phase bist du dabei, schätzt Machbarkeit und Aufwand ein und beantwortest IT- und Security-Fragen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sensor-Integration:</strong> Du bindest Maschinen- und Sensordaten (z. B. über IoT-Plattformen, OPC UA, MQTT oder Kunden-APIs) an remberg an und ermöglichst so zustandsbasierte Instandhaltung und automatisch ausgelöste Aufträge.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI Context Engineering:</strong> Du bereitest Kundendaten, Dokumente und Instandhaltungswissen so auf, dass die remberg KI präzise und verlässliche Antworten liefert. Gemeinsam mit Kunden prüfst du die Ergebnisse und verbesserst den Kontext Schritt für Schritt.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product-Feedback-Loop:</strong> Wenn mehrere Kunden vor derselben Herausforderung stehen, machst du mit Product und Engineering aus der Einzellösung ein Feature für alle. Du baust wiederverwendbare Integrationspakete und schreibst Playbooks, mit denen AEs und CSMs Standardfragen selbst beantworten können.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>HOW YOU'LL GROW WITH US</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Erfahrung:</strong> 3+ Jahre in Software Engineering, Solutions oder Integration Engineering, technischer Beratung, Product Management oder ähnlichen Rollen, idealerweise im B2B-Software-, Industrie- oder Fertigungsumfeld.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Kommunikation:</strong> Du kommunizierst sicher mit Stakeholdern vom Shopfloor über die IT bis zum Management, gehst Probleme strukturiert an und willst Dinge shippen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Integrations-Know-how:</strong> Hands-on-Erfahrung mit APIs (REST, OData), Data Mapping und Enterprise-Systemen. Erfahrung mit SAP oder anderen ERP-Systemen ist ein großes Plus.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Industriedaten &amp; IoT:</strong> Du kennst dich mit Sensordaten, IoT-Plattformen oder Industrieprotokollen (z. B. OPC UA, MQTT) aus oder hast richtig Lust, dich einzuarbeiten.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Engineering Skills:</strong> Solide Programmierkenntnisse (z. B. Python oder TypeScript) und SQL sowie praktische Erfahrung mit LLMs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mobilität:</strong> Du bist bereit, im Schnitt ein paar Tage pro Monat zu Kunden zu reisen. Zudem hast du einen Führerschein, damit du dabei flexibel bist.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sprachen:</strong> Fließendes Deutsch (C2) und Englisch (C1) in Wort und Schrift.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>EVERYTHING YOU NEED TO THRIVE</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 <strong>Competitive compensation package</strong>: Enjoy a salary, benefits, and equity*, with annual reviews.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>💻 State-of-the-art tools and equipment</strong> for a modern and efficient setup.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🍏 Health and wellness benefits</strong>: Access to Nilo Health, JobRad*, and your choice between a GUUD card or Wellpass / Urban Sports Club for sports and fitness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🥨 Prime office location &amp; culture</strong>: Our office is in the heart of Munich, near the main train station, making it easily accessible for commuters and travelers. Our office is always lively, with 3 days/week in the office.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🌞 Work-from-anywhere flexibility</strong>: You can work remotely for up to 3 months per year.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🌴 Attractive Compensation &amp; Benefits</strong>: In addition to a competitive salary, you'll enjoy different company benefits and 30 vacation days*.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">📚 <strong>Continuous learning</strong>: Get a €1,500 development budget plus 1 day of educational leave per year.*</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤝 <strong>Volunteering day</strong>: 1 paid day per year to give back to a cause you care about.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">*Some perks apply to permanent full-time employees only.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>ABOUT US</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">remberg is a fast-growing start-up based in Munich. Founded in 2018 as a spin-off from TU Munich &amp; CDTM. We help industrial companies to keep the physical world running by simplifying maintenance with modern, agentic software. Today, we are serving clients like Remondis, Würth, Edeka, Rotkäppchen and 300+ more. With ~28 M € capital raised by the visionary founders of category-defining businesses such as Celonis, Dash0, UiPath, Personio and Forto, as well as leading investors like Earlybird, Speedinvest, Oxx, Acton, and Fly Ventures, remberg is positioned to be the European category leader for modern, agentic maintenance software (CMMS/EAM).</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/remberg/forward-deployed-engineer-munich-209208","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich Office","created_at":1794616815},{"slug":"workplace-and-people-operations-manager-berlin-335933","company_name":"Telli","title":"Workplace and People Operations Manager","description":"<h1><strong>about us</strong><br /></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every 10 minutes, 18 million conversations happen between businesses and consumers around the world.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For decades, the consumer side of those conversations sucked: long queues, robotic menus, repeated explanations, and advice that is often unhelpful. Most people today still cannot simply say what their problem is in natural language when communicating with businesses.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI changes that. For the first time, companies can have natural conversations with customers at massive scale. Every B2C company - from energy providers to telcos to insurers - will use AI agents to talk to their customers. The number of conversations businesses will handle is going to explode in the coming years.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At telli, we are solving the challenges that come with that shift. Today, leading B2C companies like Sky are already using telli to deploy thousands of voice agents to provide their customers with a new experience. But building a first voice agent is easy, getting it to drive real outcomes for customers and businesses is the hard part. telli helps companies build, deploy, and improve consumer-facing AI voice agents at scale. This will become one of the most important software categories of the next decade, and we intend to win it.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a small, AI-pilled team that likes to solve hard problems. Be it engineering, product, or GTM - we build, experiment, and move fast, while heavily leveraging the capabilities of AI models. All of us like to challenge ourselves and take real ownership over what we do, all while still staying humble and keeping a low-ego culture.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://principles.telli.com/"><strong>principles</strong></a> to see how we work.<br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>mission</strong><br />As Workplace &amp; People Operations Manager at telli, you own the environment our team does its best work in. You're responsible for keeping our Berlin office running smoothly day to day: workplace processes, people ops, internal events, and the culture initiatives that make telli feel like telli. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>what you'll do:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">run our Berlin office: supplies, equipment, and making sure we stay productive and well-organized</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">drive culture initiatives that keep the team connected as we grow</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">own the employee lifecycle, from onboarding (so new joiners have desk, hardware, and access ready before they walk in) to offboarding</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">build automations around workplace and people ops (ordering, inventory, requests) with AI and no-code tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">jump in wherever help is needed, because no two weeks look the same</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>what makes you a great fit:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">you have a few years of experience in workplace, office, or people operations, ideally at a startup</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">you're hands-on and happy to do the unglamorous work that makes everything else possible</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">you're organized, reliable, and notice the details others miss</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">you build processes that scale instead of solving the same problem twice</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">you're curious about tools and automation and pick up new things fast</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">you take ownership and don't wait for detailed instructions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">you communicate well in both English and German</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">you're a host at heart and love creating great experiences for others</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>you may not be a great fit if:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">you only want to do high-level "strategic" work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">juggling multiple things at once stresses you out</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">you want to work fully remote, since this role lives in the office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">you'd rather watch than roll up your sleeves</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/telli/workplace-and-people-operations-manager-berlin-335933","tags":["General"],"job_types":["Part Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1794616815},{"slug":"tech-lead-cto-munchen-376478","company_name":"Vogel","title":"Tech Lead / CTO (m/w/d)","description":"<h3>The opportunity</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tax advisory has everything automation needs: structured data, recurring work, clear rules. Yet the profession never made the leap, because recurring does not mean uniform. Every case has its own twist, and the law keeps moving. Reasoning resolves exactly this variance. That is why the window is open now.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The model is no longer the scarce part. Expert knowledge and real case data are, and AI labs pay a premium for exactly this. Vogel holds what no AI-native player has: decades of accounting data, edge cases and judgment calls from several thousand mid-sized companies, audited and closed. It never leaves the house, and it becomes the edge of what you build.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The market is being reordered: four in ten tax advisors in Germany leave the profession within ten years, and many of their firms will find no successor. Vogel acquires established advisory firms and develops them further, and every acquisition adds to that base. We have already produced our own annual financial statements with AI. Today, that is one person with a tool. Turning it into a capability of the whole company is the job.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own the technology that makes Vogel AI-first: the data layer above DATEV, the agent infrastructure on top, and the control layer without which nothing in this profession may go live. You decide the architecture and the stack of what we build. What it does and in which order is decided together with Operations and Moritz Vogel in the role of chief product officer, close to the advisors who use it; you shape it with them. You report to and work directly with Moritz Vogel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>What you'll do</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Architecture above DATEV</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the data layer above DATEV. DATEV stays the system of record (for now); the value is created in the layer above it, designed to outlive the system beneath.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Choose and build the agent infrastructure: framework, orchestration, versioning, observability. You answer these questions with code, not with a slide deck.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make integration a capability, not a project: every client brings their own upstream systems, and today each connection is built by hand. Build the layer those systems plug into, so what makes a client different arrives as context the agents read, never as custom code. One more client must never mean one more integration project.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reproducibility and control</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A tax advisor must get the same result twice, and an auditor must be able to trace it. Probabilistic where there is variance, deterministic where there are numbers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the control layer so that a certified professional sees within seconds what an agent did (version, source, decision) and can sign off on it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build evaluation on decades of audited, completed work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team and scale</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make the architecture calls: design, stack, build or buy for the layer. Nobody has decided it for you, and nobody will overrule it by committee.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hire and lead the engineering team. The budget for your first engineers is approved. You start hiring in your first quarter.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make every acquired firm land on the same base, so technology scales with every acquisition. And stay in the code: you commit and you review.</p></li></ul><h3>Questions you'll answer</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Where exactly does probabilistic end and deterministic begin?</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">How does a system learn from closed cases without losing its reproducibility?</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A new client arrives with their own systems. What may change in the system, and what may not?</p></li></ul><h3>What success looks like</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>6 months:</strong> Architecture decided. One real use case from the core business runs in production and is used daily. Your first engineers are hired.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>12 months:</strong> Several agentic use cases in regular operation. The control layer holds up in a real review, and evaluation runs against closed cases, not test data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>24 months:</strong> Automation is a capability of the organization, not of individuals. Every acquired firm runs on the same base, and your team ships without you in the room.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Where it leads:</strong> the full CTO mandate, a management career earned by contribution, not by years served.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>What you bring</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have built something that ran in production and was used by people who did not build it, as founding engineer, engineering lead, technical co-founder or in a comparable role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have taken agentic systems into production and know where they break.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have integrated against systems that fight back: legacy ERPs, banking backends, badly documented interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You write production code. AI is your everyday tool, and your position on the stack comes from what you built and threw away.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You work in German, because our clients and tax advisors do, and you build in person in Munich.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You learn from practitioners, and you set the highest standard in everything you ship, not because someone checks, but because mediocrity bothers you.</p></li></ul><h3>A plus, not a requirement</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A regulated field where mistakes have consequences: fintech, banking tech, payments (N26, Trade Republic, Solaris, Klarna, Mollie, Pleo) or software for professional services (Personio, Workato).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of accounting, tax or DATEV.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">No conventional CV required: a technical co-founder of a sold or failed product, or someone who can show publicly what they have built, is explicitly invited. We assess contribution, not labels. The salary range shown refers to the primary profile; a different background starts at a different market price and converges after twelve months of proven performance.</p></li></ul><h3>What this role is and what it isn't</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Building, not managing.</strong> You lead engineers and stay in the code. If you want to run managers, this is the wrong role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>An operating company, not a software vendor.</strong> The users are our own teams. IT operations, tool rollouts and the product work sit with Operations; what we build and in which order is decided together with management. You own how it is built and run.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In person in Munich, not a distributed team.</strong> An architecture being decided and a team finding its standards need a shared room.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h3>Why join us</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn our data into the edge.</strong> Decades of audited, completed work become the test every agent has to pass before a human sees its result.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leverage through acquisitions.</strong> Every firm that joins Vogel runs on what you build. One decision of yours reaches several thousand clients from day one, and more with every acquisition.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Yours to decide.</strong> The architecture and the stack of this layer are open. Hierarchical in decisions, flat in communication, autonomous in execution. Performance is celebrated, not hidden, without politics and without consensus theater.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Substance behind you.</strong> A profitable, growing business. No funding round decides whether your team exists.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">The FAQ below is in German, as is our working day.</p><h1><u>FAQ</u></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>1. Was ist Vogel – und wo arbeitet ihr?</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vogel ist eine der führenden Mittelstandsberatungen Deutschlands – seit 1959, inhabergeführt in zweiter Generation, mit eigenem Kapital – und baut daraus die führende Beratungsplattform für den Mittelstand. Wir arbeiten an drei Standorten: Aalen als gewachsenem Stammsitz, Bopfingen im Kerngeschäft und München als neuem Hub. An allen dreien suchen wir quer durch die Funktionen – von Steuerberatung über Beratung bis zu den Teams, die das Fundament darunter bauen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>2. Wie sind die Gehaltsbänder zu verstehen?</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bewusst breit – und an jeder Stelle ausgewiesen, bevor du dich bewirbst. Wir differenzieren nach Track Record und Marktwert, nicht nach Abschluss: knappe, stark gefragte Profile am oberen Ende, weniger knappe am unteren. Die ausgewiesene Spanne ist kein Verhandlungsspielraum, sondern eine Profil-Skala – zwei Menschen mit ähnlicher Erfahrung können bei uns unterschiedlich verdienen. Was das obere Ende bestimmt, ist der Reifegrad, nicht die Zahl der Berufsjahre und nicht das Verhandlungsgeschick.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>3. Wie viel – und wie – wird bei Vogel gearbeitet?</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gemessen wird an dem, was du bewegst, nicht an Stunden. Ehrlich ist aber auch: Wer 9-to-5 sucht, ist bei uns nicht die erste Adresse. Wir suchen Menschen, die aus eigenem Antrieb intensiv arbeiten, weil die Aufgaben es wert sind. Wie du deine Zeit verteilst, ist weitgehend deine Sache. Was wir teilen: Wir arbeiten präsent zusammen und sehen uns im Normalfall täglich im Büro – Kultur, Sparring und die besten Ideen entstehen in der täglichen Nähe. Wir sind keine Remote-Company und haben keine großen Home-Office-Policies; einzelne Remote-Tage sind kein Problem.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>4. Wie läuft die Bewerbung?</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Schlank, schnell, transparent – und nach Profil gestaffelt. In der Regel sind es vier Schritte: eine schriftliche Aufgabe, in der du zu acht Fragen Position beziehst – KI ist ausdrücklich erlaubt, wir bitten nur um eine kurze Selbstauskunft dazu; ein Gespräch von einer halben Stunde; eine gemeinsame Arbeitssitzung an einem echten Problem aus unserem Alltag; und ein Termin vor Ort mit dem Team und gemeinsamem Essen. Wie viele Schritte es tatsächlich werden, hängt von der Rolle ab: Bei Praktikum und Werkstudium fällt der Vor-Ort-Termin weg, für Schülerjobs genügt ein Gespräch, bei Senior-Rollen kommt ein gemeinsamer Arbeitsnachmittag dazu. Vorab kannst du einen Zehn-Minuten-Call buchen, in dem nur du fragst. In der Regel hörst du nach jedem Schritt innerhalb von 48 Stunden von uns.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>5. Wie funktioniert die variable Vergütung?</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Quartalsweise an Leistung gekoppelt, qualitativ bewertet. Die Skala steigt mit dem Level: bis 20 % Associate, 27,5 % Manager, 35 % Senior Manager, 42,5 % Director, 50 % VP. Erwartungswert bei guter Leistung – du erfüllst die Anforderungen, setzt eigene Akzente, bestehst den Keeper Test – liegt bei rund 50 % des Maximums; der Maximalbonus ist nicht der Normalfall. Im Fokus steht eine ganzheitliche Beurteilung durch deine Führungskraft anhand von sechs Kriterien: Impact, Judgement, Communication, Execution, Growth und Values.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>6. Wie entwickle ich mich – welche Karrierewege gibt es?</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Zwei aktive Wege: die IC-Karriere (fachliche Tiefe, Expertenlaufbahn) über die Stufen Expert, Senior, Lead und Principal – und die Management-Karriere (Führung, Personalverantwortung) über Manager, Senior Manager, Director und VP. Beide werden gleich vergütet, und beide müssen nicht nach oben führen: Wer auf einer Stufe bleibt und dort weiter in die Tiefe geht, ist bei uns genauso richtig. Die Richtung wählst du nach dem Onboarding, meist in Jahr 1–3. Berufseinstieg ist kein Sonderweg, sondern der frühe Teil derselben Strecke – vom Werkstudenten oder Praktikanten zum Associate, für die Besten ohne erneutes Bewerbungsverfahren.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>7. Team, Kultur, Urlaub?</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Das gemeinsame Mittagessen ist der tägliche Ankerpunkt – wer im Büro ist, isst mit; erwartet, nicht kontrolliert. Das Abendessen ist dasselbe Angebot ohne jede Erwartung. Beides ohne Eigenanteil. Dazu Social Events und Offsites in regelmäßigem Rhythmus – nicht als Pflichtprogramm, sondern weil ein gutes Team auch abseits der Arbeit Zeit teilt.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Benefits sind bei uns nicht das Sahnehäubchen, sondern das, was Intensität über Jahre tragbar macht: Examensförderung mit 25.000 EUR Qualifizierungsbudget und drei Monaten Freistellung, 100-prozentige Übernahme der Kinderbetreuung, EGYM Wellpass, betriebliche Altersvorsorge, Job-Ticket mit 90 % Zuschuss, Homeoffice-Ausstattung und ein Gerät deiner Wahl aus unserem Katalog, ein Buch im Monat aus dem Vogel-Kanon – und KI-Tools ohne Token-Limit und ohne Budgetdeckel. Urlaub: 28 Tage.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><hr><p>Compensation: €156K – €205K • Offers Equity • €55K – €60K Bonus</p><ul><li>5+ Years of Experience (Full-Time) • Fix €156K – €205K • Offers Equity • €55K – €60K Bonus</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/vogel/tech-lead-cto-munchen-376478","tags":["Vogel"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"München","created_at":1794616814},{"slug":"data-engineer-merchant-intelligence-agent-munich-364148","company_name":"Constructor","title":"Data Engineer: Merchant Intelligence Agent","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Launched in 2019, Constructor is an AI-first e-commerce search and discovery platform that helps shoppers find the right products at the right time and enables leading global e-commerce brands to drive meaningful revenue and conversion gains.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We build the AI agent that helps merchandisers, product managers, and executives grow their e-commerce business: it finds opportunities in their data, tailors insights to each person's role, and takes routine work off their plate by delivering answers where they already work. We are transforming how digital merchandising teams work: instead of digging through reports and configuring rules by hand, they ask in plain language, get answers grounded in their own data, and approve the changes the agent prepares. Customers already rely on the agent to save time and make better decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We own the agent end to end, from the first question a merchant asks to the answer they act on. We also own the analytics behind it: the pipelines and cubes for search, browse, and recommendation performance, and the metric definitions merchants rely on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That is why we build the agent and the Customer Dashboard as a platform that every Constructor team extends. We create the foundation that other teams build on: the agent framework, shared components, and infrastructure. On top of it, teams add their own data, tools, and skills, so the agent can answer questions in their domain and the dashboard can show their features without separate interfaces. Each new capability gives merchants more ways to grow their business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and own the batch pipelines and cubes behind dashboard analytics and agent insights</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Model shopper, trend, and benchmark data so the agent can find opportunities across the shopping journey</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape data for each role: a merchandiser's category, a product manager's funnel step, an executive's total</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own data quality and trust: freshness, monitoring, alerting, and metric definitions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with engineers, analysts, and product to find the data the agent is missing and turn merchant questions into data products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ship your data into the product: simple analytics UIs, and the agent skills, tools, and prompts that use it</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Must-have</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in Python and SQL (any dialect)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and maintaining batch data pipelines with Spark (PySpark)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with the big data stack: Databricks, ClickHouse and dbt</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with data modeling for analytics: aggregated tables and cubes that feed dashboards and APIs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with data quality and pipeline monitoring: freshness checks, alerting, incident response</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to prototype fast and pick the metrics that matter in e-commerce</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to translate business questions into technical requirements, and back</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communication with engineers and non-technical stakeholders</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Nice-to-have</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building frontend UIs, or willingness to work across the full stack to ship data into product features</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with pandas, NumPy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building AI agents: tools, skills, prompts, context, and evaluations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with real-time analytics: ClickHouse, Cube.js</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with AWS</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with statistics for experimentation (A/B tests)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏝️ Unlimited vacation, with a recommended minimum of 3 weeks per year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌎 Fully remote team: choose where you live</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🛋️ Work-from-home stipend to set up your home office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💻 Apple laptop for new employees</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🧑‍🎓 Annual training and development budget for every employee</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">👪 Maternity and paternity leave for qualified employees</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🧠 Smart colleagues who help you grow and make a meaningful impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💵 Base salary