ess"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany","created_at":1794606016},{"slug":"remote-solution-consulting-manager-286794","company_name":"Rillet","title":"Solution Consulting Manager","description":"<h1>What We Do</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rillet serves accounting and finance teams, the financial brains of their companies. Our job is to help them run the numbers with impossible speed, accuracy, and insight.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rillet is the Agentic ERP built for modern finance teams. We help companies automate the most critical parts of finance, from closing the books and recognizing revenue to consolidating entities and reporting to investors. More than 600 companies run on Rillet, including Mercor, Scribe, and Function Health, and we partner with leading accounting firms including EY and KPMG.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building in one of the largest software markets in the world, with the momentum to match. Rillet has raised more than $200M, is valued at $1B, and is backed by Sequoia, a16z, ICONIQ, Bain Capital Ventures, Oak HC/FT, and other leading investors. We’re using that backing to build the financial infrastructure for the next generation of companies and help every business run its numbers at the speed of AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who We Are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rillet’s pace is not for everyone. Intelligence is table stakes. To succeed here, you need extreme speed, agency, and flexibility.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The people who thrive at Rillet do not wait for assignments. They internalize the mission, design a strategy, and bring back results that are better, faster, and more creative than a manager could have asked for.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work revolves around our customers. The people who succeed here are energized by delivering what matters most, even when it was not part of the original plan.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rillet is built on deep accounting expertise, and it takes people from many disciplines to build a category-defining company. You do not need to be an accountant to thrive here. You do need to care deeply about the problems we solve and the impact our customers can create. Together, we combine the precision of accounting with the speed, creativity, and ambition of AI-native software to power the financial core of the world’s fastest-growing companies while redefining what finance teams should expect from their software.</p><h2><strong>The Role</strong><br /></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have grown quickly, and our Solution Consulting team is at the center of how prospects evaluate Rillet as their next ERP. We are looking for a Solution Consulting Manager to lead and scale that team.<br /><br />This is a player-coach role weighted heavily toward coaching. You will spend roughly <strong>25% of your time running your own sales cycles </strong>(staying sharp, credible and close to the customer and product) and roughly <strong>75% of your time coaching, mentoring and developing your team</strong>, primarily by riding shotgun on live deals and giving real-time feedback. You will also be a key voice in shaping the product and building the Solution Consulting infrastructure that lets the organization scale.<br /><br />You will work directly with the CEO, GTM leadership and the Product team.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong><br /></h2><h2><strong>Coach, mentor and develop the team (~75%)</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ride shotgun on deals. </strong>Join discovery calls, demos, technical validations and POCs to observe, step in when needed, and give specific, real-time feedback. Run tight pre-call prep and post-call debriefs so every deal is a learning opportunity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Raise the bar on craft. </strong>Coach Solution Consultants on discovery, value selling, storytelling, demo design, handling technical objections, and tailoring sandbox environments to each customer's use cases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow each person individually. </strong>Set clear expectations and development plans, give regular honest feedback, and help each Solution Consultant build deep product and accounting domain expertise and advance in their career.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hire and onboard. </strong>Recruit, interview and ramp new Solution Consultants, and build an onboarding program that gets them deal-ready quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner on deal strategy. </strong>Work with Account Executives and sales leadership to staff deals, pressure-test strategy on complex ERP evaluations, and keep technical wins on track.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Run your own sales cycles (~25%)</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remove technical objections. </strong>Take on strategic and complex opportunities, understanding the prospect's business requirements and existing technology stack, and clearly articulating how Rillet integrates and improves their processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deliver high-impact demos. </strong>Set up and tailor the sandbox environment, answer questions in real time, and act as the prospect's trusted consultant throughout the purchase process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Represent Rillet. </strong>Be the face of the company, applying high customer empathy and structured problem-solving to ensure every prospect interaction is excellent, including with finance and accounting leaders.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Inform product and build for scale</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be the voice of the prospect. </strong>Synthesize front-line feedback, objections, competitive intel and feature gaps from across the team, and bring it to founders and Product in close to real time, with clear patterns and prioritization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Influence the roadmap. </strong>Partner with Product on discovery, early feedback on new features, and how capabilities are positioned and demoed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build Solution Consulting infrastructure. </strong>Create the systems, playbooks and tools that help the team scale, such as discovery frameworks, demo standards and reusable assets, sandbox and demo-data templates, technical FAQs and objection libraries, POC and technical-validation processes, a deal-review cadence, and enablement and certification paths.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Measure what matters. </strong>Define and track team metrics (technical win rate, ramp time, deal coverage, cycle time) and use them to improve how the team operates.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years managing or formally mentoring pre-sales, solutions consulting or sales engineering teams, with a track record of developing people.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of industry accounting experience across areas such as revenue recognition, month-end close and multi-entity consolidation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years supporting complex ERP sales cycles with implementation and/or customer support for accounting or financial solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of the ecosystem of tools in the office of the CFO.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communicator who makes complex concepts easy to understand, and who can give direct, constructive feedback in the moment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building processes, enablement or tooling for a growing team, ideally in an early-stage, fast-moving environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thrives in a dynamic environment while keeping high attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CPA certification or having started your career in audit is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Note</strong>: All official Rillet recruiting communications will come from an @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://rillet.com">rillet.com</a> email address. If you’re contacted from another domain, please disregard the message and report it as spam.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Life at Rillet</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow with us.</strong> Take meaningful ownership, expand your scope, and make an impact as Rillet scales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive pay and meaningful equity.</strong> Be rewarded for the value you help create.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits that support you.</strong> We offer competitive benefits designed to support your health, wellbeing, time away from work, family, and long-term financial goals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Better together.</strong> We value collaboration, connection, and spending meaningful time together as a team. We regularly create opportunities to connect through team meals, events, and company gatherings.</p></li></ul><hr><p>Compensation: $210K – $320K • Offers Equity • Multiple Ranges</p><ul><li>Zone A • OTE $225K – $320K • Offers Equity</li><li>Zone B • OTE $210K – $290K • Offers Equity</li><li>Zone C • OTE $210K – $290K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/rillet/remote-solution-consulting-manager-286794","tags":["GTM"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1794606016},{"slug":"software-development-engineer-in-test-ii-navnative-mapbox-germany-325475","company_name":"Mapbox","title":"Software Development Engineer in Test II, NavNative","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Mapbox is the leading real-time location platform for a new generation of location-aware businesses. Mapbox is the only platform that equips organizations with the full set of tools to power the navigation of people, packages, and vehicles everywhere. More than 4 million registered developers have chosen Mapbox because of the platform’s flexibility, security and privacy compliance. Organizations use Mapbox applications, data, SDKs and APIs to create customized and immersive experiences that delight their customers. </p><h2><strong>What We Do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Navigation Native team builds the high-performance C++ engine that serves as the "brain" of our Navigation SDKs. This library runs directly on end-user systems (on-board), powering everything from mobile apps to in-vehicle infotainment systems for partners like BMW, Porsche, and Zeekr.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We solve the fundamental challenges of movement: transforming noisy GPS/IMU data into precise map-matching, managing complex road-network graphs, supporting routes and alternatives, tracking progress along a route, and providing "Electronic Horizon" capabilities for ADAS. Our work happens at the edge, supporting location frequencies up to 10Hz and ensuring a seamless experience even in tunnels or dense urban canyons.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As AI becomes embedded in modern engineering workflows, we value engineers who can thoughtfully integrate AI into design, development, and decision-making. Our interview process will include discussion of how you use AI in your engineering workflow.<br /></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for smart, fast-learning engineers who care as much about proving that navigation works as about making it work. As an SDE(T), you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain the unit, integration, and functional test architecture for a C++17 library, and the CMake and CI pipelines that run it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn real-world location recordings into regression tests, and define the quality metrics for map-matching, routing, and route-following.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the quality signal fast and trustworthy: eliminate flaky tests, run sanitizer and performance builds, and track coverage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build AI-driven test tooling: agent-based test generation, automated dogfooding and triage, and AI-assisted PR review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with feature engineers on testability and review designs for how they will be verified.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thoughtfully leverage AI tools in your workflow and set the standard for how the team uses them. </p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We Believe Are Important Traits for This Role</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> 5+ years of experience in C++17: comfortable writing test code and tooling, reading production code, and debugging with sanitizers and profilers. Python or similar for harnesses and analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience building test infrastructure for a large native codebase: test frameworks, CMake, and CI systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A data-driven mindset: you define metrics, build the tooling to measure them, and use them to argue for or against a change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience diagnosing hard-to-reproduce failures: flakiness, platform-specific behavior, memory and threading bugs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong English skills, with the ability to explain test results, risk, and trade-offs to peers and stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Would be a Plus</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with navigation concepts (map matching, dead reckoning, route progress, or Electronic Horizon).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with replay- or simulation-based testing using real sensor and GPS data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience building AI- or agent-based developer tooling for testing, code review, or triage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with coverage tooling, performance benchmarking, or testing SDKs through generated bindings.</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>Employment Requirements</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full-time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Weekly Hours:</strong> 40 h per week</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location/Hybrid Policy:</strong> Remote (from any city in Germany)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We Value</h2></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">In addition to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.mapbox.com/about/values/">our core values</a>, which are not unique to this position and are necessary for Mapbox leaders:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value high-performing creative individuals who dig into problems and opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe in individuals being their whole selves at work. We commit to this through supportive health care, parental leave, flexibility for the things that come up in life, and innovating on how we think about supporting our people.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We emphasize an environment of teaching and learning to equip employees with the tools needed to be successful in their function and the company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We strongly believe in the value of growing a diverse team and encourage people of all backgrounds, genders, ethnicities, abilities, and sexual orientations to apply.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How We Support You</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hybrid/Remote Options: </strong>Enjoy flexibility to work comfortably from home or periodically from an office where applicable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Country-Specific Care &amp; Coverage: </strong>Private health, dental, and income protection plans tailored to elevate your regional statutory benefits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Family-First Support:</strong> Family care, maternity and paternity leave policies to support your growing family.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lifestyle Spending Account: </strong>Contributions to support your health, wellness, and personal growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Balance &amp; Brainpower: </strong>Mental health support for you and your dependents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Rest &amp; Recharge:</strong> Paid time away, company holidays, and generous absence policies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time Off to Give Back: </strong>Dedicated paid volunteering time in addition to your standard PTO.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By applying for this position, you acknowledge that you have received the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.mapbox.com/legal/applicant-privacy-notice/">Mapbox Non-US Privacy Notice</a> for applicants, which is linked here.  Completing this application requires you to provide personal data, such as your name and contact information, which is mandatory for Mapbox to process your application. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We are committed to