ranslate operational needs into scalable, standard-first enterprise solutions.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Team Lead Functional Analyst, you will act as the <strong>Chapter Lead</strong> for Functional Analysis, providing both disciplinary leadership and methodological governance for your team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your responsibilities include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Leadership &amp; Development:</strong> Providing horizontal leadership to the Functional Analyst team, overseeing personal skill development, coaching, and managing capacity allocation across various value streams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Methodology &amp; Standards:</strong> Setting and enforcing best-practice methodology standards for the chapter, including process modeling (BPMN 2.0), agile requirements engineering, user story writing (Jira/Confluence), and User Acceptance Testing (UAT) protocols.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategic Governance:</strong> Empowering your team to act as "The Bridge" that effectively translates business pain points into structured functional specification documents (FSDs) while strictly enforcing Fit-to-Standard and Clean Core principles to prevent unnecessary custom complexity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration:</strong> Partnering seamlessly with Business Product Owners (who prioritize the "WHAT &amp; WHY"), SAP Consultants (The Solution), Solution Architects (The Gatekeepers), and App Engineers (The Build) to ensure a unified end-to-end delivery lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Process Integrity:</strong> Ensuring your team upholds strict Segregation of Duties (SoD) guidelines and four-pillar controls during process design (e.g., keeping functional analysis strictly separated from 