ake the call when full consensus isn’t possible, and focus everyone on what is truly urgent</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Own delivery: keep the teams focused on their promise dates, get them to the finish line and course-correct fast. Use modern metrics to track progress and speed</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Stay close to the tech: pair with engineers, review work, join technical discussions, and challenge estimates and trade-offs</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Drive AI adoption across engineering with fellow Engineering Managers (tools, workflows, review standards and measuring real impact), starting in your own teams</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Drive hiring and take care of your people and their growth through regular 1:1s, honest feedback and by evolving our engineering leveling matrix</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Connect product, design and engineering, keep stakeholders informed early, and work with engineering leadership on cross-team strategy</span></p></li></ul> <br> <h3><strong>Requirements:</strong></h3><ul><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Substantial experience as an Engineering Manager, with a track record of delivering business outcomes. You’re accountable for results, not only team happiness, and comfortable owning and reporting engineering metrics</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">A software engineering background with a strong foothold in at least one of our stacks: Angular/TypeScript, PHP/Symfony or Kotlin/Spring. You don’t need all three, but you can challenge solutions and form an objective view of your teams’ work, even if you don’t code day to day</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Experience driving or shaping AI adoption in engineering teams, or a strong focus on it</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">High self-organization and drive: you spot what’s urgent among many important topics and act on it without waiting to be told</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">The ability to flex between hands-on support, decisive action and department-level thinking</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Fast, documented decision-making and direct, transparent communication</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Fluent English</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#1D1C1D">Nice to have</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">German (a big plus)</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Experience with customer-facing products or e-commerce</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Experience building or scaling teams, or evolving career frameworks</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong>Location:</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Berlin</p></li><li><p>Hybrid model (Must be willing to work from the office at least 1 day per week)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong>Purpose, a great company culture and incredible benefits - what to expect at rebuy:</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Work with a friendly team that is passionate about circularity and wants to make the world a little more sustainable, one transaction at a time.</p></li><li><p>Feel comfortable in an environment where independence and new ideas are welcome.</p></li><li><p>Benefit from flat hierarchies and the greatest possible transparency so that things don't take longer than they have to and you always feel well informed.</p></li><li><p>Enjoy our centrally located office in Berlin (Erkelenzdamm 11 - 13, 10999 Berlin).</p></li><li><p>Benefit from our family-friendly, flexible environment and paid child sick leave.</p></li><li><p>Bring your dog to the office: we love animals and want to cuddle yours, too!</p></li><li><p>Use employee discounts on <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.rebuy.de/">rebuy.de</a>, sustainable products at <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.futureb