&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics is a leading global sports platform redefining how fans connect with the teams, players and moments they love. Our businesses — Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, Fanatics Events, Fanatics Advertising, Fanatics Markets and Fanatics Studios — maximize the presence and reach for hundreds of partners globally and create a one-stop experience that allows fans to buy, bet, collect, and earn, while engaging with sports in deeper, more immersive ways. This includes licensed fan gear and lifestyle products, sportsbook and iGaming, physical and digital trading cards, live events, premium sports entertainment content, credit card offerings and more. Together, they form a powerful, integrated ecosystem — connected by the Fanatics ONE loyalty program and FanCash, the currency of sport — delivering personalized experiences to over 100 million fans worldwide. Fanatics holds partnerships with over 900 sports properties, from professional leagues and players’ associations to teams, colleges and retail partners; over 7,000 athletes and celebrities; and over 2,000 retail locations, including all Lids stores. Backed by a team of more than 22,000 employees, Fanatics is committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Product Manager, Trading Product&lt;/strong&gt; at Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming (FBG), you’ll support the development and delivery of key features that power our pre-match and in-play betting experiences. You’ll work closely with product, trading, and engineering teams to improve how we manage and price markets - helping ensure a fast, reliable, and competitive offering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a great opportunity for a product manager with strong collaboration skills, a passion for sports, and a desire to work on impactful, customer-facing features that directly influence what users see and bet on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the scoping and delivery of new trading product features and enhancements, helping manage a multi-team roadmap&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear product requirements and partner with engineering to deliver high-quality features efficiently&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with traders, risk teams, and operations to understand workflows and identify pain points&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor product and market performance to identify trends, flag issues, and recommend improvements&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data and customer insights to support prioritization and validate feature impact post-launch&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct research on competitor offerings and industry trends to ensure strong market positioning&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate updates, decisions, and outcomes clearly to stakeholders across the business&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1–3 years of product management or sports trading experience&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of sports — particularly how fans engage with live events and betting&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills; ability to clearly convey product ideas, specs, and decisions to a wide range of stakeholders.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with engineers, analysts, and operational users to deliver cross-functional solutions&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset and comfort using data to guide product decisions&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using AI tools to support product research, analysis, requirements writing and prototyping, with sound judgement on when to use them and how to validate their outputs.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, team-first mindset and strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-LS2&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ranges will change based on country and state of residence, which are reflected in Geographical Zones defined by Fanatics Betting and Gaming. The range incorporates all of our Geographical Compensation Zones and is subject to change as the Zone associated with the actual offer is confirmed. In addition to the base and bonus, full-time employment, and more. For information about our benefits, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&quot;&gt;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£40,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£50,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our &lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a -----
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/fanaticsfbg/product-manager-trading-product-leeds-london-493139","tags":["Gaming - Product"],"job_types":[],"location":"Leeds; London","created_at":1794682517},{"slug":"client-complaint-senior-analyst-london-hybrid-28639","company_name":"Clearbank","title":"Client Complaint Senior Analyst","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Trust unlocks our greatest potential.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For decades, the clearing of payments remained unchanged and unchallenged. We asked, what if there was a better way? What if we could make banking infrastructure faster, safer, more reliable, and easier to access for all? Here is where you can think radically and responsibly to find the best solution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What happens when you know you’re inherently trusted? Trust creates safety. Safety encourages you to be brave, to challenge, to fail, to try new things and to execute. At ClearBank everything revolves around trust. We’re not expected to earn it, but we are expected not to break it. We’re trusted to own it. To solve issues in the moment. To know a good risk when we see one, and the judgement to know that ‘can’ doesn’t always mean you ‘should’</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you can expect:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClearBank is a place where you can do things differently and challenge the status quo. We will give you a high level of autonomy and transparency, and we trust you to make the right decisions for the bank.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If that excites you, how about joining our Client Services team as a <strong>Client Complaint Senior Analyst?</strong> Reporting to the Associate Director, Client Support you will take independent ownership of client complaints, using your judgement and complaints expertise to resolve non-routine cases fairly, effectively and within relevant requirements. You will support consistently high standards across complaint handling by identifying themes and improvements, sharing your knowledge and providing direct line management, day-to-day support and coaching to the Complaint Analyst.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your role includes:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Independently manage client complaints from receipt through to resolution, applying sound judgement to deliver fair, timely and well-evidenced outcomes in line with complaint handling standards, relevant requirements and internal policies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Investigate non-routine complaints, bringing together information from systems, teams and stakeholders to establish root cause, reach appropriate conclusions and identify when complex matters require escalation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce clear, accurate and customer-focused written responses, ensuring decisions and outcomes are appropriately supported and communicated</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify recurring complaint themes, risks and root causes, using insight from cases to suggest practical improvements to customer outcomes, service quality and complaint management processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take direct line management responsibility for the Client Complaint Analyst, setting clear objectives, holding regular one-to-ones, providing feedback and coaching, and supporting their onboarding, performance and development</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share complaints knowledge and best practice across the team while continuing to manage your own complaint caseload</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support consistent complaint handling standards across the team by providing guidance on day-to-day cases and constructively challenging where an approach may not achieve the right outcome</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build trusted relationships across Client Services, Financial Crime, Operations, Product and other relevant teams to resolve issues and support improvements that benefit customers and the Bank</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To excel in this role, you’ll also need:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong working knowledge of complaint handling in a customer service, financial services, operations or regulated environment, with the ability to apply relevant processes, policies and controls independently</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical and problem-solving capability, including the ability to investigate non-routine issues, assess evidence, identify root causes and reach well-reasoned conclusions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sound judgement, with the confidence to make day-to-day decisions independently and recognise when a more complex or higher-risk matter should be escalated</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain complex matters clearly and produce high-quality customer communications</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organisational skills and the ability to manage varied complaint activity and competing priorities while maintaining quality and timeliness</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative approach, with the ability to line manage the Complaints Analysts, set clear expectations, provide constructive feedback and coaching, and support their performance and development</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity and a continuous-improvement mindset, with the confidence to identify problems, challenge constructively and suggest better ways of working</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What makes a great ClearBank team member? Does this sound like you?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You focus on solutions and positive outcomes, thinking radically and responsibly to find the best result for our customers, your colleagues and the bank;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You actively seek feedback from others to drive your growth and development, always assuming positive intent from others and develop strong, trusting relationships you’re your colleagues and customers: you really, genuinely care;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You always strive for the highest quality, but you know that done is better than perfect; you welcome a challenge knowing that they learn as you go and iterate;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">‘I’ before ’we’, isn’t in your vocabulary.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regretfully we are not able to sponsor applicants for immigration purposes at the current time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer in return:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're flexible – We support a culture of flexibility which allows our employees to achieve a strong work-life balance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offices – Work in a way that works for you – whether that’s in the London office, at home, or hybrid.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Holiday – 27 days of annual leave per year, plus bank holidays.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Holiday buy/sell - Buy or sell up to five days of annual leave each year and shape your year around what matters most.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work abroad – You have the flexibility to work outside of the UK for up to 30 days in a rolling 12-month period.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Socials – Regular social events open to all.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Holiday swap – Option to swap your bank holidays to any other day of your choice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wellbeing – 24/7 employee assistance programme including mental health support, life assurance and income protection.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bigger than ClearBank – Take a couple of days per year to do something that matters to you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Healthy living – Private healthcare and discounted dental cover, with employee perks and discounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Family – Enhanced family-friendly leave.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Personal development – We offer personal development budgets, opportunities to take part in role-related training and unlimited LinkedIn Learning.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">And not forgetting the biggest benefit of all. The opportunity to be part of an incredible team that’s building a tech-bank fit for the future.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A little bit more about us!</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ClearBank is Where You Can belong:</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At ClearBank we think about Diversity, Equity and Inclusion (DE&amp;I) a lot. Not because we think we should. But because we know we should – how else can we build a happy workforce and be successful as a business. We’re committed to making sure our teams reflect society. And we put energy and effort into making this a place where everyone feels at home, where they’re given the trust and encouragement to do their very best work. Here are some of the things we’re most proud of: </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">42% of our senior management roles are held by women </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our enhanced family leave policies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Launching our partnership with Code First Girls </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Increasing awareness of neurodiversity in the workplace through our partnership with the Inclusive Group </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our hiring process and what you can expect:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application:</strong> a member of our talent acquisition team will review your application against the key requirements for the role and let you know within two weeks whether you’re moving forward to the next stage; </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Screening:</strong> You’ll spend 30-45 minutes speaking to one of our recruiters learning more about the role and ClearBank, and we’ll get it know more about you, your experience and how your skills align with the role (this will be via phone or Teams video call). You can expect to hear back from us within seven days following this meeting (if things are taking longer than expected, we’ll let you know that too); </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First Interview:</strong> You’ll spend one hour with a member of our hiring team focusing on your skills, competencies and your ways of working at the same time we’ll give you time to ask more questions about the role, the team and learn more about the ClearBank culture. This will be via Teams.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Second Interview:</strong> This will be a competency-based interview with one or more members of our team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final Stage: </strong>You will have a final meeting with the Head of Department. This will be around 45-60 minutes.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Offer:</strong> Congratulations! Get ready to transform banking forever! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our commitment to you as a candidate:</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We will always try our best to get back to you within seven days of your interview whether you’ve been successful or not and provide you with feedback. Sometimes things take a little longer, so we may not have a decision to share but we will get it touch to let you know we need a little more time.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re unable to provide specific individual feedback at the application or screening stage but know that your application was reviewed and considered carefully.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We wish you the best of luck with your application and maybe we’ll be celebrating your new role at ClearBank soon!  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal Opportunities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClearBank is committed to ensuring equal opportunities throughout every stage of the recruitment process. ClearBank recognises that diversity is vital to the long-term success of the business in the communities and markets in which it operates. ClearBank is also a firm believer that an inclusive culture fosters greater employee engagement and collaboration. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClearBank strives for diversity and inclusion of all forms, including (but not limited to): gender, age, educational and professional background, disability, gender reassignment, marital or civil partner status, pregnancy or maternity, race, colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin, religion or belief and sexual orientation. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As part of the Company’s commitment to equal employment opportunity, we provide reasonable adjustments, to candidates during the recruitment process, including to individuals with disabilities. We want to create a safe space that welcomes everyone so please let us know how we can accommodate you. In case you have any accessibility requirements you can share that with our Talent Acquisition team prior to your interview stage, if applicable. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The legal bit</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By submitting your CV to ClearBank Limited you are providing your consent for us to use the information you provide for recruitment purposes. For more information on how we manage your data go and check out our Candidate Privacy Notice on the ClearBank website to see how we process, manage and look after your data. You are also allowing us to communicate with you by email and telephone for recruitment purposes. </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/clearbank/client-complaint-senior-analyst-london-hybrid-28639","tags":["ClearBank Group Holdings"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London Office - Hybrid","created_at":1794681614},{"slug":"people-analytics-analyst-london-hybrid-16796","company_name":"Clearbank","title":"People Analytics Analyst","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>People Analytics Analyst</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClearBank is a technology-enabled bank built to help transform banking and payments. We combine banking expertise and technology to provide infrastructure that enables our clients to deliver innovative financial products and services. Our culture is founded on trust, accountability, learning, collaboration and the confidence to challenge established ways of working responsibly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We built ClearBank on the belief that banking infrastructure would no longer slow down progress. Instead, it would be a catalyst that unlocks the potential to innovate. It would adapt to different needs so a new era in financial services could begin. We’re here to challenge the status quo in banking, are you?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We all know that transforming banking forever is not an easy mission, but we’re more than ready to rise to that challenge. We all do it every day; navigating new, unexpected and sometimes even daunting challenges. But we believe in ourselves and trust we can do it. Want to innovate? Go for it. Push for a better way? You Can. If you think you have it in you, this is Where You Can.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reporting to our Head of People, as the People Analytics Analyst you will help the People Team make informed, evidence-led decisions by turning data into clear, accurate and actionable insight.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working across the People Team you will deliver reporting and analysis that supports organisational effectiveness, particularly focusing on Reward and People Operations among the wider team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will strengthen data quality, reporting controls and analytical capability across the People function, making insight easier to understand and use while protecting the confidentiality of employee information.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Produce</strong> regular and ad hoc people reporting that gives stakeholders a clear view of workforce trends, risks and opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Analyse</strong> data across the employee lifecycle, including workforce composition, recruitment, retention, progression, performance, absence, engagement and inclusion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Develop</strong> accessible dashboards, reports and visualisations that turn complex data into clear insights for People and business stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner</strong> with Reward to support pay benchmarking, reward reviews, pay-positioning analysis and other compensation-related activity through accurate data preparation and analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Maintain</strong> accurate and consistent people datasets, including clear data definitions, validation checks, reconciliation, documentation and version control.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Investigate</strong> data anomalies and work with People, Finance, Payroll and other stakeholders to resolve root causes and improve source-data quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support</strong> workforce planning and organisational analysis by identifying patterns, modelling scenarios and presenting evidence-based observations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Provide</strong> analytical support for People projects and recurring processes, ensuring outputs are accurate, timely and appropriate for their intended audience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Improve</strong> reporting processes through automation, standardisation and the reduction of unnecessary manual activity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Promote</strong> responsible use of people data by applying appropriate confidentiality, access, governance and quality controls.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What success looks like in the role:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stakeholders receive accurate, timely and decision-ready people insights that help them understand workforce priorities and take appropriate action.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Core People reporting is supported by clear definitions, effective controls and reliable data that stakeholders trust.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">People analytics increasingly covers the wider employee lifecycle, while Reward receives consistent and high-quality analytical support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recurring reports and processes become more efficient, scalable and easier to use through thoughtful automation and standardisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Complex findings are communicated clearly, with appropriate context, enabling stakeholders to understand both the evidence and its limitations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Skills &amp; Experience: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in people analytics, HR reporting, workforce analytics, business analysis or another data-focused role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical and numerical skills, including experience working with detailed or complex datasets. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to translate analysis into concise insights, clear visual outputs and practical recommendations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong Excel / Databricks capability, including formulas, data validation, reconciliation, data manipulation and structured analysis.  Use or advocacy of AI is welcome. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience producing recurring reports, dashboards or management information for different stakeholder groups.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong attention to detail and a consistent approach to checking, documenting and controlling analytical outputs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of data quality, confidentiality and the responsible handling of sensitive employee information.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to investigate anomalies, identify root causes and work collaboratively with others to resolve data issues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong planning and organisational skills, with the ability to manage recurring reporting alongside ad hoc analytical requests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communication and stakeholder-management skills, including the ability to explain analytical findings to non-technical audiences.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working within a People or HR function in a regulated organisation, financial-services business or technology company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with HR information systems, reporting platforms or data-visualisation tools. Notable;  Databricks. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting workforce planning, organisational design, employee-listening or inclusion analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to reward analytics, salary benchmarking, pay-review modelling or compensation data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience improving or automating reporting and data processes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ways of Working &amp; Culture</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Care like we mean it:</strong> Handle people data with care, respect and discretion, while producing insight that considers its impact on colleagues and the organisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build trust together:</strong> Take ownership of data quality and delivery, follow through on commitments, exercise sound judgement and raise risks or limitations early.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow with the challenge:</strong> Stay curious, seek feedback and build analytical capability while adapting to changing priorities and new questions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Succeed as one:</strong> Work collaboratively across People, Reward, Finance, Payroll and the wider business, engaging stakeholders early and focusing on shared outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clear a bold new path:</strong> Challenge inefficient reporting practices, test better approaches and build solutions that can scale as the organisation’s analytical needs evolve.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role Level: 2 </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>If this sounds like you then we encourage you to dust off that CV and apply!</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>*Please note that we are not currently able to sponsor applicants for immigration purposes.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A little bit more about us!</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ClearBank is Where You Can belong:</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At ClearBank we think about Diversity, Equity and Inclusion (DE&amp;I) a lot. Not because we think we should. But because we know we should – how else can we build a happy workforce and be successful as a business. We’re committed to making sure our teams reflect society. And we put energy and effort into making this a place where everyone feels at home, where they’re given the trust and encouragement to do their very best work. Here are some of the things we’re most proud of: </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">42% of our senior management roles are held by women </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our enhanced family leave policies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Launching our partnership with Code First Girls </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Increasing awareness of neurodiversity in the workplace through our partnership with the Inclusive Group </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our hiring process and what you can expect:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application:</strong> a member of our talent acquisition team will review your application against the key requirements for the role and let you know within two weeks whether you’re moving forward to the next stage; </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Screening:</strong> You’ll spend 30-45 minutes speaking to one of our recruiters learning more about the role and ClearBank, and we’ll get it know more about you, your experience and how your skills align with 