94681614},{"slug":"product-manager-london-159565","company_name":"Trainline","title":"Product Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Trainline, our purpose is to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.thetrainline.com/terms/sustainability-faqs">empower greener travel choices, connecting people and places.</a> Trainline enables millions of travellers to find and book the best value tickets across carriers, fares, and journey options through our highly rated mobile app, website, and B2B partner channels. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Great journeys start with Trainline 🚄 </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re Europe’s leading independent rail platform, helping millions of travellers find and book the best-value rail and coach journeys across our app, website and partner channels.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our job is to make the green travel choice the best choice. By building a better train travel experience, we help more people choose rail - creating a positive impact for customers, our business and the planet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a team of more than 1,000 Trainliners from over 50 nationalities, working across London, Paris, Barcelona, Milan, Edinburgh and Madrid. Now is a brilliant time to join us and help shape the future of travel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Introducing the Trainline Core Experience Team 👋</strong><br />The Core Experience team looks after how our customers find and book rail travel across the UK and Europe. Our work covers search, supply from carriers and the booking experience, all in service of our purpose of empowering greener travel choices and connecting people and places. We are a collaborative group who enjoy learning from our customers and from each other.<br /><br />This is a brand new role, created to own what happens once a customer has found the right journey and moves towards booking: reservation details, optional extras and payment. Because it sits so close to the point of purchase, it offers a direct line to customer experience and revenue, and plenty of room to grow. You will work alongside our Search team and the Supply and Payments platform teams, with colleagues in commercial, design, data and engineering, to make booking simple and reliable for customers in every market we serve.<br /><br /><strong>In this role as the Product Manager, Booking Conversion, you will...🚄</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the customer experience from the moment someone chooses a journey to a confirmed booking, setting clear goals for conversion (the share of customers who complete their booking) and revenue while enabling other teams with a stake in the journey.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run quick cycles of experimentation by forming hypotheses, testing ideas, learning from the results and iterating, while shaping a longer-term vision and roadmap for the booking journey.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use customer insight and data to understand where people hesitate or leave, and decide where to invest limited team capacity across each step of the journey.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a deep understanding of how rail works in different markets and with different carriers. Decide when a market or carrier specific improvement is the right investment, and when to bring ideas and learnings together across markets so that value grows for customers everywhere, rather than staying in one place.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Balance wider business goals from other teams, such as adding new supply, increasing booking features for each carrier, and introducing optional extras and new revenue streams, against keeping the journey simple and low in friction for customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with the Supply, Search, New Business, and Payments platform teams, alongside design, data and engineering, to align priorities and deliver improvements together.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate openly with a wide range of stakeholders, including commercial colleagues, explaining the reasoning behind decisions and sharing progress and results in a way that builds trust.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring AI tools into your everyday work, such as prototyping, analysis and delivery, and help the team grow in confidence using them.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We'd love to hear from you if you have...🔍</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience improving conversion in a digital booking, checkout or purchase journey, using data to spot opportunities and measure the impact of your changes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience designing and running experiments, and turning what you learn into the next set of improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A customer-first mindset, with the ability to combine customer insight and data to make confident decisions even when information is incomplete.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence setting direction for a product area, balancing near-term improvements with a longer-term vision.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear, thoughtful communication, with the ability to explain complex trade-offs and build alignment between teams who may have different priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort weighing limited capacity against competing demands, and explaining what you will focus on and why.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ideally, experience balancing local needs with a wider shared strategy, for example across several markets or with third-party suppliers. It is also helpful if you are familiar with travel, ticketing or payments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You may also be curious about AI tools and keen to use them to prototype ideas, analyse results and speed up delivery.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>More information:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enjoy fantastic perks like private healthcare &amp; dental insurance, a generous work from abroad policy, 2-for-1 share purchase plans, an EV Scheme to further reduce carbon emissions, extra festive time off, and excellent family-friendly benefits. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We prioritise career growth with clear career paths, transparent pay bands, personal learning budgets, and regular learning days. Jump on board and supercharge your career from day one! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're operating a hybrid model and ask that Trainliners work from the office a minimum of 60% of their time over a 12-week period. We also have a 28-day Work from Abroad policy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our values represent the things that matter most to us and what we live and breathe everyday, in everything we do: </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💭 <strong>Think Big</strong> - We're building the future of rail </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">✔️ <strong>Own It </strong>- We focus on every customer, partner and journey </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤝 <strong> Travel Together</strong> - We're one team </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">♻️<strong> Do Good</strong> - We make a positive impact </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We know that having a diverse team makes us better and helps us succeed. And we mean all forms of diversity - gender, ethnicity, sexuality, disability, nationality and diversity of thought. That's why we're committed to creating inclusive places to work, where everyone belongs and differences are valued and celebrated.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interested in finding out more about what it's like to work at Trainline? Why not check us out on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/trainline/">LinkedIn</a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/lifeattrainline/">Instagram</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.co.uk/Overview/Working-at-Trainline-EI_IE249203.11,20.htm">Glassdoor</a>! </p><hr><p>Compensation: £70K – £80K</p><ul><li> • Base Salary £70K – £80K</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/trainline/product-manager-london-159565","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794681613},{"slug":"member-of-technical-staff-simulated-universes-london-354193","company_name":"Ineffable","title":"Member of Technical Staff, Simulated Universes","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Our mission is <strong>to make first contact with superintelligence.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are creating a superlearner that discovers all knowledge from its own experience, from elementary motor skills through to profound intellectual breakthroughs. This superlearning capability - the ability to endlessly discover knowledge and skills, without relying on human data - will be driven by the world’s most powerful reinforcement learning algorithms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The superlearner is expected to rediscover and then transcend the greatest inventions in human history, such as language, science, mathematics and technology. If successful, this will represent a scientific breakthrough of comparable magnitude to Darwin: where his law explained all life, our law will explain and build all intelligence.<br /><br /><strong>Role brief</strong><br /><br />Intelligence cannot emerge in a void. It needs a place to grow and flourish. As a Simulated Universes Engineer, you’ll help us craft, shape and maintain the worlds in which superlearners can emerge and thrive. That means making those worlds accurate, reliable and intricate, and scaling them to unprecedented highs in terms of both parallelism and speed. It’s a challenging quest and one that’s critical to our mission.  In this role, you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build</strong> the engineering foundations of our new environments; designing, implementing and maintaining them as they grow</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner</strong> closely with the team creating the blueprints for the worlds we need to build</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Close the loop</strong> between blueprint and build, enabling fast, iterative research cycles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scale</strong> the environments up, while utilising state-of-the-art hardware<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About you</strong><br /><br />You’re an engineer with a passion for creating artificial worlds, and you know what it takes to make them emerge at scale. You may be a good fit if you:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring industry experience with large-scale simulations</strong>, whether in demanding scientific domains or in the games industry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Know how to build systems like huge distributed MMOs </strong>that rely on world parallelism, large-scale physics engines, or logic that preserves consistency despite decentralised computation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn ambitious research visions into reality</strong> by designing, building and maintaining codebases that support fast research iteration and efficient execution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enjoy working closely with researchers</strong> and/or "designers", taking their blueprints and turning them into worlds that agents can explore and learn</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">On the pure engineering side, you’ll likely have experience with the following:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Physics engines</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">GPU-accelerated physics and simulation frameworks, such as NVIDIA Warp</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lower level languages such as Rust, C or C++</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implementation of distributed server-client architectures</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Writing efficient GPU code</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We move fast, give people real ownership and trust engineers to make good judgment calls. We are a team that cares as much about doing this well as doing it fast.<br /><br />If you're interested in joining Ineffable and think your skills would be better suited to a different position please explore the careers page for other opportunities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/ineffable/member-of-technical-staff-simulated-universes-london-354193","tags":["Technical Staff"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794681613},{"slug":"executive-assistant-chief-product-officer-chief-technology-officer-london-451133","company_name":"Accurx","title":"Executive Assistant - Chief Product Officer & Chief Technology Officer","description":"<h2><strong>Accurx is solving healthcare productivity for the NHS</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">For decades, the NHS has struggled with fragmented systems that make simple tasks feel impossible. At Accurx, we’re changing that by building a single, system-wide platform that helps every patient get gold-standard, efficient, and joined-up care.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What started as a way for GPs to text a patient, has now evolved into an all-in-one digital toolkit used by 98% of GP practices and 68% (and growing!) of NHS Trusts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our platform now powers<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.accurx.com/primary-care"><u> </u><strong><u>Total Triage</u></strong></a><strong> </strong>to manage patient demand, and<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.accurx.com/booking"><u> </u><strong><u>Self-Book</u></strong></a><strong> </strong>that lets patients schedule their own appointments in seconds. We’ve automated routine care with<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.accurx.com/questionnaires"><u> </u><strong><u>Patient Questionnaires</u></strong></a> for long-term conditions, while<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.accurx.com/accumail"><u> </u><strong><u>Accumail</u></strong></a> finally allows staff-to-staff communication to happen instantly across different care settings. We’re now pushing the boundaries of the consultation itself with<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.accurx.com/scribe"><u> </u><strong><u>Accurx Scribe</u></strong></a>, our AI-powered note-taker that drafts medical notes in real-time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re not just shipping features. We’re giving clinicians their time back and ensuring every patient journey is as smooth as it should be.</p><h2><br /><strong>How you'll empower our tech and product leadership</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You be a strategic partner and a vital force multiplier for our Chief Product Officer, Tom (CPrO) and incoming Chief Technology Officer (CTO). By anticipating their needs, shaping their organisational engagement, and prioritising their diaries against company objectives, you will help turn their strategic vision into real momentum across the Product &amp; Technology teams.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Owning the operating rhythm:</strong> You will proactively manage the executives' time and diaries, utilising your knowledge of Product Development Lifecycles and Engineering to effectively balance urgent requests with important strategic priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Driving strategic communications:</strong> You will draft, shape, and constructively challenge key messaging from the executives, ensuring communications are clear, consistent, and land successfully with various audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preparing with a point of view:</strong> You will go beyond basic preparation by synthesising information, highlighting crucial details, and recommending decisions ahead of key meetings and board sessions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Being the ear to the ground:</strong> You will stay attuned to team sentiment and blockers across Product &amp; Technology, bringing insights to the executives early and advising on the best response.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fostering an AI-native culture:</strong> You will partner with the executives and other Executive Assistants to design impactful cultural moments, such as hackathons and Town Hall meetings, ensuring momentum continues long after the events conclude.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Running the Product &amp; Tech engine:</strong> You will oversee logistics for the Product &amp; Tech Leadership forum, manage fast-changing schedules, and monitor asynchronous Slack conversations to highlight matters needing executive attention.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Delivering impactful projects and events:</strong> You will own and run projects on behalf of the executives from planning to delivery, while also managing the logistics for internal and external events, offsites, and team socials.</p></