tomer data profiles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create intelligent testing agents that simulate real user behavior to validate different configuration combinations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and maintain GitHub workflows and actions to automate testing, deployment, and validation processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage and optimize Helm charts for deployment consistency across environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement and maintain ArgoCD workflows for continuous deployment and environment management</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish best practices for testing methodologies and ensure adoption across engineering teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build scalable infrastructure that supports parallel test execution across diverse configurations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop infrastructure-as-code templates and configurations for reproducible test environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement containerization strategies for test environments and dependencies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create benchmarking frameworks to measure performance and reliability across different configurations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor and improve test coverage and reliability metrics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with product and engineering teams to understand testing requirements and translate them into automated solutions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Troubleshoot and resolve complex testing infrastructure issues<br /></p></li></ul><h2>Required Qualifications</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of software engineering experience with a focus on automation and testing infrastructure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expert proficiency in Python and TypeScript</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extensive experience with GitHub workflows and actions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of testing methodologies and best practices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and maintaining CI/CD pipelines</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Containerization experience (Docker, Kubernetes)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Benchmarking experience and performance testing methodologies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cloud platform experience (AWS, GCP, or Azure)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in developer tools or platform engineering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to design and implement complex automation systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail<br /></p></li></ul><h2>Preferred Qualifications</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with LLMs in production environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with infrastructure-as-code principles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with container orchestration and management</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of performance testing tools and frameworks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with monitoring and observability tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in test framework development</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong working knowledge of Helm charts and ArgoCD</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Infrastructure-as-code experience (Terraform, Pulumi, or similar)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You'll Build</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll enhance our testing platform to allow engineers to:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spin up environments with specific feature flag combinations using infrastructure-as-code</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Load test configurations with realistic customer data volumes in containerized environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run comprehensive test suites across multiple environment configurations with automated benchmarking</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generate detailed performance and reliability reports across different cloud environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Automatically detect and flag regressions in diverse usage scenarios</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scale testing infrastructure to accommodate our growing customer base<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a critical role for ensuring the reliability and scalability of our North platform as we continue to grow our customer base and expand our feature set. You'll have the opportunity to shape the future of our development infrastructure and make a significant impact on product quality. (edited)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Full-Time Employees at Cohere enjoy these Perks:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A weekly lunch stipend of $75/£75 or equivalent in your local currency for lunch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full health and dental benefits, including a separate budget for mental health.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">RRSP matching, 401K, Pension Scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">100% Parental Leave top-up for up to 6 months, for either parent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Annual enrichment benefits:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Arts &amp; culture, fitness/wellness, quality time, and a workspace improvement credit.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Education &amp; learning stipend for conferences, courses, and coaching.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">6 weeks of paid vacation (30 working days!)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Budget for traveling to other offices if you are remote, plus an annual company offsite.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>How and Where We Work:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cohere is remote-friendly, but we also have offices in Toronto, London, New York City, San Francisco, Montreal, Paris, Berlin and Seoul with more opening soon.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">For those in the office: a daily lunch program, plenty of snacks, and regular community and social events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">For those not near an office: a co-working benefit so you can work alongside others in your city.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everyone receives a $500 home office stipend to set up your workspace properly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If any of the above doesn’t line up exactly with your experience, we still encourage you to apply. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We strive to create an inclusive work environment for all; we welcome applicants from all backgrounds and are committed to providing equal opportunities. Should you require any accommodations during the recruitment process, please submit an<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/12a6IrLdF3kI2nonKSr4tiFuz18rLQbaeYV-JM9L4o9Q/edit"> Accommodations Request Form</a>, and we will work together to meet your needs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We may use AI-enabled tools to screen and assess applicants against the criteria for this position. This helps our recruiters identify potentially qualified candidates, but it doesn't limit the applications our recruiters may review or consider.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Beware of Scams: Cohere will never ask for payment or third-party services (e.g., CV writing) as part of our hiring process. All legitimate roles are listed on the Cohere careers page and LinkedIn only, with all communications from Cohere employees coming from an ----- or ----- email alias. If jobs are viewed on other sites then please verify these through our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://cohere.com/careers"><em>official careers</em></a><em> page.</em></p><hr><p>Compensation: $185K – $300K • Offers Equity • Multiple Ranges</p><ul><li>USA - California, New York and Washington • Base Salary $215K – $300K • Offers Equity</li><li>USA - All Other States • Base Salary $185K – $275K • Offers Equity</li><li>Canada • Base Salary CA$275K – CA$360K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/cohere/senior-staff-software-engineer-developer-experience-london-400311","tags":["Engineering & Infra"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794681612},{"slug":"regional-director-client-engagement-london-294999","company_name":"9Fin","title":"Regional Director, Client Engagement","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About 9fin</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">9fin is the AI platform powering global debt markets — the world’s largest asset class at over $145 trillion.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Debt markets are vast, global, and mission-critical, yet still run on fragmented data, PDFs, and manual workflows. 9fin replaces this broken infrastructure with a single platform that centralises proprietary credit data, deep analysis, and high-value workflows across global markets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, 9fin powers teams at 300+ blue-chip institutions worldwide, including global banks, asset managers, private equity firms, law firms, and advisors. The business is scaling at exceptional speed, with rapid expansion in the US and best-in-class retention driven by deep workflow adoption.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re at a defining inflection point. With proven product-market fit and strong, global market pull, 9fin is accelerating toward becoming the category-defining platform for debt markets worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>The Opportunity</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">9fin is the AI platform powering global debt markets, the world’s largest asset class at over $145 trillion. Debt markets are vast, global and mission-critical, yet still run on fragmented data, PDFs and manual workflows. 9fin replaces this with a single platform that centralises proprietary credit data, deep analysis and high-value workflows across global markets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, 9fin powers teams at 350+ blue-chip institutions worldwide, including global banks, asset managers, private equity firms, law firms and advisors. The business is scaling at exceptional speed, with rapid expansion in the US and best-in-class retention driven by deep workflow adoption.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are bringing Client Engagement together as a single global function under our Global Head of Client Engagement. We are hiring Regional Directors to lead it on the ground. You will own retention, adoption and growth for your region (EMEA or the Americas), lead a team of Client Engagement Managers across a tiered coverage model, and turn client insight into action across the business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a role for a proven CS or AM leader who wants to scale a function. You will inherit a strong foundation, shape the next stage, and be accountable for commercial outcomes: gross and net revenue retention, product adoption, and the health of our most important client relationships.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You’ll Work On</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every day is different, but here is the kind of work you will lead:</p><h3><strong>Leadership &amp; Team Development</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead, coach and develop a regional team of Strategic CEMs, Senior CEMs and Client Engagement Managers across the whole region, and the managers beneath you as the team grows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run a tiered coverage model: Strategic CSMs for our most important accounts, Senior CSMs for key accounts, and CSMs for the wider base. Define clear roles, service levels and career paths at each level.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hire, onboard and train to a rapid growth plan, with a strong bench of internal successors.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Retention, Adoption &amp; Growth</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own regional gross revenue retention (GRR), with clear early-warning signals and remediation plans for at-risk accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive seat-level adoption: activate and re-activate users, build champion networks, and embed 9fin in each client’s daily workflow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead adoption of our newest products, including 9fin AI and Private 9fin, with client-specific programmes and measurable usage goals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design role and client-specific adoption metrics that forecast usage trends, so the team drives usage proactively.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Account Management and Relationship Managers on renewals and expansion, with clear ownership at each stage of the client lifecycle.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Strategy &amp; Operating Model</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate the global Client Engagement strategy into a regional plan, with the playbooks, success plans and lifecycle programmes to execute it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use health scoring and usage data to decide where the team spends its time, and to move accounts between coverage tiers as their needs change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Report regularly on regional KPIs to global leadership: retention, adoption, health, renewals and expansion pipeline.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Voice of the Client</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent clients in conversations with Product, Engineering, Data and Editorial, backing requests with evidence such as the accounts affected, the ARR at stake and the workflow impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with our Forward Deployed team on strategic accounts, setting shared success criteria and feeding what you learn back into the product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build executive relationships with senior stakeholders at your region’s most important clients.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Operational Excellence</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use Salesforce, our analytics tools and client engagement platforms to make the team more proactive, with automation where it frees up time for high-value work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep playbooks, client communications and dashboards current, and create feedback loops that improve the client experience.</p></li></ul><h2>What Success Looks Like</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Within 3 months: a clear picture of your region’s accounts, risks and team, and a regional plan agreed with the Global Head of Client Engagement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Within 6 months: accounts assigned and covered under the tiered model, with health scoring in use and a visible improvement in early-warning response.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Within 12 months: measurable gains in regional retention, adoption and AI and Private 9fin usage, and a team with the capacity and leadership depth to keep scaling.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role will be a great fit if you have:</p><h3><strong>Experience &amp; Expertise</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8+ years in Customer Success, Account Management or related client-facing roles in Capital Markets, Enterprise B2B SaaS or Financial Data, including 3+ years leading teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing AMs, CSMs, AEs or building the layer of leadership beneath you, ideally across more than one region or client segment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of scaling or structuring a CS or AM function through a period of fast growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of global financial markets, and credibility with buyside, sellside and advisory clients.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Commercial Acumen</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven success driving retention, adoption and expansion in enterprise accounts, ideally accountable for a portfolio of $50m in ARR.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort being measured on GRR, NRR and adoption, and designing the KPIs, dashboards and forecasting that support them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working alongside sales and account management on renewals and expansion, with clear ownership between teams.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Leadership &amp; Communication</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent people leadership: you coach, develop and hold a high bar for high-performing teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear written and verbal communication, with the ability to influence senior stakeholders both inside 9fin and at clients.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The judgement to prioritise competing demands and to use data to decide where the team focuses.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Bonus Points</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Existing relationships in the Leveraged Finance, Debt Capital Markets or Restructuring community.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a high-growth fintech or data provider, or with seat-based professional data products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience driving adoption of AI products or working with embedded or forward deployed teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with Salesforce, product analytics and client engagement platforms.</p></li></ul><h2>Why Join Us?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will join a fast-moving, ambitious team helping to power the largest financial market in the world. This role offers the chance to lead a regional Client Engagement team at a pivotal moment: with a clear global strategy, a product that clients rely on daily, and the mandate to shape how we retain and grow our client base for years to come.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a scaling start up, and we enjoy sharing our success, when the company succeeds, we always reinvest that in our people. We also offer huge amounts of responsibility, an abundance of opportunity for growth and a platform to truly excel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Financial &amp; Insurance</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Salary (our salary bands are benchmarked at the top end of the market)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension (your minimum contributions are 4% with 9fin matching up to 7%)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private Medical Insurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid sick leave with Income Protection for long periods of illness</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Group Life Assurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Season Ticket Loan &amp; Cycle to Work schemes</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time off</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 holiday days per year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Local public holidays (with the ability to exchange them for alternative days)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work abroad for up to 3 months a year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1 month paid sabbatical after 5 years of service</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhanced parental leave &amp; flexible working arrangements available</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth &amp; Culture</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional learning and development budget</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI experimentation budget of £800 (UK) per employee to trial AI tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Quarterly team socials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Summer and Winter company social events</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hybrid Policy</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">9fin is a hybrid company, and the office is a regular part of how we work. From January 2027, all employees will work from their designated 9fin office on Tuesdays and Wednesdays. Some teams may be asked to be in the office more often, where the nature of their work calls for it. For the rest of the week, you may work from wherever works best for you and your team. Your Talent Partner will share hybrid working details for this role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>9fin is an equal opportunities employer</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At 9fin we are dedicated to building and promoting a fair and inclusive workplace where everyone can reach their full potential and truly belong. We recognize that building diverse teams enables a more creative and productive environment. If you’re excited about this role but your experience doesn’t perfectly align with the job description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You might just be who we’re looking for — either for this role, or perhaps another.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/9fin/regional-director-client-engagement-london-294999","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794681611},{"slug":"application-security-engineer-agents-platform-united-kingdom-410548","company_name":"Elevenlabs","title":"Application Security Engineer - Agents platform","description":"<h2>About ElevenLabs</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenLabs is an AI research and product company transforming how we interact with technology.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We launched in January 2023 with the first human-like AI voice model. Today, we serve millions of users and thousands of businesses - from fast-growing startups to large enterprises like Deutsche Telekom and Meta. Our investors are some of the world's most prominent, including Andreessen Horowitz, ICONIQ Growth and Sequoia. We've raised $781M in funding and our last valuation was $22B - multiples of 11, always.<br /><br />We have expanded from voice into three main platforms:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenAgents enables businesses to deliver seamless and intelligent customer experiences, with the integrations, testing, monitoring, and reliability necessary to deploy voice and chat agents at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenCreative empowers creators and marketers to generate and edit speech, music, image, and video across 70+ languages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenAPI gives developers access to our leading AI audio foundational models.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everything we do is the result of the creativity and commitment of our team - builders doing the best work of their lives. We are researchers, engineers, and operators. IOI medalists and ex-founders. If you want to work hard and create lasting positive impact, we want to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How we work</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-velocity: </strong>Rapid experimentation, lean autonomous teams, and minimal bureaucracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact not job titles: </strong>We don’t have job titles. Instead, it’s about the impact you have. No task is above or beneath you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI first:</strong> We use AI to move faster with higher-quality results. We do this across the whole company—from engineering to growth to operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellence everywhere: </strong>Everything we do should match the quality of our AI models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Global team: </strong>We prioritize your talent, not your location.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Innovative culture:</strong> You’ll be part of a generational opportunity to define the trajectory of AI, surrounded by a team pushing the boundaries of what’s possible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth paths: </strong>Joining ElevenLabs means joining a dynamic team with countless opportunities to drive impact - beyond your immediate role and responsibilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; development</strong>: ElevenLabs proactively supports professional development through an annual discretionary stipend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Social travel</strong>: We also provide an annual discretionary stipend to meet up with colleagues each year, however you choose.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Annual team offsite: </strong>Each year, we bring your entire team together in a new location - past offsites have included Croatia, Italy and Cancún</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Co-working</strong>: If you’re not located near one of our main hubs, we offer a monthly co-working stipend.</p></li></ul><h2>About the role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenAgents is our platform for building and running conversational AI agents at scale. As our first Application Security Engineer embedded in the Agents team, you’ll make the secure way the easy way. You’ll build the security tooling and reusable primitives that let engineers ship securely by default.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a builder role. Expect to spend about 70% of your time building tools and internal systems, and the rest working with engineers, staying in sync with Core Security, and doing security research. More than half of the work is greenfield and most of it starts with you, you’ll spot the problems worth solving and own each solution from idea to production.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build security primitives that are easy for engineers to adopt, starting from what you find when you audit the Agents codebase</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review new product work for security and feed what you learn back into shared tooling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the major security improvements to the Agents platform, working closely with Core Security</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make sure Agents platform uses authn and authz controls correctly and building the guardrails that keep the platform from compromising on security best practices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the security bar for the Agents platform and make meeting it the easy path for product engineers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with engineers daily to help them ship fast and safely</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in application security engineering at scale, covering secure design, vulnerability management and security tooling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong software engineering skills: you have built and shipped products end to end, in production-quality code</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in Python, our main language. Golang or another language is fine if you can pick up Python quickly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with authentication and authorization. Experience securing cross-service communication is a bonus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with large-scale, customer-facing backend systems and enterprise-grade security</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communication and a real enjoyment of working with developers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of owning delivery end to end</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Security for AI and LLM applications</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cloud-native experience (AWS or GCP, Kubernetes, Terraform, IAM, networking, Linux internals)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in regulated environments (SOC 2, ISO 27001, PCI, HIPAA)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Not required: </strong>Compliance certifications, incident response experience, a traditional security background, or prior domain knowledge. We care about what you have built and shipped, and open source work or conference talks are welcome evidence of that.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Location</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is remote and can be executed globally. However, to facilitate working with the Security Team, we prefer candidates based in GMT to GMT+3 or UK. If you prefer, you can work from our offices in Dublin, London or Warsaw</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability or other legally protected statuses.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/elevenlabs/application-security-engineer-agents-platform-united-kingdom-410548","tags":["Engineering & Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1794681611},{"slug":"sector-analyst-proprietary-research-london-890","company_name":"Point72","title":"Sector Analyst, Proprietary Research","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT PROPRIETARY RESEARCH&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On our proprietary research team—Market Intelligence— you will uncover insights about companies, industries, and the broader economy through deep compliant fundamental research and applying data science and engineering techniques to alternative data sets. In partnership with our investment professionals and Compliance team, our team of analysts, data scientists and engineers work together to produce compliant research and build tools that inform our firm’s investments. We look for other bright, motivated, and collaborative people to join our team and grow with us—a majority of the leaders in our group were promoted from within.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Sector Analyst for European Equities, you will work with alternative data to gather industry context and business fundamentals. You will then partner with our team of data scientists and engineers to develop analyses that you’ll deliver as synthesized insights to our investment professionals to help aid in their research processes. The work is ever evolving, affording opportunities to tackle new challenges alongside research teammates from diverse backgrounds.&amp;nbsp;Specifically, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and interpret alternative data from multiple sources and develop subject-matter expertise on the key themes and KPIs that drive the industry and companies within your assigned coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce research for internal consumption by our investment professionals across a variety of mediums, including written research reports, verbal communication, and visualization tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interact directly with our investment professionals to learn the discretionary investment process and help them to drive more informed investment decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with our proprietary research teams including Data Sourcing, Data Science, and Data Engineering, as well as Compliance, to source, evaluate, and draw value from new and existing data assets&amp;nbsp;to produce actionable research for investment professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT’S REQUIRED &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An undergraduate or advanced degree with demonstrated academic success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One to five years of prior equity/investment/scientific/industry research or consulting experience, including any relevant internship experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with technical coding/programming and ability to participate in a live technical screen (SQL, Python)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leveraging data analysis as part of the fundamental research process for business, public policy, finance, engineering, applied sciences, or other quantitative fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with analyzing novel data and explaining concepts to non-technical partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for finance, research, and using data to solve problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great organizational skills to handle a demanding workload, creativity, and a strong work ethic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate productively in a team environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
