ofollow" href="http://Vibe.co">Vibe.co</a> to reach 120 million+ households. And in August 2026, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Vibe.co">Vibe.co</a> became a Walmart company, opening up a new chapter for the business and the industry. With Walmart’s first-party data and purchase signals now part of the Vibe platform, advertisers can connect TV advertising to real-world transactions and measure the impact of CTV with a level of precision previously associated with platforms like Google and Meta.<br /><br /><strong>This is a unique moment to join Vibe.</strong> With Walmart’s scale, data, and reach behind us, we’re building the next generation of TV advertising and creating a more measurable, performance-driven future for the channel.</p><h2>Your team</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will join the Supply team, which owns Vibe's inventory: the publishers we partner with, the deals we run, and the catalog of apps, channels and shows our advertisers care about.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shows are the reason people turn on their TV. Advertisers don't just want impressions: they want to show up next to the right shows, live sports and premium channels. Supply brings that content to Vibe through direct publisher partnerships, curated deals and sponsorships. It makes it easy to find, understand and buy, through real-time bidding, or any technology the publisher uses.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Premium publishers care as much about which ads run on their shows as about who buys them, and great creatives are what earn us access.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The team brings together partnerships, operations, and product. You will work closely with the DSP team, which runs the bidding infrastructure, and the Performance team, which decides how to value each opportunity, as well as with publisher partners directly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Your mission</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Software Engineer on 