ale jet propulsion systems (12–25 kg thrust class), from concept to flight-ready hardware. This is a hands-on, high-ownership role in a fast-moving startup environment where speed and iteration matter more than lengthy upfront studies.<br /><br /><strong>Responsibilities: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and develop new small jet engines (12–25 kg thrust range) in-house, optimized for very low production cost</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the aerodynamic design of turbine components, balancing performance, manufacturability, and cost</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design a large portion of the turbine for metal 3D printing (additive manufacturing), leveraging design-for-AM principles to reduce part count, weight, and cost</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with 3D printing operations to define printable geometries, tolerances, post-processing, and qualify parts for flight use</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive a rapid, fail-fast iteration process: build, test, learn, and redesign quickly rather than relying on long analytical phases before prototyping</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integrate propulsion systems into airframes such as flying wings and other interceptor drone configurations, working with aerostructures and systems teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply and enforce design rules for operation in extreme environments (cold and hot climates, rain, humidity, icing conditions) to ensure engine reliability across the full operational envelope</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to engine testing (bench and flight), performance validation, and continuous design improvement</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Candidate Profile: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Minimum 8 years of experience in jet engine / gas turbine design, with a proven track record of having designed and delivered engine models (not just component-level work)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong hands-on experience with small jet engines in the 12–25 kg thrust class</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid global understanding of jet engine architecture: compressor, combustor, turbine, fuel system, controls, and their interactions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing turbine/engine components for metal additive manufacturing (DfAM), and practical knowledge of metal 3D printing processes and constraints</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working in a rapid-iteration, fail-fast development culture rather than a traditional long-cycle aerospace process</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience integrating propulsion systems into airframes (flying wing or similar unconventional platforms is a strong plus)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of design requirements for extreme operating environments (temperature extremes, precipitation, icing)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work autonomously in a small, fast-paced startup team, wearing multiple hats when needed</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with UAV/drone propulsion specifically (vs. manned aviation)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with low-cost manufacturing strategies for defense/dual-use hardware</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prior startup or skunkworks experience</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/alta-ares/senior-jet-engine-design-engineer-interceptor-drones-blagnac-262136","tags":["Hardware"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Toulouse","created_at":1794606015},{"slug":"vp-production-platform-paris-185718","company_name":"Mistral.ai","title":"VP, Production Platform","description":"<h2><strong>About Mistral</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral provides full-stack AI solutions: from frontier models to developer tools, applications, and compute. We partner with enterprises tackling the hardest problems across high-stakes industries like finance, manufacturing, defense, healthcare, and the public sector, co-creating customized AI systems that they can run on their terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a dynamic, collaborative team passionate about AI and its potential to transform society. Our diverse workforce thrives in competitive environments and is committed to driving innovation. Our teams are distributed between Europe, North America, Asia and the Middle East. We are creative, low-ego and team-spirited.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the Vice President of our Production Platform organization, you will own how reliably Mistral runs in production and how fast every Mistral engineer ships. This role combines deep infrastructure expertise with organizational leadership to build a platform that scales ahead of the company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Production Platform brings together around 55 engineers across site reliability, deployment, build and CI, and our internal service framework, led by strong team leads. Every deploy and every model release goes through this organization, from our own cloud to the major hyperscalers, private clouds and our customers’ on-premise environments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will set the strategy for the organization, grow its leaders and shape the organization as it scales. The role is key to the reliability of our products, the velocity of our engineering and research teams, and our ability to deliver Mistral wherever our customers need it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Will Do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the Production Platform organization through its Engineering Managers, and grow them as leaders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the strategy and roadmap for reliability, deployment, build and CI, and the internal service framework.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the reliability of our production environment: SLOs, on-call, incident management and capacity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make delivery to every environment, from SaaS to private cloud and on-premise, as simple and dependable as a single deploy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Raise engineering velocity across the company with fast, trusted CI and safe deployments by default.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Give product teams strong defaults and the ownership of their own services and tests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design the organization as it scales: structure, hiring, on-call models and processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to architecture and the hard technical decisions, staying close to the systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Product Engineering, Research and our enterprise teams to align the platform with their needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and track the metrics that matter: reliability, delivery speed and developer experience.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep background in infrastructure, site reliability or production engineering, starting as a hands-on engineer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading leaders: managing managers and growing strong team leads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience scaling an infrastructure or platform organization through fast growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of running production systems at scale, with measurable results on reliability or delivery speed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to set strategy in an ambiguous scope and turn it into execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical judgment in distributed systems, Kubernetes, cloud infrastructure and CI/CD.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience delivering software into customer environments (on-premise, private cloud, air-gapped) is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with AI infrastructure, such as model serving or GPU platforms, is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Low ego, at ease with constant change, and driven by results.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being, growth, and work-life balance. Benefits vary by country and may include healthcare coverage, parental leave, retirement plans, relocation support, wellness programs, meal and transportation allowances, and other location-specific perks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For the most up-to-date details on benefits available in your location, please refer to our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://app.notion.com/p/mistralai/Benefits-at-Mistral-36e6ba59a7fe836b93dd01737fcc27ef?source=copy_link">Benefits page</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Privacy Policy</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your privacy matters to us. You can learn more about how we handle your personal data in our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://legal.mistral.ai/terms/applicant-privacy-policy"><u>Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/mistralai/vp-production-platform-paris-185718","tags":["Engineering & Infra"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794606015},{"slug":"product-support-enablement-lead-paris-209026","company_name":"Mistral.ai","title":"Product Support & Enablement Lead","description":"<h2><strong>About Mistral</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral provides full-stack AI solutions: from frontier models to developer tools, applications, and compute. We partner with enterprises tackling the hardest problems across high-stakes industries like finance, manufacturing, defense, healthcare, and the public sector, co-creating customized AI systems that they can run on their terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a dynamic, collaborative team passionate about AI and its potential to transform society. Our diverse workforce thrives in competitive environments and is committed to driving innovation. Our teams are distributed between Europe, North America, Asia and the Middle East. We are creative, low-ego and team-spirited.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a <strong>Product Support &amp; Enablement Lead</strong> to lead and develop our existing L1 Product Support team. You will help the team resolve more customer issues without escalating to L2, while improving the tools, training, and workflows that allow support to scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a senior technical and people-management role—not simply a role overseeing today’s queue. You will lead frontline delivery for Product Support (L1) and develop the team’s ability to investigate and resolve increasingly technical requests, including paid self-serve and first-level enterprise issues.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work closely with L2 and other teams to define clear ownership, identify work Product Support (L1) can safely take on, and build repeatable escalation paths. You will also contribute to operational continuity for the wider Support organization.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be equally comfortable coaching a team member through a customer issue, investigating an API error, improving a support workflow, and partnering with Engineering or Product to address a recurring problem.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Key responsibilities</strong></h2><h3><br /><strong>Lead frontline support delivery</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead, coach, and develop a distributed L1 Product Support team, providing regular feedback and supporting technical growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own day-to-day L1 Product Support delivery, including queue prioritization, backlog management, customer communication, and regional handoffs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and maintain clear ownership of L1 Product Support queues and handoffs to L2, including for paid self-serve and first-level enterprise requests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor service quality, response and resolution times, backlog health, and customer satisfaction; turn insights into practical improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay hands-on with complex or sensitive customer issues and model strong technical judgment.</p></li></ul><h3><br /><strong>Increase Product Support (L1) technical autonomy</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Train and coach Product Support (L1) agents to investigate, reproduce, and resolve more technical issues across Mistral products, including Vibe, Studio, and APIs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with L2 to identify issue types that Product Support (L1) can safely take on and define the knowledge, access, and safeguards needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create playbooks, troubleshooting guides, and escalation criteria that help Product Support (L1) agents resolve issues independently and consistently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve L1-to-L2 handoffs so escalations contain customer impact, investigation steps, and relevant evidence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track escalation patterns and use them to prioritize training, documentation, and product improvements.<br /></p></li></ul><h3><strong>Scale systems, workflows, and automation</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own improvements to frontline support tooling, routing, workflows, macros, and internal processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own improvements to frontline Product Support (L1) tooling, routing, workflows, macros, and internal processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop AI-assisted support and automation, including Intercom Fin, to reduce repetitive work while maintaining response quality and appropriate human escalation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify recurring contact drivers and partner with Product, Engineering, and other teams to address them at the source.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build reporting and operating reviews that make workload, service performance, escalation patterns, and risks visible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish shared processes with specialist Support teams while respecting their ownership of technical delivery.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Build knowledge and operational continuity</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop onboarding materials and technical training that help agents become autonomous.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Documentation and Product teams to keep internal guidance and customer-facing help content accurate and useful.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share customer insights and support trends with Product, Engineering, and go-to-market teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help coordinate support readiness for new products, features, and processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to operational continuity for the Support organization through team coordination, reporting, and escalation management.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant experience in customer-facing technical support, product support, or support operations in a fast-moving technology environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Senior people-management experience, including leading, coaching, and developing a Support  team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical judgment and troubleshooting skills, including the ability to investigate product issues, reproduce bugs, and understand API requests and errors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing support queues, escalations, service quality, and operational performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience improving workflows, tooling, or knowledge management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to use support data to identify bottlenecks and prioritize improvements without losing sight of the customer experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English, including the ability to explain technical issues clearly to different audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A pragmatic, collaborative approach and comfort working across time zones and functions.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Nice to have</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Intercom, Fin, or comparable support and AI automation tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting developer tools, APIs, SaaS products, or AI applications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with scripting or lightweight automation