ross-Functional Engineering Coordination</strong> – Work closely with Cloud Engineering, Data Center Infrastructure, Networking, Storage, Kubernetes, and Fleet teams to align priorities, resolve blockers, and drive execution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Engineering Operations &amp; Process Improvement</strong> – Identify opportunities to streamline infrastructure deployment processes, improve coordination, and introduce scalable, lightweight workflows that accelerate delivery.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Location &amp; Office Policy</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The position is based in our Paris HQ offices and we encourage going to the office as much as we can (at least 3 days per week) to create bonds and smooth communication. Our remote policy aims to provide flexibility, improve work-life balance and increase productivity. Each manager can decide the amount of days worked remotely based on autonomy and a specific context (e.g. more flexibility can occur during summer). In any case, employees are expected to maintain regular communication with their teams and be available during core working hours.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You Will Do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Program Management</strong> — Lead and coordinate complex cloud infrastructure programs, from physical infrastructure handover through software deployment and production readiness.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Infrastructure Deployment</strong> — Oversee the software bring-up of newly deployed compute infrastructure, coordinating engineering teams responsible for networking, storage, Kubernetes, fleet delivery, and infrastructure health.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration</strong> — Work closely with Cloud Engineering, Data Center Infrastructure, and other technical teams to ensure alignment across deployment activities, technical dependencies, and operational priorities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Project Delivery</strong> — Define and track project milestones, timelines, and resources. Anticipate blockers, coordinate technical dependencies, and ensure infrastructure is brought into production efficiently and reliably.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Process Improvement</strong> — Continuously identify opportunities to improve deployment workflows, reduce time to production, and establish scalable processes that support our growing infrastructure needs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stakeholder Management</strong> — Maintain clear communication with engineering teams, technical leads, and leadership, providing visibility into program progress, risks, and key decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Risk Management</strong> — Proactively identify technical and operational risks, develop mitigation strategies, and drive the resolution of critical issues that could delay infrastructure availability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You hold a degree in a relevant scientific or technical field (e.g., Computer Science, Engineering, or a related discipline).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have at least <strong>4 years of relevant experience</strong> managing technical programs, preferably in cloud infrastructure, software infrastructure, data centers, GPU computing, hosting, or related environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have proven experience coordinating complex technical projects involving multiple engineering teams and interdependent workstreams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a strong understanding of infrastructure deployment processes and the technical challenges involved in bringing systems into production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have excellent project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple complex