:1.5em"></p><h2>About the role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Between a conversation and a model sit the formats and tokenizers that every part of our stack relies on. You will help own them, and the tooling around them, so that training, evaluation and production all speak exactly the same language.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work across the entire stack, spanning pretraining, post-training and deployment, and your decisions will reach every model we ship.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you will do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, build and maintain core libraries for tokenization and model interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evolve our formats and tokenizers as models and use cases change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn research needs into robust, shared tooling.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we're looking for</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong software engineering background, with excellent Python.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent understanding of tokenizers: BPE and other tokenization algorithms, special tokens, chat templates, and tokenizer training; ideally hands-on experience with libraries such as tiktoken or Hugging Face tokenizers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building production-grade libraries used by many people.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A taste for correctness and attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good knowledge of how LLMs are trained and served.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communication, low ego, and a collaborative mindset.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice to have</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Open-source maintenance experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with inference engines.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Location and remote</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is primarily based at one of our European offices (Paris and London). We will prioritize candidates who either reside there or are open to relocating. We strongly believe in the value of in-person collaboration to foster strong relationships and seamless communication within our team. In certain specific situations, we will also consider remote candidates based in one of the countries listed in this job posting — currently France &amp; UK. In that case, we ask all new hires to visit our local office for the first week of their onboarding (accommodation and travelling covered), then at least 4 days per month</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being, growth, and work-life balance. Benefits vary by country and may include healthcare coverage, parental leave, retirement plans, relocation support, wellness programs, meal and transportation allowances, and other location-specific perks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For the most up-to-date details on benefits available in your location, please refer to our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://app.notion.com/p/mistralai/Benefits-at-Mistral-36e6ba59a7fe836b93dd01737fcc27ef?source=copy_link">Benefits page</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Privacy Policy</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your privacy matters to us. You can learn more about how we handle your personal data in our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://legal.mistral.ai/terms/applicant-privacy-policy"><u>Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/mistralai/research-engineer-tokenizer-protocols-paris-36059","tags":["Science"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794606015},{"slug":"head-of-fde-learning-programs-paris-446388","company_name":"Mistral.ai","title":"Head of FDE Learning Programs","description":"<h2><strong>About Mistral</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral provides full-stack AI solutions: from frontier models to developer tools, applications, and compute. We partner with enterprises tackling the hardest problems across high-stakes industries like finance, manufacturing, defense, healthcare, and the public sector, co-creating customized AI systems that they can run on their terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a dynamic, collaborative team passionate about AI and its potential to transform society. Our diverse workforce thrives in competitive environments and is committed to driving innovation. Our teams are distributed between Europe, North America, Asia and the Middle East. We are creative, low-ego and team-spirited.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the job</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral is hiring a <strong>Head of FDE Learning Programs</strong> to build the learning system for one of the company’s fastest-growing organizations. Mistral is scaling its FDE organization from its first hire to several hundred Deployment Strategists and Applied AI Engineers within two years. Your mandate is to make capability grow as fast as headcount without lowering the bar for customer work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You will own:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning content:</strong> Build practical learning across three areas: technical skills, strategic and business capabilities, and product enablement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Onboarding:</strong> Build a clear path from a new hire’s first week to independent customer work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical bootcamps:</strong> Turn new products, research, and field methods into practical training for customer work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategic bootcamps</strong>: Empower client-facing teams of FDEs to drive business and strategic discussions and to set up for success large partnership programs with customers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Program ownership:</strong> Own the roadmap, curriculum, contributor model, regional delivery, tools, measurement, and central team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scaling:</strong> Launch useful programs now, then adapt them for larger cohorts without making the content generic or relying on a small group of experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team building:</strong> Launch the first programs, build a network of instructors, and hire the team needed to support several hundred FDEs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-functional work:</strong> Work with functional managers, Product, Engineering, Science, People, GTM Enablement, DevRel, and regional leaders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Readiness standards:</strong> Ensure FDEs in every region meet the same standard, can find current material, learn from recent customer work, and understand expectations at the next career level.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Knowledge structuration:</strong> Ensure internal resources are up to date and pushed to the right stakeholders with a knowledge management approach.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>How We Work in Solutions</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We care about people and outputs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">What matters is what you ship, not the time you spend on it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bureaucracy is where urgency goes to vanish. You talk to whoever you need to talk to. The best idea wins, whether it comes from a principal engineer or someone in their first week.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Always ask why. The best solutions come from deep understanding, not from copying what worked before</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We say what we mean. Feedback is direct, timely, and given because we care.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">No politics. Low ego, high standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We embrace an unstructured environment and find joy in it.<br /></p></li></ul><h2>About you</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have helped build a learning, enablement, or capability function for a technical organization during rapid growth. You can start as the first dedicated owner, deliver useful programs immediately, and build the team and operating model needed to serve several hundred people.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are technically fluent enough to work credibly with AI engineers, Product, and Science, inspect the substance of a program, and challenge material that is unclear or outdated.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have designed programs that work across cohorts, regions, and experience levels without reducing the content to generic training.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can lead work across senior stakeholders, subject-matter experts, managers, and operational partners without relying on reporting lines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can make firm trade-offs when hiring demand, expert capacity, and program quality compete for attention.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You pay attention to the full learner experience, including communications, scheduling, practice, feedback, and manager follow-through.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You use evidence to decide which programs to expand, revise, or stop.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You communicate clearly with executives, managers, technical experts, and learners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are fluent in English and can work with teams across regions and time zones.<br /></p></li></ul><h2>Ideally, you have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scaled a one-person or small learning function into a team and program that served hundreds of technical employees.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Built onboarding that kept pace with rapid hiring in an engineering, FDE, solutions, consulting, or professional-services organization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Designed and operated technical bootcamps or other cohort-based learning programs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Worked in technical DevRel, developer education, or a related role built around demos, code examples, workshops, and practitioner communities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Built role- and level-based curricula connected to skills frameworks or career progression.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Managed a global program with contributors and learners across multiple regions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Worked closely with Product, Engineering, Science, People, and customer-facing teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Designed practical assessments, readiness standards, or certification where appropriate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Used learning platforms, knowledge systems, AI coaches, or program-operations tooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Worked in AI/ML or another technically complex and fast-changing field.<br /></p></li></ul><h2>Why this role matters</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral is compressing years of organization growth into two. An FDE organization of several hundred people cannot depend on manager-by-manager onboarding, one-off sessions, and informal access to experts. If learning capacity trails hiring, ramp times would lengthen, standards would diverge, and teams would repeat the same mistakes across regions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role will build the programs, teaching network, and systems at the same pace as the organization. Two years from now, success would mean several hundred Deployment Strategists and Applied AI Engineers working from shared standards, learning new capabilities quickly, and improving the system with evidence from customer work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being, growth, and work-life balance. Benefits vary by country and may include healthcare coverage, parental leave, retirement plans, relocation support, wellness programs, meal and transportation allowances, and other location-specific perks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For the most up-to-date details on benefits available in your location, please refer to our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://app.notion.com/p/mistralai/Benefits-at-Mistral-36e6ba59a7fe836b93dd01737fcc27ef?source=copy_link">Benefits page</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Privacy Policy</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your privacy matters to us. You can learn more about how we handle your personal data in our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://legal.mistral.ai/terms/applicant-privacy-policy"><u>Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/mistralai/head-of-fde-learning-programs-paris-446388","tags":["Business"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794606015},{"slug":"site-reliability-engineer-paris-24957","company_name":"Mistral.ai","title":"Site Reliability Engineer","description":"<h2><strong>About Mistral</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral provides full-stack AI solutions: from frontier models to developer tools, applications, and compute. We partner with enterprises tackling the hardest problems across high-stakes industries like finance, manufacturing, defense, healthcare, and the public sector, co-creating customized AI systems that they can run on their terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a dynamic, collaborative team passionate about AI and its potential to transform society. Our diverse workforce thrives in competitive environments and is committed to driving innovation. Our teams are distributed between Europe, North America, Asia and the Middle East. We are creative, low-ego and team-spirited.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a <strong>Site Reliability Engineer (SRE)</strong> on the <strong>Platform</strong> team, you will shape the reliability, scalability, and performance of our platform and customer-facing applications. You’ll work closely with software engineers and research teams to ensure our systems meet and exceed the expectations of both internal and external customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role balances day-to-day operations on production systems with long-term software engineering improvements. Your work will reduce operational toil, foster reliability, and ensure high availability for our web services, inference environments, and ML workloads. You’ll enable seamless replication of work environments across multiple HPC clusters, directly impacting the stability and efficiency of our AI platform.</p><h2>What You Will Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, build, and maintain scalable, highly available, and fault-tolerant infrastructures to support web services and ML workloads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure our platform, inference, and model training environments are always highly available and enable seamless replication across HPC clusters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operate systems and troubleshoot issues in production, including interrupts, on-call responses, and infrastructure scaling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement and improve monitoring, alerting, and incident response systems to minimize downtime and optimize performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and maintain workflows and tools for CI/CD, containerization, orchestration, monitoring, and logging.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate in on-call rotations to respond to incidents and perform root cause analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive continuous improvement in infrastructure automation, deployment, and orchestration using tools like Kubernetes, Flux, and Terraform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with AI/ML researchers to enable safe and reproducible model-training experiments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a cloud-agnostic platform that abstracts infrastructure complexities for science and engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and develop new workflows, tooling, and automation to improve system reliability, availability, and performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with the security team to ensure infrastructure adheres to best practices and compliance requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Document processes and procedures to ensure consistency and knowledge sharing across the team.</p></li></ul><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A Master’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of experience in a DevOps or SRE role, with strong expertise in cloud computing and distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with site reliability issues, including root cause analysis, in-production troubleshooting, and on-call rotations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in working with reliability KPIs, such as observability, alerting, and