and open source:</strong> We encourage publishing results and contributing to open tools such as NeuralHydrology and Caravan.</p></li><li><p><strong>Compute:</strong> GPU resources are available for training and experimentation.</p></li></ul><p><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><ul><li><p>Bring global flood models to the local scale</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Take state-of-the-art hydrological ML models (LSTMs, Transformers) trained on large-sample datasets and adapt them to the catchments our customers care about.</p></li><li><p>Use our own sensor data alongside public gauge, reanalysis and radar data to fine-tune and validate those models locally.</p></li><li><p>Tackle prediction in ungauged and data-scarce basins through transfer learning and regionalisation.</p></li><li><p>Own hydrological modelling end to end: set the technical direction, decide when to adapt pre-trained models or train our own, and lead the work from experimentation through validation to production.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Work as one modelling team</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Make practical trade-offs between forecast accuracy, model complexity and development effort to build a reliable product that meets customer needs.</p></li><li><p>Work side by side with our hydrologist specialising in rainfall radar and nowcasting to directly integrate rainfall nowcasts into your flood models.</p></li><li><p>Work with software engineers to put models into production and monitor their performance.</p></li><li><p>Identify and test advances in ML flood forecasting, turning promising research into more accurate and reliable forecasts for our customers.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Stay close to the real world</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>We believe the best modellers understand the world behind their models. We encourage you to join field deployments and customer conversations to build that understanding firsthand.</p></li><li><p>You are an opinionated contributor to key technical decisions.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Who You 