ree workplace. Lightspeed welcomes and encourages applications from people with disabilities. Accommodations are available on request for candidates taking part in all aspects of the selection process.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Where to from here?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Obviously, this has to be mutually beneficial: we want you to step into a role you love, and we want to offer you a place you’re proud to come to every day. For a glimpse into our world check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.lightspeedhq.com/careers/">career page here</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed is building communities through commerce, and we need people from all backgrounds and lived experiences to do that. We were founded in 2005, in Montreal’s gay village and our original members were all part of the LGBTQ+ community. The ethos of our business has been about inclusion from the very beginning, and we strive to provide a workplace where everyone belongs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who we are:</strong> </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Powering the businesses that are the backbone of the global economy, Lightspeed's one-stop commerce platform helps merchants innovate to simplify, scale, and provide exceptional customer experiences. Our cloud commerce solution transforms and unifies online and physical operations, multichannel sales, expansion to new locations, global payments, financial solutions, and connection to supplier networks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Montréal, Canada in 2005, Lightspeed is dual-listed on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE: LSPD) and Toronto Stock Exchange (TSX: LSPD). With teams across North America, Europe, and Asia Pacific, the company serves retail, hospitality, and golf businesses in over 100 countries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed handles your information in accordance with our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="c-link" href="https://www.lightspeedhq.com/legal/applicant-privacy-statement/">Applicant Privacy Statement</a>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/lightspeedhq/field-sales-representative-amsterdam-349903","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794444014},{"slug":"senior-business-controller-operations-almere-288632","company_name":"HG International b.v.","title":"Senior Business Controller (Operations)","description":"<p class="Paragraph SCXW146165284 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Would you like to work closely with the business as a Senior Business Controller and use your financial expertise to make a real impact on decisions? You will bring financial structure and insight, while keeping a forward-looking perspective: where can we improve, which decisions will make a financial difference, and what will they mean for our results?</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW146165284 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">HG is a compact, international organisation. This means considerable responsibility, direct contact with decision-makers and room to drive change yourself. We are therefore looking for someone who takes ownership, works pragmatically and is not afraid to challenge existing ways of working.</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW146165284 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">You will be based at our head office in Almere. Hybrid working opportunities are limited: regular office attendance is important in this role because of the close collaboration with Finance, Operations and other stakeholders. You will also travel to the United Kingdom or Germany several times a year.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#5a5f72">About the role</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">As Senior Business Controller, you will be responsible for business control within Operations and will also support our subsidiaries in the United Kingdom and Germany. You have a clear vision of what the best operational business control model looks like and have proven experience in realizing this. The Senior Business Controller plays a key role in strengthening financial control, transparency and decision-making across Operations. The scope covers procurement and product costing, as well as warehouse and transport operations. Working closely with Finance, Procurement and Operations, the Senior Business Controller translates operational developments and improvement initiatives into clear financial insights and P&amp;L impact</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Our business is undergoing significant change. HG has recently changed its logistics service arrangements, consolidating most local warehouses into one central location as part of a cost-saving initiative. At the same time, a new ERP system is being implemented. This creates an interesting and dynamic environment in which existing budget models, cost allocation models, reporting and financial processes need to be further developed to reflect the new operating model and provide a solid basis for financial control and decision-making.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#5a5f72">What you will do</span></strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Your responsibilities will include:</span></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Owning the operational cost lines between Net Sales and Contribution Margin for the whole group and</span><s><span style="color:#5a5f72">.</span></s><span style="color:#5a5f72"> act as a strong Finance business partner to the Chief Operating Officer and his team, translating operational developments into actionable financial insights;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Identifying and driving continuous improvements to the operational business, improving insights while reducing costs.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Being the financial business partner for the country managers in the UK and Germany, including reviewing commercial deals and business cases.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Analyzing budget versus actuals and explaining significant variances.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Developing a clear understanding of budgeted versus actual purchase prices and identifying the key drivers behind price variances.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Providing insight into raw material and purchase price developments and translating these into expected P&amp;L impact.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Quantifying and tracking the financial impact of Procurement and product-costing initiatives and other savings programmes.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Establishing and further developing standard COGS based on expected cost developments.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph TrackedChange SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Build a thorough understanding of the warehouse and distribution budget, operational performance and key savings initiatives.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph TrackedChange SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Track whether the expected savings from the recently implemented warehouse and transport provider change are being realized in the P&amp;L.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Further developing cost allocation models for individual markets, using meaningful drivers, and working towards more complete and reliable management reporting.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Ensuring the Operations P&amp;L, budget and actual costs are consistently captured and reported in the same structure.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Translating inventory developments into financial impact and creating a clear link between stock levels, budget assumptions and cost allocation.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Supporting and improving an efficient month-end closing process, ensuring Operations costs are accurately and consistently booked, allocated and reconciled.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5A5F72">E</span><span style="color:#5a5f72">stablish or improve proper accounting entries together with Finance Administration and relevant operational partners.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Co-lead the annual budget cycle and budget presentations to the Board.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW25715031 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Using and improving Power BI, ERP data and financial processes to reduce manual work and increase transparency.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">You will report directly to the Chief Financial Officer and work closely with colleagues in Finance, Procurement and Operations. You will also have regular contact with the Germany and UK country managers.</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW25715031 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">This position requires more than strong analytical skills. You will need to explain your insights clearly, engage stakeholders and constructively challenge where necessary. You will be a knowledgeable sparring partner who asks questions, brings structure and takes responsibility from analysis through to implementation. You proactively identify opportunities to improve financial processes, controls, reporting and transparency across Operations.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#5a5f72">HG is a compact, fast-growing and international organization where you can directly see the impact of your work. This requires ownership, initiative and a pragmatic, results-oriented mindset. The team culture is open, pragmatic and focused on results, encouraging you to bring ideas forward, challenge constructively and take responsibility. Everything we do is guided by our three core values: Aim High, Be Brave, Be Connected.</span></p> <br> <p class="Paragraph SCXW139534942 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#5a5f72">What you bring</span></strong></p><p class="Paragraph TrackedChange SCXW139534942 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">We are looking for a financially strong, hands-on and improvement-oriented controller who combines analytical capability with a practical understanding of Operations. The ideal candidate is comfortable working across Finance, Procurement and Operations and is able to turn complex cost drivers into clear insights and concrete actions.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph TrackedChange SCXW139534942 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">You bring a proactive mindset, strong stakeholder-management skills and a natural drive to simplify and improve processes. You are comfortable challenging existing ways of working, creating structure in a changing environment and taking ownership from analysis through implementation.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW38523178 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">You will also have:</span></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW38523178 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW38523178 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">A completed university master’s degree in Finance, Economics, Business Administration or a related field. A Registered Controller (RC) qualification is a strong advantage.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW38523178 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW38523178 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Around 10 years of relevant experience in business control, operations control or a comparable financial role.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW38523178 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW38523178 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Experience in a manufacturing environment is important, including knowledge of production processes, procurement and cost calculations.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW38523178 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW38523178 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">A sound understanding of business control, financial controls and treasury.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW38523178 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW38523178 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Experience with ERP systems and an understanding of how financial data and accounting flows are structured.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW38523178 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW38523178 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Good knowledge of Power BI. You do not need to build everything from scratch, but you can independently investigate, improve and develop analyses.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW38523178 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW38523178 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Experience working with consolidation tools.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW38523178 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW38523178 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Strong analytical, communication and stakeholder management skills.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW38523178 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW38523178 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">A proactive, hands-on and improvement-oriented mindset, with the ability to create structure in a changing environment.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW38523178 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW38523178 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Fluency in English. Knowledge of Dutch is desirable, and German is an advantage.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW38523178 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW38523178 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Experience with AI tools, such as Copilot.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW38523178 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW38523178 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Willingness to travel to the United Kingdom and Germany several times a year.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW38523178 BCX8"><em><span style="color:#5a5f72">Please note that we do not offer visa or work permit sponsorship for this position. You must therefore hold a valid EU work permit</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW15198906 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#5a5f72">What do we offer</span></strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW15198906 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">At HG, you will not be stepping into a role where everything is already set in stone. Changes in our logistics operations, systems and reporting create opportunities to further professionalize financial control and implement improvements yourself.</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW15198906 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">You can expect:</span></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW15198906 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW15198906 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">a senior role with broad responsibility and direct influence on financial and operational decision-making;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW15198906 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW15198906 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">a salary appropriate to the seniority of the role, with an indicative range of €85,000 to €100,000 gross per year;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW15198906 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW15198906 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">an annual on-target bonus of 25% of your gross annual salary;&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW15198906 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW15198906 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">full-time employment with 30 days of annual leave;&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW15198906 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW15198906 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">a pension scheme;&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW15198906 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW15198906 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">a commuting allowance;&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW15198906 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW15198906 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">a full-time role based at our head office in Almere. Hybrid working is possible on a limited basis, with office attendance being an important part of the role;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW15198906 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW15198906 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">a dynamic and ambitious working environment where initiative and ownership are valued;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW15198906 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW15198906 BCX8"><span style="color:#5a5f72">a friendly, welcoming team, with a free shared lunch every Monday and monthly social drinks.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#5a5f72">We are HG</span></strong></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#5a5f72">HG is a leading European brand in specialist cleaning and maintenance products.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#5a5f72">We believe a home should be a place where people can live carefree, with confidence in the products they use to care for the spaces and belongings around them. Our products are developed to do exactly what they promise: deliver effective, reliable and specialist cleaning solutions that help consumers solve real household problems.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#5a5f72">HG’s mission is to help people enjoy their homes without worrying about what might go wrong. We do this through high-quality products, specialist expertise, clear advice and a relentless focus on performance.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#5a5f72">We are dedicated to delivering superiority, innovation, quality and customer satisfaction. With a strong presence across Europe and beyond, we are continuously investing to make an even bigger impact.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#5a5f72">HG does what it promises.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#5a5f72"><br>Do you have any questions?</span></strong></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Our colleague Ilse de Groot, Corporate Recruiter, will be happy to answer any questions. You can contact her at </span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ----- ----- style="color:#5a5f72">.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#5a5f72">Would you like to apply for the senior business controller position at HG? You can apply directly by uploading your CV. We aim to respond within 5 working days.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><em><span style="color:#5a5f72">Acquisition in response to this vacancy is not appreciated.</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/hg-international-bv/senior-business-controller-operations-almere-288632","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Senior manager","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Almere, Flevoland, Nederland","created_at":1794443474},{"slug":"remote-product-manager-prince2-netherlands-138530","company_name":"Peoplecert","title":"Product Manager PRINCE2","description":"<p>Are you interested in working with a leading education technology player, the global leader in the assessment and certification of professional skills industry with presence in more than 200 countries worldwide? If so, this is the chance to <strong>apply now!</strong> 📥</p><p><strong>Shape the future of PRINCE2. The home of modern projects, programme, and portfolio management.</strong></p><p><strong>PeopleCert</strong> is looking for a <strong>Product Manager to help take our PRINCE2 portfolio of Best Practice to the next level of success</strong> - developing compelling propositions for globally recognised PRINCE2 products that ensure wide adoption among senior audiences, new sectors and markets. You will be responsible for the day-to-day management of key products in the PRINCE2 portfolio – including certifications, official publications and learning materials – making sure they remain high quality, relevant and well supported in market.</p><p>As <strong>Product Manager for the PRINCE2 portfolio</strong>, you will work closely with teams across the business in order to support delivery of the overall roadmap and enable commercial success for your product set within the PRINCE2 portfolio.</p><h3>As Product Manager PRINCE2 your tasks will be the following:</h3><h3>Product strategy and vision</h3><ul><li>Contribute to the product vision and strategy, and develop and maintain the roadmap for your product set.</li><li>Conduct market research and analysis to identify trends, customer needs, and competitive landscape that will inform the product strategy.</li><li>Track agreed product goals and KPIs, and recommend actions to improve performance.</li></ul><h3>Product management</h3><ul><li>Monitor and analyze product performance, making data-driven recommendations to optimize and enhance your products.</li><li>Prioritise maintenance and improvement activities for your in-market products, to ensure continued relevance and positive customer experience.</li></ul><h3>New product development</h3><ul><li>Work proactively and collaboratively with teams across the business to ensure all aspects of product development, launch and in-market support are considered early in the business case and product design phase</li><li>Support the successful development and launch of new or updated products</li><li>Participate in all aspects of Product design, including: persona development; full end-to-end user journeys; service blueprints; key content and technical specifications</li><li>Design and manage the testing strategy for all products in development, to ensure they are consistently meeting the needs of our target audiences</li></ul><h3>Stakeholder collaboration</h3><ul><li>Contribute key elements to the go-to-market plans developed by Marketing, including positioning, key messaging and more.</li><li>Contribute to pricing proposals for your product set by providing market, competitor and partner insight, and supporting the relevant internal teams in pricing decisions.</li><li>Engage with internal and external stakeholders to secure buy-in and understanding of the product vision.</li></ul><h3>What we look for:</h3><ul><li>Bachelor’s degree in marketing, business, or related field.</li><li>Minimum of 3 years’ experience in a Product Manager or Product Owner role in one of the following sectors: education, training, professional qualifications (e.g. ACA / CIPD etc.)</li><li>Knowledge of PeopleCert best practices and ideally familiar with PRINCE2 or other similar PPM (project, programme and portfolio) certification products.</li><li>Proven track record of managing multiple products and delivering successful outcomes.</li><li>Demonstrable experience of managing products through their whole lifecycle</li><li>Familiarity with all elements of product development, from discovery to delivery</li><li>Proven ability to evaluate product feedback objectively, and propose solutions to address business needs</li><li>Strong business/commercial acumen</li><li>Excellent people and management skills to interact with colleagues, cross-functional teams, and third parties around the world</li><li>Problem-solving and analytical capabilities.</li><li>Prior exposure in Education, Consulting, Examination/Certification, or Technology sectors will be considered an asset.</li><li>Excellent command of the English language (C2 level certification desired; LanguageCert C2 LTE or C2 IESOL a plus).</li><li>Advanced computer literacy required; ECDL Advanced certification desirable. Familiarity with Microsoft Dynamics CRM or equivalent software will be considered an added advantage.</li></ul><h3>What we offer:</h3><ul><li>The opportunity to shape globally recognized frameworks used by professionals around the world.</li><li>A collaborative, high-impact international team and a purpose-driven working culture.</li><li>Flexible working conditions (location and hours).</li><li>Two <strong>free</strong> vouchers for all certifications from PeopleCert's Portfolio per year for all employees</li><li>Competitive compensation and personal development opportunities.</li><li>A global network of professionals and subject matter experts.</li></ul><p><strong>If you want to become a member of our international, dynamic and agile team that creates world leading software products, then we should certainly like to hear from you!</strong></p><h3>About PeopleCert</h3><p><strong>PeopleCert</strong> is a global leader in assessment and certification of professional skills, partnering with multi-national organizations and government bodies for the development &amp; delivery of standardized exams. Delivering exams across 200 countries and in 25 languages over its state-of-the-art assessment technology, PeopleCert enables professionals to boost their careers and realize their life ambitions.</p><p><strong>Quality, Innovation, Passion, Integrity, Clarity, and Velocity are the core values which guide everything we do.</strong></p><p>Our offices in UK, Greece, and Cyprus boast a culture of diversity, where everyone is different, yet everyone fits in. All of us at PeopleCert are committed to the reflection of the diversity and inclusion of our customers and the communities in which we do business.</p><p><strong>Working on Home Office (HO) Secure English Language Tests (SELTs)</strong></p><p>Any person who is engaged by PeopleCert to work on the SELT service must undergo a Background Check (the results of which must be acceptable to PeopleCert and the HO) prior to commencing their SELT duties. All SELT personnel will be required to complete a declaration (provided by PeopleCert) where the existence of any criminal record and/or bankruptcy must be declared.</p><p>If working on the SELT service in the UK, background checks will include:</p><ul><li>A basic or enhanced Disclosure Barring Service (DBS) check</li><li>Right to Work in the UK check (including nationality, identity and place of residence)</li><li>HO security check (Baseline Personnel Security Standard (BPSS) or Counter Terrorist Check (CTC)</li><li>Financial background check</li><li>Employment reference check.</li><li>If working on the SELT service anywhere in the world (outside of the UK) personnel will undergo background checks that are equivalent to those stated for the UK.</li></ul><p>In addition, if personnel are required to speak to SELT candidates they must be appropriately skilled in English language and, where SELT services are provided anywhere in the world (outside of the UK), the official language of the relevant country.<br><br><em>All applications will be treated with strict confidentiality.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/peoplecert/remote-product-manager-prince2-netherlands-138530","tags":["Product Management","Education Management","Growth","Remote"],"job_types":["Full time","mid-senior"],"location":"Netherlands","created_at":1794435608},{"slug":"manager-payments-scheme-economics-amsterdam-395734","company_name":"Airwallex","title":"Manager, Payments/Scheme Economics","description":"<h2><strong>About Airwallex</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Airwallex is the AI-native financial operating system for a real-time, intelligent economy. More than 675,000 businesses, including McLaren Racing, Qantas, SHEIN, and TikTok, use us, directly or through our platform partners, to run their financial operations or build and monetize financial products of their own.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We started in Melbourne in 2015 to build the infrastructure global commerce runs on. We're the regulated backbone behind global payments: not by accident, but by design. A decade plus, 85+ licenses, and a financial infrastructure spanning North America, Europe, the Middle East, and Asia-Pacific.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're co-headquartered in San Francisco and Singapore, with more than 2,700 people across 27 offices. We hire builders with founder-level energy, people who move fast with good judgment, dig in with real curiosity, and make calls from first principles rather than waiting to be told what to do. Read our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.airwallex.com/en-us/operating-principles"> <u>operating principles</u></a> to see it in full.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3>How you'll make impact</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll help Airwallex manage and improve the economics of card payments, with a focus on scheme fees and interchange across Visa and Mastercard. You’ll turn complex network rules and payment data into accurate configurations, actionable analysis and decisions that improve cost visibility and margin performance.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own payment-cost analysis across scheme fees, interchange and network rules, identifying changes and translating them into clear financial, product and operational requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain accurate fee tables, eligibility criteria and transaction-level logic with Product and Engineering, ensuring payment-cost calculations and customer billing reflect current network rules.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build models and reporting across markets, products, payment methods and transaction types to identify margin drivers, anomalies, leakage and opportunities to improve payment economics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support cost and margin optimisation through transaction qualification, BIN routing, cost configuration and related levers, contributing to pricing, product design, market launches and commercial decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strengthen governance, testing, reconciliation and controls by comparing expected costs with actual network charges and helping drive root-cause resolution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Finance, Product, Engineering, Data, Operations and external payment partners to resolve scheme pricing, interchange and rule-related questions.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll work from our Amsterdam office three days a week.</p><h3>What we're looking for</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essentials</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in payments, acquiring, issuing, card networks, payment infrastructure or a related role, ideally within a global PSP, acquirer, scheme, issuer or fintech.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong knowledge of card payment economics, particularly Visa and Mastercard interchange, scheme fees, transaction qualification and network rules.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience translating complex payment rules, fee schedules or network requirements into system logic, configurations and controls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with payment-cost systems or controls, including interchange tables, scheme fee logic, BIN-based rules, transaction attributes or similar payment configurations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical and quantitative capabilities, including experience working with transaction-level data, economic modelling and reconciliation of expected versus actual payment costs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial judgment and the ability to connect payment mechanics to pricing, product decisions and margin optimisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional attention to detail and ownership, with the discipline required to manage complex rules where small errors can create meaningful financial impact at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong cross-functional execution, with the ability to work effectively across Product, Engineering, Finance, Data, Operations and external payment partners.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience partnering directly with Visa, Mastercard or other payment networks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience applying AI or advanced analytics to rule interpretation, anomaly detection or payment-cost optimisation.</p></li></ul><h3>You'll thrive here if</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own the outcome and you don't wait for permission to fix what's broken.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable with ambiguity. Give you a problem, not a prescription, and you'll run with it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have experience at a fintech, payments company, or other highly regulated business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You connect dots across functions and hold the big picture without losing grip on the details.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You say what you mean. You're direct, but you lead with respect.</p></li></ul><h3>Learn more about your team</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Finance &amp; Corporate Development helps Airwallex grow with control. We’re a trusted partner to the business, providing actionable insights on performance, supporting market and product expansion and helping to shape the future of our product. We ensure that Airwallex meets its financial reporting, tax and safeguarding obligations globally. We work with existing and prospective investors to raise capital and ensure it is deployed effectively.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a team for people who want to reimagine how the CFO office works. We’re looking for founder-like energy, high integrity and a passion for technology. You’ll thrive here if you enjoy working cross-functionally, think from first principles and can balance speed of execution with analytical precision.</p><h2><strong>Applicant Safety Policy: Fraud and Third-Party Recruiters</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>To protect you from recruitment scams, please be aware that Airwallex will not ask for bank details, sensitive ID numbers (i.e. passport), or any form of payment during the application or interview process. All official communication will come from an @</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://airwallex.com"><em>airwallex.com</em></a><em> email address. Please apply only through </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://careers.airwallex.com"><em><u>careers.airwallex.com</u></em></a><em> or our official LinkedIn page.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Airwallex does not accept unsolicited resumes from search firms/recruiters.  Airwallex will not pay any fees to search firms/recruiters if a candidate is submitted by a search firm/recruiter unless an agreement has been entered into with respect to specific open position(s).  Search firms/recruiters submitting resumes to Airwallex on an unsolicited basis shall be deemed to accept this condition, regardless of any other provision to the contrary.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Equal opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Airwallex is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We value diversity and anyone seeking employment at Airwallex is considered based on merit, qualifications, competence and talent. We don’t regard color, religion, race, national origin, sexual orientation, ancestry, citizenship, sex, marital or family status, disability, gender, or any other legally protected status when making our hiring decisions. If you have a disability or special need that requires accommodation, please let us know.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/airwallex/manager-payments-scheme-economics-amsterdam-395734","tags":["Finance & Corporate Development"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"NL - Amsterdam","created_at":1794433214},{"slug":"global-trainee-program-outperformer-software-business-track-hilti-319697","company_name":"4Psnl","title":"Global Trainee Program - Outperformer Software Business Track (HILTI)","description":"&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4PS is part of the Hilti Group&lt;/strong&gt;, which gives our people access to international opportunities and development programs within the wider Hilti organization. This vacancy is part of Hilti’s Global Trainee Program. Interested in joining the program? Please submit your application directly via &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.hilti.group/de-ch/stellenangebote/19051-en/global-trainee-program-outperformer-software-business-track-m-f-x/&quot;&gt;Hilti Careerpage&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Construction technology is being reinvented. Be part of it.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Construction is one of the world&#39;s largest industries, and one of its least digitized. That is changing fast. At Hilti, we are not only developing software products - we are building and growing digital businesses around them. Hilti is at the centre of that shift, with a growing portfolio of software products that connect jobsites, offices, teams, and tools across the entire construction lifecycle. We are looking for ambitious, internationally mobile early-career talents with a global mindset who are excited about technology but see their future in business and leadership rather than in a purely technical software career.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Software &amp;amp; Digital Business Track of Hilti&#39;s Outperformer Program is a two-year accelerated development program that prepares you for a commercial, international leadership career in our software and digital businesses. You will learn how technology becomes customer value, how software businesses grow, how products are brought to market, and how commercial decisions are made. This is not a rotation program where you shadow senior leaders. From day one, you carry real responsibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Software Track is designed to build the next generation of software business leaders at Hilti – Business Owners, Business Directors, Segment Managers and ultimately Senior Management Team members. If you want a structured path to running a business, this program is built for that outcome.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The program places you inside one of two business units:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Construction Software: Home to Fieldwire (Field Software for project and workforce management), ON!Track (asset management), and 4PS (construction business management). You will work directly with customers, product teams, and business leadership across Europe and beyond.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fastening &amp;amp; Protection Solutions: Where design &amp;amp; engineering software for structural connections (e.g. PROFIS Engineering Suite), MEP supports and passive fire protection systems are developed and brought to market across a global customer base of structural and mechanical engineers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For the Construction Software business unit, the program is structured to provide a balanced foundation in customer and market exposure, software product understanding, and business experience, while giving you the opportunity to work with at least two software products during the program:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;​Year 1: Begin with a 12-month sales assignment, developing direct customer insight and understanding the business challenges addressed by our software solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;​Year 2: Undertake three rotations of 3–6 months each across product and business teams, including exposure to an international project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;​For the Fastening &amp;amp; Protection Solution business unit, the program provides exposure to product management , software development, exposure to customers and start-ups and international project experience:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;​Year 1: Begin with a 12-month product management assignment, building product understanding and market insight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;​Year 2: Undertake three rotations of 3–6 months each, involving international projects that broaden your business perspective and global exposure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have a dedicated senior mentor from the start, direct exposure to executive leadership, and a peer cohort of Global Trainees across all Hilti business tracks globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are close to graduating or have recently completed a Master&#39;s degree - your degree is likely to be in construction management, civil engineering, or mechanical engineering with a focus on construction, Computer Science, or also Business study programs with an affinity for Software and construction. What matters more than your degree subject is the combination of traits below:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global mobility - you are willing and able to relocate internationally, multiple times. A global thinker who is keen for diverse cultural experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Digital and AI orientation - you think natively in digital workflows, comfortable with software tools, and know the power and potential of AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Language - you are fluent in English and/or German, Dutch, French, Spanish or Italian. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial instinct - you are drawn to how businesses grow, how customers make decisions, and how products create.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low ego, high drive - you take the work seriously and yourself lightly. You seek feedback, move fast, and are energised by ambiguity rather than unsettled by it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are at the start of your career and have maximum three years of junior work experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What’s In It for You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;​​Show us what you can do, and in return, we promise you the experience of a lifetime. We offer you a transformative journey filled with learning, growth, and invaluable experiences that will shape your perspective and personal and professional development. On top of that, you’ll also take part in some fascinating courses and events:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introductory Global Summit: Experience 4 days at our global headquarters in Liechtenstein, featuring the presence of our Executive Board and Global Senior Leadership. The summit offers a comprehensive overview of our business, while fostering soft skill development and meaningful collaboration with fellow program participants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social Project Summit: 7 days dedicated to building a better future, with contribution to a hands-on, high-impact community project. This experience offers the chance to immerse yourself in a different culture while actively improving living conditions for those in need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership Summit: An enriching learning journey in partnership with a renowned business school, featuring online modules and collaborative projects with fellow program participants. The experience concludes with a 5-day on-campus summit to deepen insights and to foster business and leadership skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Hilti&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hilti is a global leader in construction innovation, with more than 34,000 team members across 120 countries. Guided by our purpose, Making Construction Better, we’re driven to keep learning, growing, and finding new ways to make a lasting impact. Here, you’ll be empowered to use your strengths, work with a global and inclusive team, and take on meaningful challenges. At Hilti, you’ll have the chance to make your ideas, achievements, and growth real through purpose, passion, and teamwork.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Learn more about our recruitment process: https://careers.hilti.group/en/candidate-interview-preparation/&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Commitment to Inclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;​​At Hilti, inclusion is a key focus in how we work, lead, and grow together. We are committed to embracing diversity of thought and creating an environment that is inclusive of everyone, everywhere. We continuously strive to ensure every voice is valued and every team member feels empowered to contribute. By building on this foundation, we strengthen our teams, our innovation, and our impact, making construction better together.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;​Exciting software journey: You will dive into the fast-paced world of our construction software business, gaining exposure to innovative digital solutions that are transforming one of the world&#39;s largest industries.&lt;br&gt;​&lt;br&gt;​Global cross-team collaboration: You will work with colleagues worldwide and get guidance from a dedicated mentor as you grow in your career.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;​We hire for a career, not for a position. If you are looking for long-term career prospects and opportunities to grow, this is the perfect start.​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;​Are you ready to jumpstart your career? Our hiring process is designed to help you showcase your skills and experience. The process has multiple steps and requires a longer period of time:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It all starts with your application and a video interview.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get connected with our HR team in an online interview.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get ready to flex your problem-solving muscles with our online Business Case Round.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Impress our Business Line Managers with your presentation skills and insights during the next round.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And, if you make it to the end, you&#39;ll receive an invitation to our Assessment Center.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;​Exciting, right? Let&#39;s get started!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4PS is part of the Hilti Group&lt;/strong&gt;, which gives our people access to international opportunities and development programs within the wider Hilti organization. This vacancy is part of Hilti’s Global Trainee Program. Interested in joining the program? Please submit your application directly via &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.hilti.group/de-ch/stellenangebote/19051-en/global-trainee-program-outperformer-software-business-track-m-f-x/&quot;&gt;Hilti Careerpage&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;​The Assessment Center will take place in Liechtenstein at Hilti Headquarter on December 1st and 2nd, 2026. Applications will be reviewed in the order they’re received, so we encourage you to apply as soon as possible since there are limited spots for the Assessment Center!​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Learn more about our recruitment process:&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.hilti.group/en/candidate-interview-preparation/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Candidate Interview Preparation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;​​For further questions, please feel free to contact Vanessa Furtner ----- and (My LinkedIn).&lt;br&gt;​&lt;br&gt;*For non-EU / EFTA citizens: Please state your eligibility status to work in EU or UK countries and note that if you do not own a valid work permit, Hilti cannot guarantee your final employment due to authority regulations.​&lt;/p&gt;
